{"parentUuid":"4a244f8a-fa67-4667-8a31-8c6600b88a99","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md","content":"# Brain: proposed speed and efficiency fixes\n\n> **Read BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md first.** It corrects several estimates (realistic cold setup is about 65-80 s, not 45-55 s), splits #6, refutes parts of #1/#7/#8, and adds M1: read paths take the exclusive write lock, so brief fails with brain_locked after 10.5 s while any writer holds it. M1 is the new #2 priority.\n\nMeasured 2026-10-24 on entire-brain `main` 318e4b05 (= installed v0.2.0-nightly), with the graph at d4a0c186.\nIsolated store, no daemon. Quiet-machine numbers (load 7-10).\nFull process maps: `PROCESS-MAP.md`. Raw data: `results/`. Profiles: `profiles/`, `results/pprof/`.\n\n**Status: proposals only.** Per the user, no Brain fixes are being made now. Two were prototyped on scratch branches\n(`eb-exp1`, `eb-exp2`) to measure them, and nothing was committed.\n\n## Where the time goes today\n\n| Process | Time | Dominant step |\n|---|---|---|\n| setup, `cli` (5,621 checkpoints) | **never finishes**, projected 3.9-5.6 h | 5,621 sequential `entire checkpoint explain <id>` calls, 2.5-3.6 s each (99.99% subprocess wait) |\n| setup, entire-graph, cold | 105 s, 1.45 GB RSS | history index 52.4 s (50%), pattern layer 31.6 s (30%), semantic 10.3 s, entity index 7.4 s |\n| setup re-run, nothing changed | 17.3 s | entity index 10.6 s (re-runs 10 `graph diff` every time) |\n| setup re-run after one `remember` | 37 s | pattern corpus rebuilt, 21.5 s |\n| first `brief` after setup | 6.4 s, 609 MB | lazy history search-index build, 5.37 s (sqlite write) |\n| warm `brief` | 610 ms | status 383 ms, graph context 127 ms, history rank 67 ms |\n| first `brain_brief` over MCP | 3.9 s | waits about 3.5 s on a background worker's write lock |\n| `doctor` | 1.94 s, 788 MB RSS | decodes all 158k history records |\n| `status` | 445 ms | |\n| `distill --dry-run` | 6.7 s | CPU over 1.27 GB of transcripts |\n| recall / query / search | 72-128 ms | fine |\n| MCP tool list | 31.8 KB (~8k tokens) per agent session | 32 tool schemas |\n\n## Proposed fixes, ranked by user-visible saving\n\n| # | Fix | Where | Saving | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Stop the per-checkpoint host-CLI call during export.** The list call (5.8 s) already returns session ids, agent and date for all checkpoints. Use those fields, or a batch call, an immutable per-checkpoint cache, bounded parallelism, or the local fast path for local checkpoints. | session export (repos with a separate checkpoint remote, e.g. cli) | **hours: from \"never finishes\" to finishing.** About 4-5.6 h becomes seconds to minutes. | timing log: 336 calls in 1,198 s; 2.5-3.6 s each |\n| 2 | **`historyTerms` normalizes the whole text once per keyword**, up to 26x. Normalize once, then match. | history index | **history 52.4 s → 31.5 s (−40%), setup −17.7 s.** Measured, with identical output (157,977 records, same sha256). | CPU profile: `historyTerms` 18.2 s, of which `normalizeHistorySearchText` 16.3 s |\n| 3 | **Typed JSON decode** instead of untyped maps, and stream the records instead of holding them all in memory. | history index | estimated −10 s CPU and a much smaller heap than the 1.45 GB peak | profile: `json.Unmarshal` 14.2 s; `runtime.madvise` 11.4 s; GC 8.5 s |\n| 4 | **Parse each transcript once** for history, episodes and corpus. Today it is parsed three times. Write the staging DB with sqlite fast-write pragmas and one transaction. | pattern layer + history | **estimated 15-25 s** off a cold setup | profile: second and third parse 11 s + 6.2 s CPU; about 13 s off-CPU in sqlite, one transaction per session |\n| 5 | **Build the history search index during setup**, not lazily on the first brief. | brief | **first brief 6.4 s → about 0.6 s** | profile: `openHistoryFTS` 6.49 s |\n| 6 | **SPLIT (corrected by the review):** brain PR #474 fixes the LEGACY-store variant (export aborted on a divergent cached transcript in a non-checkpoint-backed brain). The loop this study reproduced is a DIFFERENT bug and survives #474 (reviewer built ef41d238; the same 3 jobs still go stale): a **session-ref collision**. conversationSessionRef = sha(repo, branch, sid); an empty branch maps to \"main\" in both jobs and receipts, so a session with an unknown/ copy and a main/ copy shares one ref with two digests. The receipt keeps the first copy, the job keeps the last, and they never match (conversation_session.go:40-52, memory_cmd.go:591-594/656-668, memory_receipts.go:180-187). Fix: make jobs and receipts pick the same copy (fact e60bf39e: do not reject duplicate ids). memory_cmd.go:1162 is correct. The first-MCP-brief lock wait (about 3.9 s) is separate and also survives #474. | memory worker, MCP | first MCP brief 3.9 s → about 0.5 s (lock part); 3/229 sessions never project | review: BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md |\n| 7 | **Run the 10 `graph diff` calls in parallel or as one batch**, and skip commits already indexed. | entity index | **6-8 s off every warm setup and watch tick** | 10 sequential calls, 7.4-10.6 s |\n| 8 | **Cache the git filter probe and the `graph store` result per process.** brief calls `graph store` twice. | brief, status, small-repo setup | **brief −26% (610 → 449 ms), status −48% (445 → 234 ms).** Measured, identical output. Probe is 19% of small-repo setup. | prototype `eb-exp2` |\n| 9 | **Run the status probes in parallel with graph context** in brief. | brief | estimated 100-250 ms | estimate only |\n| 10 | **doctor reads health metadata** instead of decoding the full index. | doctor | **about −1.5 s and −750 MB** | profile: `loadBrainHistoryIndex` 1.10 s, `decodeBrainHistoryIndex` 0.91 s |\n| 11 | **Pattern corpus: update incrementally** after a `remember`, instead of rebuilding it. | setup re-run | about −20 s on the next re-run (37 s → 17 s) | re-run after remember: corpus rebuilt 21.5 s |\n| 12 | **Trim the MCP tool list** (descriptions, rarely used tools behind one dispatcher). | every agent session | about 8k tokens of context per session | tools/list = 31.8 KB |\n| 13 | **Host dispatch overhead** of about 30-50 ms per `entire graph` call (Brain → host CLI → graph). Call the graph binary directly when it is known. | brief, setup | about 30-50 ms per graph call | shim timings |\n\n## Bugs found while measuring (not speed, but user-visible)\n\n- **cli semantic index fails**: the graph refuses `index --head` on a partial-clone repo, and the real `devenv/cli` has the same configuration.\n- **No-egress session export fails** on the partial clone (missing blobs).\n- **Every new commit silently drops code context from brief** (\"search store not built for this commit\") until the graph store is rebuilt.\n- **The memory-worker retry loop** above (#6) runs forever-ish in the background.\n\n## If these were all done (rough, cold setup on entire-graph)\n\n105 s → roughly 45-55 s: −17.7 s from #2, −10 s from #3, −15-25 s from #4, plus #7 on re-runs. The first brief would be about\n0.6 s instead of 6.4 s, the first MCP brief about 0.5 s instead of 3.9 s, and cli setup would finish at all.\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}},"displayPath":"../../devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"37d23a2e-5050-4cab-8860-2ccfd7a082fb","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:05:39.760Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Brain: proposed speed and efficiency fixes\n2\t\n3\t> **Read BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md first.** It corrects several estimates (realistic cold setup is about 65-80 s, not 45-55 s), splits #6, refutes parts of #1/#7/#8, and adds M1: read paths take the exclusive write lock, so brief fails with brain_locked after 10.5 s while any writer holds it. M1 is the new #2 priority.\n4\t\n5\tMeasured 2026-10-24 on entire-brain `main` 318e4b05 (= installed v0.2.0-nightly), with the graph at d4a0c186.\n6\tIsolated store, no daemon. Quiet-machine numbers (load 7-10).\n7\tFull process maps: `PROCESS-MAP.md`. Raw data: `results/`. Profiles: `profiles/`, `results/pprof/`.\n8\t\n9\t**Status: proposals only.** Per the user, no Brain fixes are being made now. Two were prototyped on scratch branches\n10\t(`eb-exp1`, `eb-exp2`) to measure them, and nothing was committed.\n11\t\n12\t## Where the time goes today\n13\t\n14\t| Process | Time | Dominant step |\n15\t|---|---|---|\n16\t| setup, `cli` (5,621 checkpoints) | **never finishes**, projected 3.9-5.6 h | 5,621 sequential `entire checkpoint explain <id>` calls, 2.5-3.6 s each (99.99% subprocess wait) |\n17\t| setup, entire-graph, cold | 105 s, 1.45 GB RSS | history index 52.4 s (50%), pattern layer 31.6 s (30%), semantic 10.3 s, entity index 7.4 s |\n18\t| setup re-run, nothing changed | 17.3 s | entity index 10.6 s (re-runs 10 `graph diff` every time) |\n19\t| setup re-run after one `remember` | 37 s | pattern corpus rebuilt, 21.5 s |\n20\t| first `brief` after setup | 6.4 s, 609 MB | lazy history search-index build, 5.37 s (sqlite write) |\n21\t| warm `brief` | 610 ms | status 383 ms, graph context 127 ms, history rank 67 ms |\n22\t| first `brain_brief` over MCP | 3.9 s | waits about 3.5 s on a background worker's write lock |\n23\t| `doctor` | 1.94 s, 788 MB RSS | decodes all 158k history records |\n24\t| `status` | 445 ms | |\n25\t| `distill --dry-run` | 6.7 s | CPU over 1.27 GB of transcripts |\n26\t| recall / query / search | 72-128 ms | fine |\n27\t| MCP tool list | 31.8 KB (~8k tokens) per agent session | 32 tool schemas |\n28\t\n29\t## Proposed fixes, ranked by user-visible saving\n30\t\n31\t| # | Fix | Where | Saving | Evidence |\n32\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n33\t| 1 | **Stop the per-checkpoint host-CLI call during export.** The list call (5.8 s) already returns session ids, agent and date for all checkpoints. Use those fields, or a batch call, an immutable per-checkpoint cache, bounded parallelism, or the local fast path for local checkpoints. | session export (repos with a separate checkpoint remote, e.g. cli) | **hours: from \"never finishes\" to finishing.** About 4-5.6 h becomes seconds to minutes. | timing log: 336 calls in 1,198 s; 2.5-3.6 s each |\n34\t| 2 | **`historyTerms` normalizes the whole text once per keyword**, up to 26x. Normalize once, then match. | history index | **history 52.4 s → 31.5 s (−40%), setup −17.7 s.** Measured, with identical output (157,977 records, same sha256). | CPU profile: `historyTerms` 18.2 s, of which `normalizeHistorySearchText` 16.3 s |\n35\t| 3 | **Typed JSON decode** instead of untyped maps, and stream the records instead of holding them all in memory. | history index | estimated −10 s CPU and a much smaller heap than the 1.45 GB peak | profile: `json.Unmarshal` 14.2 s; `runtime.madvise` 11.4 s; GC 8.5 s |\n36\t| 4 | **Parse each transcript once** for history, episodes and corpus. Today it is parsed three times. Write the staging DB with sqlite fast-write pragmas and one transaction. | pattern layer + history | **estimated 15-25 s** off a cold setup | profile: second and third parse 11 s + 6.2 s CPU; about 13 s off-CPU in sqlite, one transaction per session |\n37\t| 5 | **Build the history search index during setup**, not lazily on the first brief. | brief | **first brief 6.4 s → about 0.6 s** | profile: `openHistoryFTS` 6.49 s |\n38\t| 6 | **SPLIT (corrected by the review):** brain PR #474 fixes the LEGACY-store variant (export aborted on a divergent cached transcript in a non-checkpoint-backed brain). The loop this study reproduced is a DIFFERENT bug and survives #474 (reviewer built ef41d238; the same 3 jobs still go stale): a **session-ref collision**. conversationSessionRef = sha(repo, branch, sid); an empty branch maps to \"main\" in both jobs and receipts, so a session with an unknown/ copy and a main/ copy shares one ref with two digests. The receipt keeps the first copy, the job keeps the last, and they never match (conversation_session.go:40-52, memory_cmd.go:591-594/656-668, memory_receipts.go:180-187). Fix: make jobs and receipts pick the same copy (fact e60bf39e: do not reject duplicate ids). memory_cmd.go:1162 is correct. The first-MCP-brief lock wait (about 3.9 s) is separate and also survives #474. | memory worker, MCP | first MCP brief 3.9 s → about 0.5 s (lock part); 3/229 sessions never project | review: BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md |\n39\t| 7 | **Run the 10 `graph diff` calls in parallel or as one batch**, and skip commits already indexed. | entity index | **6-8 s off every warm setup and watch tick** | 10 sequential calls, 7.4-10.6 s |\n40\t| 8 | **Cache the git filter probe and the `graph store` result per process.** brief calls `graph store` twice. | brief, status, small-repo setup | **brief −26% (610 → 449 ms), status −48% (445 → 234 ms).** Measured, identical output. Probe is 19% of small-repo setup. | prototype `eb-exp2` |\n41\t| 9 | **Run the status probes in parallel with graph context** in brief. | brief | estimated 100-250 ms | estimate only |\n42\t| 10 | **doctor reads health metadata** instead of decoding the full index. | doctor | **about −1.5 s and −750 MB** | profile: `loadBrainHistoryIndex` 1.10 s, `decodeBrainHistoryIndex` 0.91 s |\n43\t| 11 | **Pattern corpus: update incrementally** after a `remember`, instead of rebuilding it. | setup re-run | about −20 s on the next re-run (37 s → 17 s) | re-run after remember: corpus rebuilt 21.5 s |\n44\t| 12 | **Trim the MCP tool list** (descriptions, rarely used tools behind one dispatcher). | every agent session | about 8k tokens of context per session | tools/list = 31.8 KB |\n45\t| 13 | **Host dispatch overhead** of about 30-50 ms per `entire graph` call (Brain → host CLI → graph). Call the graph binary directly when it is known. | brief, setup | about 30-50 ms per graph call | shim timings |\n46\t\n47\t## Bugs found while measuring (not speed, but user-visible)\n48\t\n49\t- **cli semantic index fails**: the graph refuses `index --head` on a partial-clone repo, and the real `devenv/cli` has the same configuration.\n50\t- **No-egress session export fails** on the partial clone (missing blobs).\n51\t- **Every new commit silently drops code context from brief** (\"search store not built for this commit\") until the graph store is rebuilt.\n52\t- **The memory-worker retry loop** above (#6) runs forever-ish in the background.\n53\t\n54\t## If these were all done (rough, cold setup on entire-graph)\n55\t\n56\t105 s → roughly 45-55 s: −17.7 s from #2, −10 s from #3, −15-25 s from #4, plus #7 on re-runs. The first brief would be about\n57\t0.6 s instead of 6.4 s, the first MCP brief about 0.5 s instead of 3.9 s, and cli setup would finish at all.\n58\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"37d23a2e-5050-4cab-8860-2ccfd7a082fb","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md","content":"# Semantic-layer plan: graph + brain\n\nThe one shared sequence for both sessions:\n- **graph**: the session `merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption`\n- **brain**: the session `fix-brain-initialization-ux`\n\nEdit your own lane's lines only, and announce changes by SendMessage. The todo board\n(`.claude/todo-board.json`) tracks the rows. This file is the order and the handoffs.\n\nRules that hold throughout:\n- nothing merges until all of this is finished; there is one merge handoff to Suhaan at the end\n- no approval asks\n- board writes go under the flock\n- ask before touching the other's repo or any shared state\n\n## Phase A: finish measuring (now)\n| # | Who | What | Done when | Hands off |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| A1 | graph | Graph timing study P1 finishes (latest main d4a0c186) | `devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md` exists | graph pings brain: **heavy I/O may start** |\n| A2 | graph | Adversarial review of the Brain speed list | `devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` exists | graph pings brain: **start Brain fixes (C2)** |\n\nUntil A1 ends, neither session runs heavy disk or CPU work (full suites, re-index, large deletes). The timing is\nbeing measured.\n\n## Phase B: refresh, after A1. One heavy job at a time, in this order.\n| # | Who | What | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | graph | Run the held deletions: 123 stale or dirty clones (79.9 GB, `devenv-worktrees/cleanup-audit/delete-check.txt`, minus `Documents/Coding/entire-judge`), Ollama models, old Rust toolchains, **plus the stray Brain stores**: `gh/entireio/entire-sem` (the old name of entire-graph) and about 25 hackathon/demo repos | Keep the 4 that matter: entire-brain, entire-graph, entiredb, cli (about 17.5 GB). Facts stay backed up. Ping brain when done. |\n| B2 | brain | Re-index Brain on **3 repos, in order: entire-graph (canary) → entire-brain → entiredb** | **cli moves to Phase C** as the acceptance test. It needs both Brain fix #1 (export/explain, about 4-5.6 h today) and graph G-partial (graph refuses `index --head` on the partial clone). |\n| B3 | graph | **graph runs `entire graph setup` ONCE per repo, with both products active, never concurrently**, then prewarms `index --head` on the same 3 repos | One setup writes the combined guide for graph+brain (`renderActivation`, activation.go:26). Two interleaved setups can leave a duplicate activation marker, which `parseActivation` (activation.go:42) refuses until it is hand-repaired. brain does not call `entire brain setup` on shared repos. Setup rewrites tracked CLAUDE.md blocks in main checkouts; nothing is committed. |\n| B4 | graph | Delete the dev-mods `todo-live` copy before the next restart | The permanent `todo-board` mod carries the band. |\n\nThe real Brain store (`~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos`, about 37 GB, facts backed up 141/141) is\ndeleted **only after** brain lands the export/explain speedup (Brain fix #1) and a rebuild on one repo is proven to\ntake minutes. brain owns that call.\n\n## Phase C: fix loops, in parallel lanes\n| # | Who | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | graph | G1: graph fix list with estimated savings, from P1. G2: adversarial review. G3: work through it, one PR per fix, each with a before/after timing and mutation-proven tests. |\n| C2 | brain | Work through `BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md` as corrected by the review. #6 is already resolved by #474. **cli re-index is the acceptance test** for fix #1, once G-partial lands too. |\n| C3 | graph | Graph items that block Brain: **G-partial** (graph refuses `index --head` on partial clones, so Brain's cli semantic index fails), per-commit graph store rebuild (brief drops code context after each commit), host dispatch overhead of about 30-50 ms per call |\n| C4 | graph | #142 rescope: drop `--max-seconds` and the partial path; keep cancellation, `refuseTruncatedSnapshot` in all 3 writers plus its test, the filterActive guard, and the TestTF142R6 allowlist entry |\n| C5 | graph | Tune the graph arm of the adoption counter (brain-memory mod, built by brain) against `devenv-worktrees/fresh-env` (repo outside $HOME) |\n\n**Measuring windows (agreed; applies to both sessions, brain first).** A fix's before/after timing needs a quiet machine. Before measuring, post a board row\n`measuring: <what>, until <time>` in your lane and message the other session. The other session holds heavy work\nuntil it clears.\n\n## Phase D: close out\n| # | Who | What |\n|---|---|---|\n| D1 | graph | Fill the Graph tab of https://claude.ai/artifact/1YbGGd5Gk19omne4PyU7h1 and update the Brain tab with the fixes that landed |\n| D2 | both | Fresh-env usage check on the final builds (graph + brain), re-baselined after #474 |\n| D3 | graph | Close graph PRs superseded by what landed (git ancestry checked first) |\n| D4 | both | **One merge handoff to Suhaan**: every open PR in both lanes, in dependency order, CI and findings state for each |\n| D5 | Suhaan | `/compact` (graph says when) |\n","numLines":58,"startLine":1,"totalLines":58}},"displayPath":"../.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"fe3dbddf-2b5b-4491-9ead-de721dfe3f12","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:05:39.760Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Semantic-layer plan: graph + brain\n2\t\n3\tThe one shared sequence for both sessions:\n4\t- **graph**: the session `merge-graph-fixes-and-improve-agent-adoption`\n5\t- **brain**: the session `fix-brain-initialization-ux`\n6\t\n7\tEdit your own lane's lines only, and announce changes by SendMessage. The todo board\n8\t(`.claude/todo-board.json`) tracks the rows. This file is the order and the handoffs.\n9\t\n10\tRules that hold throughout:\n11\t- nothing merges until all of this is finished; there is one merge handoff to Suhaan at the end\n12\t- no approval asks\n13\t- board writes go under the flock\n14\t- ask before touching the other's repo or any shared state\n15\t\n16\t## Phase A: finish measuring (now)\n17\t| # | Who | What | Done when | Hands off |\n18\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n19\t| A1 | graph | Graph timing study P1 finishes (latest main d4a0c186) | `devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md` exists | graph pings brain: **heavy I/O may start** |\n20\t| A2 | graph | Adversarial review of the Brain speed list | `devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` exists | graph pings brain: **start Brain fixes (C2)** |\n21\t\n22\tUntil A1 ends, neither session runs heavy disk or CPU work (full suites, re-index, large deletes). The timing is\n23\tbeing measured.\n24\t\n25\t## Phase B: refresh, after A1. One heavy job at a time, in this order.\n26\t| # | Who | What | Notes |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| B1 | graph | Run the held deletions: 123 stale or dirty clones (79.9 GB, `devenv-worktrees/cleanup-audit/delete-check.txt`, minus `Documents/Coding/entire-judge`), Ollama models, old Rust toolchains, **plus the stray Brain stores**: `gh/entireio/entire-sem` (the old name of entire-graph) and about 25 hackathon/demo repos | Keep the 4 that matter: entire-brain, entire-graph, entiredb, cli (about 17.5 GB). Facts stay backed up. Ping brain when done. |\n29\t| B2 | brain | Re-index Brain on **3 repos, in order: entire-graph (canary) → entire-brain → entiredb** | **cli moves to Phase C** as the acceptance test. It needs both Brain fix #1 (export/explain, about 4-5.6 h today) and graph G-partial (graph refuses `index --head` on the partial clone). |\n30\t| B3 | graph | **graph runs `entire graph setup` ONCE per repo, with both products active, never concurrently**, then prewarms `index --head` on the same 3 repos | One setup writes the combined guide for graph+brain (`renderActivation`, activation.go:26). Two interleaved setups can leave a duplicate activation marker, which `parseActivation` (activation.go:42) refuses until it is hand-repaired. brain does not call `entire brain setup` on shared repos. Setup rewrites tracked CLAUDE.md blocks in main checkouts; nothing is committed. |\n31\t| B4 | graph | Delete the dev-mods `todo-live` copy before the next restart | The permanent `todo-board` mod carries the band. |\n32\t\n33\tThe real Brain store (`~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos`, about 37 GB, facts backed up 141/141) is\n34\tdeleted **only after** brain lands the export/explain speedup (Brain fix #1) and a rebuild on one repo is proven to\n35\ttake minutes. brain owns that call.\n36\t\n37\t## Phase C: fix loops, in parallel lanes\n38\t| # | Who | What |\n39\t|---|---|---|\n40\t| C1 | graph | G1: graph fix list with estimated savings, from P1. G2: adversarial review. G3: work through it, one PR per fix, each with a before/after timing and mutation-proven tests. |\n41\t| C2 | brain | Work through `BRAIN-SPEEDUPS.md` as corrected by the review. #6 is already resolved by #474. **cli re-index is the acceptance test** for fix #1, once G-partial lands too. |\n42\t| C3 | graph | Graph items that block Brain: **G-partial** (graph refuses `index --head` on partial clones, so Brain's cli semantic index fails), per-commit graph store rebuild (brief drops code context after each commit), host dispatch overhead of about 30-50 ms per call |\n43\t| C4 | graph | #142 rescope: drop `--max-seconds` and the partial path; keep cancellation, `refuseTruncatedSnapshot` in all 3 writers plus its test, the filterActive guard, and the TestTF142R6 allowlist entry |\n44\t| C5 | graph | Tune the graph arm of the adoption counter (brain-memory mod, built by brain) against `devenv-worktrees/fresh-env` (repo outside $HOME) |\n45\t\n46\t**Measuring windows (agreed; applies to both sessions, brain first).** A fix's before/after timing needs a quiet machine. Before measuring, post a board row\n47\t`measuring: <what>, until <time>` in your lane and message the other session. The other session holds heavy work\n48\tuntil it clears.\n49\t\n50\t## Phase D: close out\n51\t| # | Who | What |\n52\t|---|---|---|\n53\t| D1 | graph | Fill the Graph tab of https://claude.ai/artifact/1YbGGd5Gk19omne4PyU7h1 and update the Brain tab with the fixes that landed |\n54\t| D2 | both | Fresh-env usage check on the final builds (graph + brain), re-baselined after #474 |\n55\t| D3 | graph | Close graph PRs superseded by what landed (git ancestry checked first) |\n56\t| D4 | both | **One merge handoff to Suhaan**: every open PR in both lanes, in dependency order, CI and findings state for each |\n57\t| D5 | Suhaan | `/compact` (graph says when) |\n58\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
