,"version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"9dcb52ef-a758-4e7e-a09c-36752b5a16d0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9248d1c4-b40a-485b-bea6-15e6c3184d7e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01N7KcL42VM2Luu6FnL5xasg","type":"tool_result","content":"## Missed items\n\n| id | finding | evidence | impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **M1** | **Read paths take the exclusive brain write lock.** A CLI `brief` or MCP `brain_brief` **fails with `brain_locked` after 10.5 s** whenever a writer holds `write.lock`. Writers hold it for long spans: the whole pattern build (`pattern_corpus.go:477`, 21.5-31.6 s), history writes (setup pprof `withBrainWriteLock` 18.7 s CPU), and worker passes (8-17 s). The first-MCP-brief wait in #6 is a symptom of this. | **Measured** on a clone, holding flock for 15 s: CLI brief rc=1 at 10,544 ms; MCP JSON-RPC error -32000 `brain_locked` at 10,578 ms. Without the lock it took 536 ms. Code: `mcp.go:521`, `retrieval_transport.go:147`, `brain.go:33`. Already observed in `fact:c71a4457` (\"reads fail brain_locked during long refreshes\"), still open on 318e4b05. | Agents' tool calls error out during setup, during a refresh after `remember`, and during worker passes. **Highest-impact item for agents.** |\n| **M2** | **FTS full rebuild after every history change.** This is a wider version of #5. | `history_fts.go:95-111`, `:252-283`, `:824`; `history_delta.go:510`. Source-derived and **not measured**. | About 5-6 s and about 600 MB on the agent's first query after each new session is indexed, plus write-lock hold, which leads to M1. |\n| **M3** | **The FTS and corpus builds are page-cache bound.** | Brief-cold pprof: `Pwrite` 5.82 of 7.46 s CPU through `_getPageNormal`. Setup: `_pagerStress` 3.70 s plus Pread 2.08 s; commit 0.28 s. | `PRAGMA cache_size` and bulk-load settings are likely the cheapest large win for #4, #5 and M2. Not measured. |\n| **M4** | **An idle memory-worker pass costs about 8.5 s and holds the lock**, then relaunches itself with a delay of about 28 m to 2 h. | Measured: 8.51 s wall with 0/0/0 jobs. Worker pprof: `sessionTranscriptDigest` 1.30 s, cat-file 3.19 s. In the study, worker.log shows 11 passes in 7 min. | Cache transcript digests by blob OID. Skip the startup nudge when nothing is pending. |\n| **M5** | **#1's default config fails after hours anyway** on a partial clone. | See #1 and B2. | Pair fix #1 with partial-clone handling (fetch, or a named remedy), or the outcome is a fast failure instead of a slow one. |\n| **M6** | **madvise (11.4 s) and GC (8.5 s) are unattributed.** madvise is unchanged by exp1. | prof2 vs exp1 pprof. | Try GOGC/GOMEMLIMIT or bounding the peak heap before assuming typed decode fixes it. Untested. |\n| **M7** | **A duplicate `historyTerms` \"tool\" definition** appears in graph impact (`history.go:2442`, `kind=tool`). | `entire graph impact --symbol historyTerms`. | Graph product noise (likely a HANDLES_TOOL heuristic). Not a Brain speed issue. |\n\n## Corrected ranking (user-visible impact × frequency × certainty)\n\n1. **#1, together with M5.** Today the default config spends hours and fails anyway. Use the local snapshot for metadata, and fail fast on partial clones.\n2. **M1 (with the #6 lock part).** Agents' brief and MCP calls fail with `brain_locked` during long writes, and the first MCP call pays about 3.4 s. Use a shared lock or a snapshot read for retrieval, and keep writer critical sections short.\n3. **M2 + #5 + M3.** Build the FTS in the writer that changed history (or incrementally), with a large `cache_size`. Do not move it into setup's critical path.\n4. **#2.** Measured −20.9 s on history, zero semantic risk, trivial.\n5. **#11.** −18.7 s and a 21 s lock hold on every refresh after any fact change.\n6. **#6 / B4, the real root cause (ref collision).** A correctness issue: 3 of 229 sessions never project, and stale passes repeat.\n7. **#4 + #3 together.** Parse once, typed decode and the sqlite cache: about −8-15 s cold.\n8. **#7.** Detach or parallelize the entity backfill: −5-10 s per warm setup or tick.\n9. **#8.** Per-request `graph store` memo only (−90 ms brief, −167 ms status). Drop the filter memo.\n10. **#10** doctor: −1.0-1.3 s.\n11. **#9:** ≤ 130 ms.\n12. **#13:** about 25 ms per graph call.\n13. **#12:** client-dependent tokens.\n\n**Bottom line correction.** The claim \"105 s → roughly 45-55 s if all done\" is optimistic. It double-counts #3 and #4, and it ignores the +5 s from #5 if the FTS build is moved into setup. The fixed floor is semantic 10 s + entity 7 s + memory coordinator 1.8 s + export/seed 1.1 s. A realistic cold eg setup is about **65-80 s**; only #2 is measured (87.5 s).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cacde713-aed2-4974-a44d-152538700130","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:06:31.749Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Missed items\n\n| id | finding | evidence | impact |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **M1** | **Read paths take the exclusive brain write lock.** A CLI `brief` or MCP `brain_brief` **fails with `brain_locked` after 10.5 s** whenever a writer holds `write.lock`. Writers hold it for long spans: the whole pattern build (`pattern_corpus.go:477`, 21.5-31.6 s), history writes (setup pprof `withBrainWriteLock` 18.7 s CPU), and worker passes (8-17 s). The first-MCP-brief wait in #6 is a symptom of this. | **Measured** on a clone, holding flock for 15 s: CLI brief rc=1 at 10,544 ms; MCP JSON-RPC error -32000 `brain_locked` at 10,578 ms. Without the lock it took 536 ms. Code: `mcp.go:521`, `retrieval_transport.go:147`, `brain.go:33`. Already observed in `fact:c71a4457` (\"reads fail brain_locked during long refreshes\"), still open on 318e4b05. | Agents' tool calls error out during setup, during a refresh after `remember`, and during worker passes. **Highest-impact item for agents.** |\n| **M2** | **FTS full rebuild after every history change.** This is a wider version of #5. | `history_fts.go:95-111`, `:252-283`, `:824`; `history_delta.go:510`. Source-derived and **not measured**. | About 5-6 s and about 600 MB on the agent's first query after each new session is indexed, plus write-lock hold, which leads to M1. |\n| **M3** | **The FTS and corpus builds are page-cache bound.** | Brief-cold pprof: `Pwrite` 5.82 of 7.46 s CPU through `_getPageNormal`. Setup: `_pagerStress` 3.70 s plus Pread 2.08 s; commit 0.28 s. | `PRAGMA cache_size` and bulk-load settings are likely the cheapest large win for #4, #5 and M2. Not measured. |\n| **M4** | **An idle memory-worker pass costs about 8.5 s and holds the lock**, then relaunches itself with a delay of about 28 m to 2 h. | Measured: 8.51 s wall with 0/0/0 jobs. Worker pprof: `sessionTranscriptDigest` 1.30 s, cat-file 3.19 s. In the study, worker.log shows 11 passes in 7 min. | Cache transcript digests by blob OID. Skip the startup nudge when nothing is pending. |\n| **M5** | **#1's default config fails after hours anyway** on a partial clone. | See #1 and B2. | Pair fix #1 with partial-clone handling (fetch, or a named remedy), or the outcome is a fast failure instead of a slow one. |\n| **M6** | **madvise (11.4 s) and GC (8.5 s) are unattributed.** madvise is unchanged by exp1. | prof2 vs exp1 pprof. | Try GOGC/GOMEMLIMIT or bounding the peak heap before assuming typed decode fixes it. Untested. |\n| **M7** | **A duplicate `historyTerms` \"tool\" definition** appears in graph impact (`history.go:2442`, `kind=tool`). | `entire graph impact --symbol historyTerms`. | Graph product noise (likely a HANDLES_TOOL heuristic). Not a Brain speed issue. |\n\n## Corrected ranking (user-visible impact × frequency × certainty)\n\n1. **#1, together with M5.** Today the default config spends hours and fails anyway. Use the local snapshot for metadata, and fail fast on partial clones.\n2. **M1 (with the #6 lock part).** Agents' brief and MCP calls fail with `brain_locked` during long writes, and the first MCP call pays about 3.4 s. Use a shared lock or a snapshot read for retrieval, and keep writer critical sections short.\n3. **M2 + #5 + M3.** Build the FTS in the writer that changed history (or incrementally), with a large `cache_size`. Do not move it into setup's critical path.\n4. **#2.** Measured −20.9 s on history, zero semantic risk, trivial.\n5. **#11.** −18.7 s and a 21 s lock hold on every refresh after any fact change.\n6. **#6 / B4, the real root cause (ref collision).** A correctness issue: 3 of 229 sessions never project, and stale passes repeat.\n7. **#4 + #3 together.** Parse once, typed decode and the sqlite cache: about −8-15 s cold.\n8. **#7.** Detach or parallelize the entity backfill: −5-10 s per warm setup or tick.\n9. **#8.** Per-request `graph store` memo only (−90 ms brief, −167 ms status). Drop the filter memo.\n10. **#10** doctor: −1.0-1.3 s.\n11. **#9:** ≤ 130 ms.\n12. **#13:** about 25 ms per graph call.\n13. **#12:** client-dependent tokens.\n\n**Bottom line correction.** The claim \"105 s → roughly 45-55 s if all done\" is optimistic. It double-counts #3 and #4, and it ignores the +5 s from #5 if the FTS build is moved into setup. The fixed floor is semantic 10 s + entity 7 s + memory coordinator 1.8 s + export/seed 1.1 s. A realistic cold eg setup is about **65-80 s**; only #2 is measured (87.5 s).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"70d1573a-6b71-48ce-a046-c4d4cf7d9a75","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":282},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visi