{"parentUuid":"e89b01a5-b39a-4181-b829-13871993392d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMWLmXyrcz85BMvfqGi5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2063,"cache_read_input_tokens":126079,"output_tokens":2650,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":308},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2063,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2650,"cache_read_input_tokens":126079,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2063},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3531,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"ce246751-69d6-4317-92eb-b747f0fe7b56","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMWLmCPx998BF9iT8HH3","requestRef":"72fde0e6-2ca4-4a72-bdd9-337f24f39038","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e0bf1e3-173e-490f-9b0f-4abd3506b9bf","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:06:36.909Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"8e0bf1e3-173e-490f-9b0f-4abd3506b9bf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMWLmXyrcz85BMvfqGi5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S9RKR6cXTC3yTurTMJ4BxT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('''<div class=\"callout\"><b>Setup on the cli repo never finishes.</b> Export makes one <span class=\"mono\">entire checkpoint explain</span> call per checkpoint, 5,621 of them, one after another, at 2.5–3.6 s each: about 4–5.6 hours. The list call it already makes returns most of that data in 5.8 s.</div>''',\n'''<div class=\"callout\"><b>Setup on the cli repo never finishes.</b> Export makes one <span class=\"mono\">entire checkpoint explain</span> call per checkpoint, 5,621 of them, one after another, at 2.5–3.6 s each: about 4–5.6 hours, and then it fails on the partial clone anyway. The local refs already hold all 5,621 checkpoints, so those calls are pure overhead.</div>\n    <div class=\"callout\"><b>Agents' brief calls fail while Brain writes.</b> Read paths take the exclusive write lock, so <span class=\"mono\">brief</span> and MCP <span class=\"mono\">brain_brief</span> give up with <span class=\"mono\">brain_locked</span> after 10.5 s whenever a writer holds it. Writers hold it for 8–32 s, during setup, refresh after <span class=\"mono\">remember</span>, and background memory passes. Found by the review.</div>''')\nrep('note: \"Waits on a background worker that holds the write lock; uses only 320 ms of CPU.\"',\n    'note: \"Waits on a background worker that holds the write lock (reads take the exclusive lock); uses only 320 ms of CPU. With a longer write in progress it fails at 10.5 s instead.\"')\nrep('''<p class=\"note\">Proposals only: no Brain fixes are being made right now. Two were prototyped on scratch branches to measure them (marked <span class=\"pill meas\">measured</span>). A reviewer is checking every claim against the source.</p>''',\n'''<p class=\"note\">Ranked in the order the reviewer corrected it to (user-visible impact × how often × how sure). A second agent re-checked every claim against the source and re-measured the key ones. The Brain session is now working through this list, starting with the read lock and the export calls. <b>Realistic cold setup after all of it: about 65–80 s</b>, not the 45–55 s first estimated; only one fix is measured end to end (105 → 87.5 s).</p>''')\nrep('<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fix</th><th>Saving</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead>\\n      <tbody id=\"brain-fixes\">',\n    '<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fix</th><th>Saving</th><th>Review</th></tr></thead>\\n      <tbody id=\"brain-fixes\">')\ni=s.index('const FIXES = ['); j=s.index('];',i)+2\ns=s[:i]+'''const FIXES = [\n  [\"Export: use the local snapshot for checkpoint metadata and explain only checkpoints that are not local; fail fast on a partial clone\", \"hours: cli setup finishes instead of never\", \"big\", \"adjusted: the list call lacks branch and session index, but local refs hold all 5,621\"],\n  [\"Retrieval stops taking the exclusive write lock: read without it, then re-check the privacy policy before answering\", \"brief and brain_brief stop failing during writes; first MCP brief 3.9 s → about 0.5 s\", \"meas\", \"new; failure reproduced at 10.5 s. A shared lock would not help, since it still waits for the writer\"],\n  [\"Stop rebuilding the whole history search index after every change; build it where history changed, with a larger sqlite cache\", \"first query after each new session: about −5 s and −600 MB\", \"est\", \"new; the build is page-cache bound\"],\n  [\"Build history search terms once per record, not once per keyword\", \"history −40% (52 → 31 s); setup −17.7 s\", \"meas\", \"confirmed: 105 → 87.5 s, identical output\"],\n  [\"Update the pattern corpus incrementally after a fact change\", \"−18.7 s, and a 21 s lock hold, on every refresh\", \"est\", \"confirmed and broader: any fact change on any branch\"],\n  [\"Memory worker: jobs and receipts pick the same copy of a session that appears under two branches\", \"3 of 229 sessions start projecting; stale retries stop\", \"est\", \"split: PR #474 fixes only the legacy store; this is a session-ref collision. One counterexample still unexplained\"],\n  [\"Parse each transcript once and decode records into typed structs\", \"about −8–15 s cold, combined\", \"est\", \"adjusted down from −25–35 s; double-counted\"],\n  [\"Run the entity-index graph diffs in parallel or in the background\", \"5–10 s off every re-run\", \"est\", \"adjusted: already skips indexed commits\"],\n  [\"Cache the graph store result per request\", \"brief −90 ms, status −167 ms\", \"meas\", \"adjusted: drop the git-probe memo, it conflicts with recorded security decisions\"],\n  [\"doctor reads health metadata instead of the whole index\", \"−1.0–1.3 s\", \"est\", \"confirmed\"],\n  [\"Run status checks alongside graph context in brief\", \"up to 130 ms\", \"est\", \"confirmed, smaller\"],\n  [\"Call the graph binary directly\", \"about 25 ms per graph call\", \"est\", \"adjusted: an override already exists\"],\n  [\"Trim the MCP tool list\", \"about 8k tokens per agent session\", \"est\", \"client-dependent\"],\n];'''+s[j:]\nrep('''<li>A background memory worker retries 3 jobs that always fail (<span class=\"mono\">memory_source_stale</span>), every time setup or MCP starts, backing off up to about 30 minutes.</li>''',\n'''<li>A background memory worker retries 3 jobs that always fail (<span class=\"mono\">memory_source_stale</span>), every time setup or MCP starts. Cause: a session recorded under both an empty branch and <span class=\"mono\">main</span> shares one ID, and the job and the receipt keep different copies. PR #474 does not fix this case.</li>\n        <li>An idle memory-worker pass still takes about 8.5 s and holds the write lock.</li>\n        <li><span class=\"mono\">remember</span> reports success, but <span class=\"mono\">recall</span> cannot find the memory until a refresh, and nothing says so (reported by the Brain session).</li>''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Update the artifact's Brain tab with the review verdicts"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2063,"cache_read_input_tokens":126079,"output_tokens":2650,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":308},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2063,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2650,"cache_read_input_tokens":126079,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2063,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2063},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01S9RKR6cXTC3yTurTMJ4BxT":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html'\ns=open(p).read()\ndef rep(a,b):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nrep('''<div class=\"callout\"><b>Setup on the cli repo never finishes.</b> Export makes one <span class=\"mono\">entire checkpoint explain</span> call per checkpoint, 5,621 of them, one after another, at 2.5–3.6 s each: about 4–5.6 hours. The list call it already makes returns most of that data in 5.8 s.</div>''',\n'''<div class=\"callout\"><b>Setup on the cli repo never finishes.</b> Export makes one <span class=\"mono\">entire checkpoint explain</span> call per checkpoint, 5,621 of them, one after another, at 2.5–3.6 s each: about 4–5.6 hours, and then it fails on the partial clone anyway. The local refs already hold all 5,621 checkpoints, so those calls are pure overhead.</div>\n    <div class=\"callout\"><b>Agents' brief calls fail while Brain writes.</b> Read paths take the exclusive write lock, so <span class=\"mono\">brief</span> and MCP <span class=\"mono\">brain_brief</span> give up with <span class=\"mono\">brain_locked</span> after 10.5 s whenever a writer holds it. Writers hold it for 8–32 s, during setup, refresh after <span class=\"mono\">remember</span>, and background memory passes. Found by the review.</div>''')\nrep('note: \"Waits on a background worker that holds the write lock; uses only 320 ms of CPU.\"',\n    'note: \"Waits on a background worker that holds the write lock (reads take the exclusive lock); uses only 320 ms of CPU. With a longer write in progress it fails at 10.5 s instead.\"')\nrep('''<p class=\"note\">Proposals only: no Brain fixes are being made right now. Two were prototyped on scratch branches to measure them (marked <span class=\"pill meas\">measured</span>). A reviewer is checking every claim against the source.</p>''',\n'''<p class=\"note\">Ranked in the order the reviewer corrected it to (user-visible impact × how often × how sure). A second agent re-checked every claim against the source and re-measured the key ones. The Brain session is now working through this list, starting with the read lock and the export calls. <b>Realistic cold setup after all of it: about 65–80 s</b>, not the 45–55 s first estimated; only one fix is measured end to end (105 → 87.5 s).</p>''')\nrep('<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fix</th><th>Saving</th><th>Basis</th></tr></thead>\\n      <tbody id=\"brain-fixes\">',\n    '<thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Fix</th><th>Saving</th><th>Review</th></tr></thead>\\n      <tbody id=\"brain-fixes\">')\ni=s.index('const FIXES = ['); j=s.index('];',i)+2\ns=s[:i]+'''const FIXES = [\n  [\"Export: use the local snapshot for checkpoint metadata and explain only checkpoints that are not local; fail fast on a partial clone\", \"hours: cli setup finishes instead of never\", \"big\", \"adjusted: the list call lacks branch and session index, but local refs hold all 5,621\"],\n  [\"Retrieval stops taking the exclusive write lock: read without it, then re-check the privacy policy before answering\", \"brief and brain_brief stop failing during writes; first MCP brief 3.9 s → about 0.5 s\", \"meas\", \"new; failure reproduced at 10.5 s. A shared lock would not help, since it still waits for the writer\"],\n  [\"Stop rebuilding the whole history search index after every change; build it where history changed, with a larger sqlite cache\", \"first query after each new session: about −5 s and −600 MB\", \"est\", \"new; the build is page-cache bound\"],\n  [\"Build history search terms once per record, not once per keyword\", \"history −40% (52 → 31 s); setup −17.7 s\", \"meas\", \"confirmed: 105 → 87.5 s, identical output\"],\n  [\"Update the pattern corpus incrementally after a fact change\", \"−18.7 s, and a 21 s lock hold, on every refresh\", \"est\", \"confirmed and broader: any fact change on any branch\"],\n  [\"Memory worker: jobs and receipts pick the same copy of a session that appears under two branches\", \"3 of 229 sessions start projecting; stale retries stop\", \"est\", \"split: PR #474 fixes only the legacy store; this is a session-ref collision. One counterexample still unexplained\"],\n  [\"Parse each transcript once and decode records into typed structs\", \"about −8–15 s cold, combined\", \"est\", \"adjusted down from −25–35 s; double-counted\"],\n  [\"Run the entity-index graph diffs in parallel or in the background\", \"5–10 s off every re-run\", \"est\", \"adjusted: already skips indexed commits\"],\n  [\"Cache the graph store result per request\", \"brief −90 ms, status −167 ms\", \"meas\", \"adjusted: drop the git-probe memo, it conflicts with recorded security decisions\"],\n  [\"doctor reads health metadata instead of the whole index\", \"−1.0–1.3 s\", \"est\", \"confirmed\"],\n  [\"Run status checks alongside graph context in brief\", \"up to 130 ms\", \"est\", \"confirmed, smaller\"],\n  [\"Call the graph binary directly\", \"about 25 ms per graph call\", \"est\", \"adjusted: an override already exists\"],\n  [\"Trim the MCP tool list\", \"about 8k tokens per agent session\", \"est\", \"client-dependent\"],\n];'''+s[j:]\nrep('''<li>A background memory worker retries 3 jobs that always fail (<span class=\"mono\">memory_source_stale</span>), every time setup or MCP starts, backing off up to about 30 minutes.</li>''',\n'''<li>A background memory worker retries 3 jobs that always fail (<span class=\"mono\">memory_source_stale</span>), every time setup or MCP starts. Cause: a session recorded under both an empty branch and <span class=\"mono\">main</span> shares one ID, and the job and the receipt keep different copies. PR #474 does not fix this case.</li>\n        <li>An idle memory-worker pass still takes about 8.5 s and holds the write lock.</li>\n        <li><span class=\"mono\">remember</span> reports success, but <span class=\"mono\">recall</span> cannot find the memory until a refresh, and nothing says so (reported by the Brain session).</li>''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Update the artifact's Brain tab with the review verdicts"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ce246751-69d6-4317-92eb-b747f0fe7b56","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMWLmCPx998BF9iT8HH3","requestRef":"72fde0e6-2ca4-4a72-bdd9-337f24f39038","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"459acd4c-d963-4cbb-abc7-715b4432f62a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:06:54.521Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug"