{"parentUuid":"d389828c-35d8-4d99-869a-3bf17dd8f63c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMWYiJr3HtyNcy1NLtUM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SdJ6BTNTbitAtvUbDX92eL","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"A1 fired; retraction applied; B1 order + store list","message":"**A1 fired.** The graph timing study is done (`devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md`). Heavy work may start, in Phase B order.\n\n**Retraction applied.** I'm pulling the remember/recall bullet from the artifact, and I won't propose an index append. I'm adding your line to the plan's rules: \"facts are per-branch copies forked from main, not a shared store; anything that reads or writes them names its branch\". The real defect stays on the list: recall on a branch without the facts says \"corpus exhausted\". So does the usability line for `remember --branch X` when you're standing on Y. Thanks for running the control.\n\n**Order from here, one heavy job at a time:**\n1. **B1, mine, now:** deleting the 123 stale clones (79.9 GB), the Ollama models and the old Rust toolchains. About 10-20 minutes of heavy disk I/O. I'm posting a `heavy: B1 deletions` row on the board and will ping when it's clear. M1 design and coding is fine during it; timing isn't.\n2. **B2, yours:** the re-index (entire-graph → entire-brain → entiredb), plus your #2 before/after timing window.\n3. **B3, mine:** `entire graph setup` once per repo, then the prewarm.\n\n**Stray Brain stores: your store, so your call and your hands.** I'd rather you delete these yourself, since you know whether anything registers them. If you'd rather I do it, an explicit \"OK, delete list X\" works.\n\nStray candidates under `repos/gh/`, about 0.6 GB in total:\n- **Hackathon/demo stores:**\n  - 164imran/hack_paris, alexandre-martel/rseach, alexdebelka/guillotine\n  - alvaro5/, aminechr54/, ansh2508/, gablandman/, valikprogrammer/ (all ehl-paris medical-retrieval)\n  - chenxshuo/researcher-baobyte (182M), enyolanev-bit/lucky-loop, gabriel-libardi/latenthackers, jakobtfr/ehl-paris\n  - luraxx/msd-floorplan-challenge, ouazzmoh/bourbaki-paris-2, sokcevic/hackathon-paris, tangafua/tum.ai-hackathon, yudjinsud/masloriji (106M)\n- **Ours, but dead:**\n  - entireio/entire-sem (65M; the old name of entire-graph)\n  - entireio/acme-payments (fixture)\n  - cli/cli (341M; GitHub's gh, not ours)\n- **Under `repos/local/`:** about 90 empty `cli-<hash>` dirs, plus test leftovers (demo-repo, myproject, proj, proj2, repro-dirty-gate, the 2 image-mocktest stores, entire-native).\n\n**NOT on my list:**\n- suhaanthayyil/bioinformed-brca-risk: Suhaan's own repo; leave it.\n- ashtom/entire-brain (3.6G), entirehq/entire.io (11G), entirehq/entire-api (650M), entirehq/devenv: these come under your full-store decision after fix #1.\n\n**Graph numbers you can use** (latest main, warm cache):\n- def/neighbors/impact take about 0.4-0.67 s.\n- `graph context` takes 0.18 s.\n- The sqlite store is 18-27x bigger and is only written with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1`. Without that env var, `store` and `context` return `store_unavailable`. If Brain relies on `graph store`, check whether your setup sets that var. That could be the \"search store not built for this commit\" you saw.\n- Exact-name queries can take 355 s on entire-graph (alias git-grep preselect). That's my top fix, and it's the same class as your reviewer's 45.9 s preselect.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"**A1 fired.** The graph timing study is done (`de…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4593,"cache_read_input_tokens":174998,"output_tokens":3855,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1582},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_t