o main after a branch forked are invisible from that branch until `memories promote`. Anything that reads or writes facts names its branch explicitly."," "," ## Phase A: finish measuring (now)"," | # | Who | What | Done when | Hands off |"," |---|---|---|---|---|","-| A1 | graph | Graph timing study P1 finishes (latest main d4a0c186) | `devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md` exists | graph pings brain: **heavy I/O may start** |","-| A2 | graph | Adversarial review of the Brain speed list | `devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` exists | graph pings brain: **start Brain fixes (C2)** |","+| A1 ✅ | graph | Graph timing study P1 finishes (latest main d4a0c186) | `devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md` exists | graph pings brain: **heavy I/O may start** |","+| A2 ✅ | graph | Adversarial review of the Brain speed list | `devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` exists | graph pings brain: **start Brain fixes (C2)** |"," "," Until A1 ends, neither session runs heavy disk or CPU work (full suites, re-index, large deletes). The timing is"," being measured."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/CODEBASE-MAP.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":254,"oldLines":7,"newStart":254,"newLines":7,"lines":["   - Open, mine: #142 (rescope: drop `--max-seconds`, keep cancellation plus `refuseTruncatedSnapshot` in all","     three writers), partial-clone `index --head` refusal (breaks Brain on devenv/cli), and follow-ups issue #325.","   - Timing study of every process on d4a0c186: `devenv-worktrees/timing/`. Overview page:","-    https://claude.ai/artifact/1YbGGd5Gk19omne4PyU7h1","+    https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU","   - Agents reach the graph through `.entire/agent-guide.md` plus a `SubagentStart` hook in","     `.claude/settings.local.json`. Explore/Plan subagents never load CLAUDE.md, so the hook is the only way the","     guidance reaches them."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md","/Users/suhaan/devenv/CODEBASE-MAP.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"407b05fb-7281-4f82-b940-f7820c71a1f2","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":282},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ccc6b896-8824-4450-b7b7-b89cc9279d9a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"2d157e68-b9d9-451a-aed0-f6f7843a54b2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html","snippet":""},"type":"attachment","uuid":"45e42099-248a-47a4-b097-6ec21d17f8b9","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:09:52.487Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. The changes are not shown here; use Read if you need the current content.\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"4f723866737eb26366a6c5bbfecfeb41161d435347ea60689c0f029f87198242","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SdJ6BTNTbitAtvUbDX92eL","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"A1 fired; retraction applied; B1 order + store list","message":"**A1 fired.** The graph timing study is done (`devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md`). Heavy work may start, in Phase B order.\n\n**Retraction applied.** I'm pulling the remember/recall bullet from the artifact, and I won't propose an index append. I'm adding your line to the plan's rules: \"facts are per-branch copies forked from main, not a shared store; anything that reads or writes them names its branch\". The real defect stays on the list: recall on a branch without the facts says \"corpus exhausted\". So does the usability line for `remember --branch X` when you're standing on Y. Thanks for running the control.\n\n**Order from here, one heavy job at a time:**\n1. **B1, mine, now:** deleting the 123 stale clones (79.9 GB), the Ollama models and the old Rust toolchains. About 10-20 minutes of heavy disk I/O. I'm posting a `heavy: B1 deletions` row on the board and will ping when it's clear. M1 design and coding is fine during it; timing isn't.\n2. **B2, yours:** the re-index (entire-graph → entire-brain → entiredb), plus your #2 before/after timing window.\n3. **B3, mine:** `entire graph setup` once per repo, then the prewarm.\n\n**Stray Brain stores: your store, so your call and your hands.** I'd rather you delete these yourself, since you know whether anything registers them. If you'd rather I do it, an explicit \"OK, delete list X\" works.\n\nStray candidates under `repos/gh/`, about 0.6 GB in total:\n- **Hackathon/demo stores:**\n  - 164imran/hack_paris, alexandre-martel/rseach, alexdebelka/guillotine\n  - alvaro5/, aminechr54/, ansh2508/, gablandman/, valikprogrammer/ (all ehl-paris medical-retrieval)\n  - chenxshuo/researcher-baobyte (182M), enyolanev-bit/lucky-loop, gabriel-libardi/latenthackers, jakobtfr/ehl-paris\n  - luraxx/msd-floorplan-challenge, ouazzmoh/bourbaki-paris-2, sokcevic/hackathon-paris, tangafua/tum.ai-hackathon, yudjinsud/masloriji (106M)\n- **Ours, but dead:**\n  - entireio/entire-sem (65M; the old name of entire-graph)\n  - entireio/acme-payments (fixture)\n  - cli/cli (341M; GitHub's gh, not ours)\n- **Under `repos/local/`:** about 90 empty `cli-<hash>` dirs, plus test leftovers (demo-repo, myproject, proj, proj2, repro-dirty-gate, the 2 image-mocktest stores, entire-native).\n\n**NOT on my list:**\n- suhaanthayyil/bioinformed-brca-risk: Suhaan's own repo; leave it.\n- ashtom/entire-brain (3.6G), entirehq/entire.io (11G), entirehq/entire-api (650M), entirehq/devenv: these come under your full-store decision after fix #1.\n\n**Graph numbers you can use** (latest main, warm cache):\n- def/neighbors/impact take about 0.4-0.67 s.\n- `graph context` takes 0.18 s.\n- The sqlite store is 18-27x bigger and is only written with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1`. Without that env var, `store` and `context` return `store_unavailable`. If Brain relies on `graph store`, check whether your setup sets that var. That could be the \"search store not built for this commit\" you saw.\n- Exact-name queries can take 355 s on entire-graph (alias git-grep preselect). That's my top fix, and it's the same class as your reviewer's 45.9 s preselect."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LFMVb2YVpNuyuKgWv2p3J3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/process-map/process-map.html'\ns=open(p).read()\na='''        <li><span class=\"mono\">remember</span> reports success, but <span class=\"mono\">recall</span> cannot find the memory until a refresh, and nothing says so (reported by the Brain session).</li>\\n'''\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'''        <li>On a branch that does not hold a memory, <span class=\"mono\">recall</span> returns nothing and says the store is exhausted. Memories are per-branch copies forked from <span class=\"mono\">main</span>, and <span class=\"mono\">remember --branch X</span> gives no hint when you are standing on another branch.</li>\\n''')\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na='- ask before touching the other\\'s repo or any shared state\\n'\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+'- **Brain facts are per-branch copies forked from main, not a shared store.** Facts written to main after a branch forked are invisible from that branch until `memories promote`. Anything that reads or writes facts names its branch explicitly.\\n')\ns=s.replace('| A1 | graph | Graph timing study P1 finishes','| A1 ✅ | graph | Graph timing study P1 finishes')\ns=s.replace('| A2 | graph | Adversarial review','| A2 ✅ | graph | Adversarial review')\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\nsed -i '' 's#https://claude.ai/artifact/1YbGGd5Gk19omne4PyU7h1#https://claude.ai/artifact/FkY6c5J1XdzaYGM1Q7T9dU#' /Users/suhaan/devenv/CODEBASE-MAP.md\nhead -5 /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/cleanup-audit/delete-check.txt; wc -l /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/cleanup-audit/delete-check.txt; ls -la /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/cleanup-audit/delete-check.txt","description":"Fix artifact bullet, update plan, inspect deletion list"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
