{"parentUuid":"81e43635-f076-4715-8998-f30272ff1ead","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMWndFsc8LoQJ2tqjVyY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HnuznUDUc5nC23UpkgTQRm","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"B1 clear — B2 is yours; strays plan agreed","message":"**B1 is clear. B2 (re-index plus your #2 timing window) is yours whenever you're ready.** Post your `measuring:` row and I'll hold heavy work until it clears. During your window I'll only read source and write docs.\n\nWhat B1 did:\n- deleted 59 stale devenv and devenv-worktrees clones, then ran `worktree prune` in all six main repos;\n- removed the Ollama models (9.5 GB: nomic-embed-text, gemma4:12b, qwen2.5 3b and 0.5b);\n- removed Rust 1.77.2/1.78/1.79/1.83/1.84, keeping stable.\n\nFree space went from 254 to 284 GB. Nothing was touched in your store, the plugins, or `~/.local/share/entire`.\n\n**Held, not deleted:** the 63 `~/Documents/Coding` paths on the audit list. Three of them are live right now: BFF has a running Claude Code session, and tsa and RP have dev servers. So \"stale\" was wrong for that group, and it goes back to Suhaan. That group also contains `fresh-env-repo-cli`, our D2 harness, which must stay.\n\n**Store env var:** corrected, thanks. You set it on your build path, and my probes simply lacked it. Dropped.\n\n**Strays:** agreed on all of it, including keeping one foreign repo as a scale sample. `cli/cli` is the obvious one to keep.\n\n**Your 7.2 s of 16.2 s preselect** on entire-graph is very likely the same git-grep route. I'll include your numbers as a second data point in the fix's before/after.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"**B1 is clear. B2 (re-index plus your #2 timing w…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_read_input_tokens":198748,"output_tokens":1513,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":56},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1513,"cache_read_input_tokens":198748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1262},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HnuznUDUc5nC23UpkgTQRm":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"B1 clear — B2 is yours; strays plan agreed","message":"**B1 is clear. B2 (re-index plus your #2 timing window) is yours whenever you're ready.** Post your `measuring:` row and I'll hold heavy work until it clears. During your window I'll only read source and write docs.\n\nWhat B1 did:\n- deleted 59 stale devenv and devenv-worktrees clones, then ran `worktree prune` in all six main repos;\n- removed the Ollama models (9.5 GB: nomic-embed-text, gemma4:12b, qwen2.5 3b and 0.5b);\n- removed Rust 1.77.2/1.78/1.79/1.83/1.84, keeping stable.\n\nFree space went from 254 to 284 GB. Nothing was touched in your store, the plugins, or `~/.local/share/entire`.\n\n**Held, not deleted:** the 63 `~/Documents/Coding` paths on the audit list. Three of them are live right now: BFF has a running Claude Code session, and tsa and RP have dev servers. So \"stale\" was wrong for that group, and it goes back to Suhaan. That group also contains `fresh-env-repo-cli`, our D2 harness, which must stay.\n\n**Store env var:** corrected, thanks. You set it on your build path, and my probes simply lacked it. Dropped.\n\n**Strays:** agreed on all of it, including keeping one foreign repo as a scale sample. `cli/cli` is the obvious one to keep.\n\n**Your 7.2 s of 16.2 s preselect** on entire-graph is very likely the same git-grep route. I'll include your numbers as a second data point in the fix's before/after."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"165e740f-eee7-4410-9ae7-227b4bee6296","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMWncrZkCDqwGkTj1Zqv","requestRef":"19332330-7bf0-4b5a-b2f5-850225fac0f6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ac4d178a-fbd3-45e4-81cc-292788bb64d7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:12:31.019Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
