{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"d9e1f0074d39bbf0aab0488b8b7027ab7b08eb10b284c40281dc0187dfb1fe49","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"B1 is done: free space went from 254 to 284 GB. Handing B2 to the Brain session:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HnuznUDUc5nC23UpkgTQRm","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"B1 clear — B2 is yours; strays plan agreed","message":"**B1 is clear. B2 (re-index plus your #2 timing window) is yours whenever you're ready.** Post your `measuring:` row and I'll hold heavy work until it clears. During your window I'll only read source and write docs.\n\nWhat B1 did:\n- deleted 59 stale devenv and devenv-worktrees clones, then ran `worktree prune` in all six main repos;\n- removed the Ollama models (9.5 GB: nomic-embed-text, gemma4:12b, qwen2.5 3b and 0.5b);\n- removed Rust 1.77.2/1.78/1.79/1.83/1.84, keeping stable.\n\nFree space went from 254 to 284 GB. Nothing was touched in your store, the plugins, or `~/.local/share/entire`.\n\n**Held, not deleted:** the 63 `~/Documents/Coding` paths on the audit list. Three of them are live right now: BFF has a running Claude Code session, and tsa and RP have dev servers. So \"stale\" was wrong for that group, and it goes back to Suhaan. That group also contains `fresh-env-repo-cli`, our D2 harness, which must stay.\n\n**Store env var:** corrected, thanks. You set it on your build path, and my probes simply lacked it. Dropped.\n\n**Strays:** agreed on all of it, including keeping one foreign repo as a scale sample. `cli/cli` is the obvious one to keep.\n\n**Your 7.2 s of 16.2 s preselect** on entire-graph is very likely the same git-grep route. I'll include your numbers as a second data point in the fix's before/after."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LvyCtmMbn8VUzfwTD6HY9w","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['B1'].update(status='done', note='Deleted 59 stale devenv/devenv-worktrees clones (+ worktree prune), Ollama models 9.5 GB, Rust 1.77-1.84. Free 254 → 284 GB. Strays: brain deletes after B2. Held for user: 63 ~/Documents/Coding paths (see B1-docs).')\nif 'B1-docs' not in T:\n    i=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('B1')+1\n    d['tasks'].insert(i, dict(id='B1-docs',lane='graph',title='Your call: 63 ~/Documents/Coding paths on the cleanup list',status='blocked',owner='user',source='proactive',\n      note='Held: 3 are in use (BFF has a Claude session open, tsa and RP have dev servers running), and fresh-env-repo-cli is the test harness. The group mixes personal projects with old Entire experiment clones. The list is in the cleanup-audit folder. Waiting on a yes or no for each group.'))\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF\ncp /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/scratchpad/b1-doc.txt /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/cleanup-audit/held-documents-coding.txt","description":"Mark B1 done and record the held list for the user"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
