-|\n| 1 | **Exact-name preselect: stop running the alias ERE `git grep -E -m 1 -f -` over the commit.** Use fixed strings with `-l` (`-F -i -l`), the cached term index, or a hard cap. | preselect (exact-name / alias route) | **8 s (cli) to about 6 min (entire-graph) per bare-identifier query.** Also likely the Brain reviewer's 45.9 s preselect on a cache hit, and the Brain session's 7.2 s of a 16.2 s query. | timing; earlier note: git grep multi-pattern hang |\n| 2 | **Widen the ordered per-file pipeline window.** Admit workers×16 items and keep 8 running, so one slow head file no longer stalls the rest. | `runIndexedStreamingPipeline` | **cold index cli 11.2 → 8.0 s (−29%), brain 14.3 → 9.1 s (−36%).** Applies to every cold verb. | **measured** with a local patch; snapshot sha256 byte-identical |\n| 3 | **Skip the preselect content scan on a cold query when a complete build follows anyway.** | cold query | **−4.2 s (cli), −6.3 s (brain) per cold query.** Closes most of the cold-query regression (0.65-0.90x vs OLD). | step map |\n| 4 | **Cache-hit history refresh: merge in place with an allocation-free comparator, and memoize per commit** instead of `git log -256` plus a full string-concat re-sort on every hit. | preindex load (a902231f / 07c7d0fe, 2026-10-16) | **−0.15-0.2 s per warm op (1.5-2 s per session).** Fixes the warm def/neighbors/impact regression (0.68-0.85x). | step map |\n| 5 | **Stop persisting the derived selective view on every novel warm query.** | warm query | **−0.5-0.7 s per warm query, about 2.5-3.4 s per session** | step map; 0.67 s of syscall blocking is this write |\n| 6 | **Relation producers: replace per-pattern regex with a shared single-pass lexer or shared tokens.** Regex is 54% of cold CPU (backtracking 43.6%). | returnFlowCalls, receiverCallRelations, httpCallsWithConstants | estimated −2-4 s per cold build, and the bound once #2 lands | CPU profile |\n| 7 | **Fold goHTTPRouteRelations and the other route passes into the parallel scan.** | routePasses (14.9%, single-threaded) | estimated −1-1.7 s per cold build | step map |\n| 8 | **Precompute rank token variants per candidate.** | rank (tokenVariants 14.7%, searchTermCounts 17.7%) | estimated −0.5-1 s per warm query | CPU profile |\n| 9 | **Snapshot decode** needs a faster format. The sqlite store is mixed (cli −0.9 s, brain +0.8 s) and 18-27x larger. | preindex load | −0.35-0.46 s per warm op | step map; needs a design |\n| 10 | Small: reuse the triple `prepareSource`, allocation-free sort comparator, parallel similarity, cheaper gzip level | query / build | −0.2-0.3 s per query; −0.5-1.5 s per cold build | step map |\n\n## Correctness defects (found by the Brain reviewer)\n\n| # | Defect | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| C1 | **`neighbors` misses function-value references.** openHistoryFTS reported no callers, but `history_fts.go:824` (entire-brain) passes it as a value. | `entire graph neighbors --symbol openHistoryFTS --direction in` |\n| C2 | **A spurious duplicate `kind=tool` definition** for historyTerms (`history.go:2442`) makes `impact` ambiguous. Likely the HANDLES_TOOL heuristic. | `entire graph impact --symbol historyTerms` |\n| C3 | **Query preselect took 45.9 s of a 53.2 s query on a cache HIT** (entire-brain). Probably the same route as #1; confirm before folding it in. | BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md |\n\n## Graph items that block Brain\n\n| # | Item | Effect |\n|---|---|---|\n| B-a | **Partial clones: `index --head` refuses a `blob:none` promisor clone.** The graph does emit E_NO_GIT_HEAD on the trailing summary record. | Brain's semantic index fails on devenv/cli. The acceptance test for Brain fix #1 needs this. |\n| B-b | **Per-commit store.** The store is keyed to the commit, so each new commit drops code context from brief until Brain re-indexes. | Expected behaviour, but costs a full rebuild per commit. An incremental store, or reusing a clean parent's store, would close it. |\n| B-c | Host dispatch overhead per `entire graph` call | About 25 ms (Brain reviewer); `ENTIRE_BRAIN_GRAPH_BINARY` already bypasses it. Low. |\n\n## Also open\n\n- **#142 rescope (C4):** drop `--max-seconds` and the partial path. Keep cancellation, `refuseTruncatedSnapshot` in all\n  three writers plus its test, the filterActive guard, and the TestTF142R6 allowlist entry.\n- **The store is written only with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1`.** Brain sets it on its build path. `graph store`\n  and `graph context` called outside Brain return `store_unavailable`. That is a usability edge, not a bug.\n\n## Order of work (G3)\n\n#1 → #2 → #3 → #4 → C1 → C2 → B-a → #5 → #6 → #7 → #8, then #9 and #10 as time allows.\nEach fix gets:\n- one PR off fresh main;\n- an interleaved old/new before/after in a `measuring:` window;\n- a byte-identical output check, or a stated and tested output change;\n- a mutation-proven test.\n\nPRs stay open.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d0d01bed-127a-439c-9c20-02b7a1591fc2","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMWojk6EsmXNGDirxcyw","requestRef":"8abbd76d-01aa-453d-92db-dcd3d7a503f1","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8427587a-6f48-4f59-b0ed-8da39611b685","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:13:06.105Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
