{"parentUuid":"84eb4ba8-16af-4548-9d6f-88eb7c867830","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fb5d4d77-2c82-43ae-889b-106f286917f8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HLQm8cMTbhhpW2G3akDxn5","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: af968b846daa58e1a (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'af968b846daa58e1a', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/af968b846daa58e1a.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"41f5e811-29f0-42fd-9ebb-002bf8be86bb","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:14:03.530Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"af968b846daa58e1a","description":"Adversarial review of graph speedup list","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You are an adversarial reviewer. Default stance on every claim: REFUTED unless you independently confirm it from source (file:line) or a light reproduction. Output: caveman-ultra compressed (dense bullets, no prose padding, keep every file:line and number). Use RTK for shell (commands are auto-rewritten; `rtk proxy <cmd>` for raw).\n\n## Goal\nVerify every item in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS.md` (a ranked list of entire-graph speed + correctness fixes, written from a timing study). Write your verdicts to `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`. Do NOT edit GRAPH-SPEEDUPS.md. The fixes will be implemented one PR each right after your review, so the useful output is: is the mechanism real, is the saving plausible, and **does the proposed fix change output semantics** (and how to prove it doesn't).\n\n## Inputs\n- Study outputs: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/PROCESS-MAP.md`, `results.md`, `stepmaps/process-maps.md`, `stepmaps/prof/` (pprof top lists), `raw/runs.jsonl`.\n- Source at main d4a0c186: read from `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/eg/` (clean clone of NEW). `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/eg-prof/` is a locally patched copy holding the measured pipeline-window patch for item #2 — diff it against eg/ to review that patch. Never commit in either.\n- Brain reviewer's graph findings (C1-C3) came from running against the entire-brain repo: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/brain-timing/BRAIN-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`.\n\n## Per item, specifically\n- #1 exact-name preselect (`git grep -E -m 1 -f - <commit>` alias route, 355 s on entire-graph): find the code path, why the alias ERE route exists, whether `-F -i -l` (or the term index) gives identical candidate sets. What does `-m 1` + ERE alternation semantics require? Is C3 (45.9 s preselect on a cache HIT in entire-brain) the same route?\n- #2 pipeline window: review the eg-prof patch for ordering/determinism, memory bound, cancellation, error propagation.\n- #3 skip cold-query preselect scan: does preselect output feed ranking, candidate filtering, or the selective view? If it changes which files rank, it is not free.\n- #4 cache-hit history refresh re-sort (commits a902231f / 07c7d0fe, 2026-10-16): why was the re-sort added? Is memoizing per commit safe?\n- #5 persisting the selective view on every novel warm query: is a later query reading it? What breaks if skipped?\n- #6-#10: plausibility only; flag anything that is wrong.\n- C1 (neighbors misses function-value refs), C2 (duplicate kind=tool def for historyTerms): reproduce with warm-cache queries against `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain`, then locate the producer code.\n- B-a (index --head refuses partial clones): find the refusal and say what a safe fix looks like.\n\n## Tools: required order\n1. Preflight once: `entire graph version --json`, `entire graph capabilities --json`, `entire brain version`, `entire brain capabilities --json`. Record them.\n2. Relationships (callers, callees, blast radius) MUST go through the graph first: `entire graph def|neighbors|impact --repo <eg clone> --head ...`, and `entire graph query --repo <clone> --head --format agent --max-context-bytes 4096 --query \"...\"`. grep is only a supplement.\n3. Prior decisions and why code exists: `entire brain recall \"<question>\" --json` run in `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph`. Cite fact ids. An empty result is not proof.\n\n## Hard constraints\n- **Another session (Brain) has a timing window and re-index running on this machine.** NO heavy CPU or disk:\n  - no cold index builds;\n  - no `go test ./...` or full suites;\n  - no reproducing the 355 s query;\n  - no parallel builds.\n  Run `uptime` first. Warm-cache graph queries, `git` plumbing and reading source are fine. Focused `go test -run <one test>` with GOMAXPROCS=2 is OK, at most a few.\n- If a claim needs a measurement, write the exact command into `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/g2-measure.sh` (interleaved old/new, separate `--cache-dir` per binary, 3 reps). Do not run it. Binaries: `timing/bin/eg-new`, `timing/bin/eg-old`.\n- Read-only otherwise:\n  - no commits, pushes or PRs;\n  - do not touch `~/.local/share/entire` (Brain store, plugins);\n  - never `entire brain setup`/`refresh`/`--daemon`;\n  - no git stash.\n\n## Report back (≤ 60 lines)\n- A table: item | CONFIRMED / ADJUSTED / REFUTED | evidence (file:line, fact id) | corrected saving | semantics risk + how to prove no output change.\n- New items you found.\n- Your corrected order of work.\n- What g2-measure.sh needs a quiet window for.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/af968b846daa58e1a.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ed2f4a6d-94b5-4e7a-be7d-827a6e754e4d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"84eb4ba8-16af-4548-9d6f-88eb7c867830","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
