{"parentUuid":"0240849e-8b15-4211-9283-a61bc47a25db","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMXuEgNo2NhVqVzXeJUe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PR3kEpARdAkh9AVty9TJaL","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-gitignore-worktrees && git push -q -u origin chore/gitignore-claude-worktrees 2>&1 | tail -2; gh pr create --repo entireio/entire-graph --base main --head chore/gitignore-claude-worktrees --title \"chore: ignore nested Claude Code worktrees\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n## Summary\nClaude Code checks out nested worktrees of this repository under `.claude/worktrees/`. They are untracked copies of the repo itself, so they show up in `git status` and make the working tree look dirty.\n\nThat has two concrete costs:\n- Tools that gate on a clean tree refuse to run. Entire Brain's seed step reports `dirty_worktree` and skips the repository entirely.\n- The nested checkouts inflate the working-tree digest the graph computes for uncommitted-mode queries.\n\nThis adds one `.gitignore` entry for the directory.\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `git check-ignore -v .claude/worktrees/main` matches the new rule.\n- [x] No tracked file lives under `.claude/worktrees/` on main (`git ls-files .claude/worktrees` is empty).\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1; git check-ignore -v .claude/worktrees/main; git ls-files .claude/worktrees | wc -l","description":"Push the branch and open the gitignore PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":246306,"output_tokens":1002,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":454},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":558,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens"