{"parentUuid":"c311d250-1aaa-4b45-a000-9cfed7632ce3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZv5R3HgSQXP5eVQQNg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MLwaCyFESbNWuEHF6fRUpT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-1: alias git grep fix","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #1 (+N1): the alias `git grep` preselect\nRead rows #1, C3 and N1 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first. That review overrides the original list. Summary of what it established:\n- **Route.** search.go:2577-2623, the alias route. It fires when any query term has an abbreviation alias (repository→repo, synchronous→sync). It is not about bare identifiers, and it runs only on a cache HIT. It calls git.go:649-700: `git grep -E -m 1 -f - <commit>` over the whole commit, then filters to `allowed[]` at :2607.\n- **Cost.** About 97% of the 355 s on entire-graph is scanning blobs the graph already excludes from its corpus: the .graphignored tree-sitter `parser.c`/`scanner.c`, 226 MB in total, with one 9.7 MB parser.c taking 24.5 s.\n  - cli: 7.80 s with `-m 1` vs 0.93 s with `-l`.\n  - entire-brain (C3): 45.10 s vs 2.51 s.\n  - Captured patterns are in `timing/g2-patterns/`.\n- **Fix the reviewer endorses:** keep the SAME ERE (do NOT switch to `-F -i -l`, whose substring alias hits and the `-I` asymmetry at :2625 would change results). Then:\n  - restrict the grep to corpus paths, i.e. exclude non-corpus paths by pathspec or by passing the allowed set. That is exact by construction, since those files are filtered out after the grep anyway;\n  - use `-l` for the same file set (count verified on 3 repos by the reviewer);\n  - keep content validation via the existing matcher.\n- **Edge to handle explicitly.** Oversize unreadable hits, e.g. brain `benchmarks/.../SNAPSHOT.json` at 17.6 MB, where `-m1` alone costs 30 s. textMatchesSearchQuery is monotone and line-local, so the result stays exact apart from those. Decide the behaviour, then test and disclose it. The `FilesContentRead` stat may rise; say so in the PR.\n\n## Done means\n- **Base vs new**, interleaved, under the lock:\n  - the exact `SearchRepository` query on entire-graph (base: 1 rep only, it takes about 6 min);\n  - `OpenRepository` on cli;\n  - the C3 query on entire-brain (pattern file `brain.c3.ere`; find the query text that triggers it via the review or `g2-measure.sh` block grep1/e2e1).\n- **Output identity:** JSON byte-compare after `g2-strip.py` on all three. Also cover a fixture with an oversize file.\n- **Tests:**\n  - a test pinning that non-corpus paths are never scanned, and that results are unchanged;\n  - the oversize case;\n  - each weakened to red and then restored.\n- **PR** open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-alias-grep`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":257419,"output_tokens":4303,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":61},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4303,"cache_read_input_tokens":257419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MLwaCyFESbNWuEHF6fRUpT":{"description":"G3-1: alias git grep fix","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #1 (+N1): the alias `git grep` preselect\nRead rows #1, C3 and N1 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first. That review overrides the original list. Summary of what it established:\n- **Route.** search.go:2577-2623, the alias route. It fires when any query term has an abbreviation alias (repository→repo, synchronous→sync). It is not about bare identifiers, and it runs only on a cache HIT. It calls git.go:649-700: `git grep -E -m 1 -f - <commit>` over the whole commit, then filters to `allowed[]` at :2607.\n- **Cost.** About 97% of the 355 s on entire-graph is scanning blobs the graph already excludes from its corpus: the .graphignored tree-sitter `parser.c`/`scanner.c`, 226 MB in total, with one 9.7 MB parser.c taking 24.5 s.\n  - cli: 7.80 s with `-m 1` vs 0.93 s with `-l`.\n  - entire-brain (C3): 45.10 s vs 2.51 s.\n  - Captured patterns are in `timing/g2-patterns/`.\n- **Fix the reviewer endorses:** keep the SAME ERE (do NOT switch to `-F -i -l`, whose substring alias hits and the `-I` asymmetry at :2625 would change results). Then:\n  - restrict the grep to corpus paths, i.e. exclude non-corpus paths by pathspec or by passing the allowed set. That is exact by construction, since those files are filtered out after the grep anyway;\n  - use `-l` for the same file set (count verified on 3 repos by the reviewer);\n  - keep content validation via the existing matcher.\n- **Edge to handle explicitly.** Oversize unreadable hits, e.g. brain `benchmarks/.../SNAPSHOT.json` at 17.6 MB, where `-m1` alone costs 30 s. textMatchesSearchQuery is monotone and line-local, so the result stays exact apart from those. Decide the behaviour, then test and disclose it. The `FilesContentRead` stat may rise; say so in the PR.\n\n## Done means\n- **Base vs new**, interleaved, under the lock:\n  - the exact `SearchRepository` query on entire-graph (base: 1 rep only, it takes about 6 min);\n  - `OpenRepository` on cli;\n  - the C3 query on entire-brain (pattern file `brain.c3.ere`; find the query text that triggers it via the review or `g2-measure.sh` block grep1/e2e1).\n- **Output identity:** JSON byte-compare after `g2-strip.py` on all three. Also cover a fixture with an oversize file.\n- **Tests:**\n  - a test pinning that non-corpus paths are never scanned, and that results are unchanged;\n  - the oversize case;\n  - each weakened to red and then restored.\n- **PR** open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-alias-grep`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4fdae5f9-149b-4260-a6d4-e2717719867f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMZv55BwUzFkzPrdFBAc","requestRef":"97f11b82-691e-4c2a-8711-823ff96b4fa9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a49e8dcb-faa2-4704-8bf5-f5621003eea2","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:53:40.289Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"a49e8dcb-faa2-4704-8bf5-f5621003eea2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZv5R3HgSQXP5eVQQNg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JTp7nLC5Gm7pFhgrtvjCA6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-2: pipeline window V2","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #2: widen the ordered per-file pipeline window (V2)\nRead row #2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Background.**\n- The main goroutine is blocked about 59% of cold-index wall time in chanrecv inside `runIndexedStreamingPipeline`. The ordered window admits 8 items, so one slow head file stalls the rest, and only about 1.6 of 8 workers stay busy.\n- The original local patch (window 128, buffer 2→4096, tokens taken unordered) is NOT shippable. It fails both existing tests: bound 63,487 vs 8,448, and join started 46-48 vs 8. It also has a hidden deadlock with a bounded buffer.\n\n**The reviewer built V2.** It keeps ordered admission, keeps buffer 2, and widens the window 16×.\n- Source and tests are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/g2-v2/`: `provider_parallel_stream.v2.go`, plus `eg-v2/` and `standalone/`. Raw numbers are in `timing/raw/g2/{v2-measure.txt,sha-check.txt}`.\n- Results: cli 11.5→8.5 s (−26%), brain 14.5→9.6 s (−33%), RSS ±5%.\n- It passes the original tests with `-race`, with the bound scaled to the window. Head-of-line blocking drops from 128 to 7, and 50 reps showed no deadlock.\n- Snapshot sha matches main on cli and brain.\n\n**Port V2 onto fresh main.** Requirements:\n- Run `entire graph impact` on `runIndexedStreamingPipeline` first. It also drives the warm-query pipeline at search.go:1514, which has 7 production callers, and those must not regress.\n- Keep the memory bound explicit and tested: the test's bound must scale with the window, not be deleted.\n- Make cancellation and error propagation correct, with a test that cancels mid-stream and checks no goroutine leak and no deadlock (run it many times, `-count=50 -race`, under the lock).\n- Choose the window constant deliberately (16× workers or fixed) and justify it in a code comment that matches the surrounding comment density.\n\n## Done means\n- **Cold index, base vs new**, interleaved, 3 reps, under the lock, on cli + entire-brain + entire-graph + entiredb clones in `timing/repos/`.\n- Snapshot sha256 equal on all four.\n- A warm query is not slower.\n- Tests weakened to red and then restored.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/pipeline-ordered-window`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-pipeline-window`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":257419,"output_tokens":4303,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":61},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4303,"cache_read_input_tokens":257419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JTp7nLC5Gm7pFhgrtvjCA6":{"description":"G3-2: pipeline window V2","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #2: widen the ordered per-file pipeline window (V2)\nRead row #2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Background.**\n- The main goroutine is blocked about 59% of cold-index wall time in chanrecv inside `runIndexedStreamingPipeline`. The ordered window admits 8 items, so one slow head file stalls the rest, and only about 1.6 of 8 workers stay busy.\n- The original local patch (window 128, buffer 2→4096, tokens taken unordered) is NOT shippable. It fails both existing tests: bound 63,487 vs 8,448, and join started 46-48 vs 8. It also has a hidden deadlock with a bounded buffer.\n\n**The reviewer built V2.** It keeps ordered admission, keeps buffer 2, and widens the window 16×.\n- Source and tests are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/g2-v2/`: `provider_parallel_stream.v2.go`, plus `eg-v2/` and `standalone/`. Raw numbers are in `timing/raw/g2/{v2-measure.txt,sha-check.txt}`.\n- Results: cli 11.5→8.5 s (−26%), brain 14.5→9.6 s (−33%), RSS ±5%.\n- It passes the original tests with `-race`, with the bound scaled to the window. Head-of-line blocking drops from 128 to 7, and 50 reps showed no deadlock.\n- Snapshot sha matches main on cli and brain.\n\n**Port V2 onto fresh main.** Requirements:\n- Run `entire graph impact` on `runIndexedStreamingPipeline` first. It also drives the warm-query pipeline at search.go:1514, which has 7 production callers, and those must not regress.\n- Keep the memory bound explicit and tested: the test's bound must scale with the window, not be deleted.\n- Make cancellation and error propagation correct, with a test that cancels mid-stream and checks no goroutine leak and no deadlock (run it many times, `-count=50 -race`, under the lock).\n- Choose the window constant deliberately (16× workers or fixed) and justify it in a code comment that matches the surrounding comment density.\n\n## Done means\n- **Cold index, base vs new**, interleaved, 3 reps, under the lock, on cli + entire-brain + entire-graph + entiredb clones in `timing/repos/`.\n- Snapshot sha256 equal on all four.\n- A warm query is not slower.\n- Tests weakened to red and then restored.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/pipeline-ordered-window`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-pipeline-window`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4fdae5f9-149b-4260-a6d4-e2717719867f","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgMZv55BwUzFkzPrdFBAc","requestRef":"97f11b82-691e-4c2a-8711-823ff96b4fa9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"26c0e038-0f3b-4ee2-a8fc-2c8952a3bea7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:53:49.714Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"26c0e038-0f3b-4ee2-a8fc-2c8952a3bea7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZv5R3HgSQXP5eVQQNg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MDgWcU8PkZgJv8o5eKMoRC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-Ba: partial-clone indexing","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph correctness fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item B-a (+N2): index partial clones (`blob:none` promisor remotes)\nRead rows B-a and N2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**The problem.** `entire graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head` fails with \"resolve committed HEAD for preindex: refuse Git subprocesses ... its Git config declares a promisor remote (a partial clone) ... indexing falls back to a filesystem walk to stay offline\". The fallback it promises is never reached. The same happens on devenv/cli, which has the promisor remote `https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git` with `blob:none` (not origin). This blocks graph `--head` AND Entire Brain's Graph-owned store on both repos.\n\n**What the reviewer established:**\n- **Short-circuit:** search_cache.go:604-607 (preindex) → resolveCommittedHEAD provider.go:1984 → refusal → index.go:124-129 returns.\n- **The fallback exists only on query paths:** prepareSource E_NO_GIT_HEAD at provider.go:1946, and the uncached build at search_cache.go:296-299. So **every query on a promisor repo rebuilds uncached (N2).**\n- **The message text** at provider.go:18866-18870 is false for `index`.\n- **The guard's rationale** is at git.go:2654-2665: `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` takes effect from git 2.45; the floor is 2.36. Every subprocess already sets `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`. This machine has git 2.54.0.\n\n**Safe fix the reviewer proposes:**\n- admit promisor repos when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, since lazy fetch is provably disabled there;\n- keep the refusal below 2.45, and fix the message text so it is true for every caller.\n\n**This relaxes a security guard: no-network is the invariant.** Before you change anything:\n- run `entire brain recall` on the promisor guard's history;\n- read the ADR or comments that introduced it;\n- run `entire graph impact` on the guard function.\n\nThe PR must argue why offline is still guaranteed.\n\n## Done means\nTests, each weakened to red and restored:\n- (a) A local `blob:none` clone whose remote is deleted or unreachable indexes `--head` fully offline. Simulate it locally with `git clone --filter=blob:none file://...`, then remove or rename the source.\n- (b) A missing blob produces an error, not a fetch: no network attempt, which you assert via `GIT_TRACE` or an unreachable remote URL.\n- (c) An injected git version < 2.45 still refuses, with corrected text.\n- (d) A query on a promisor repo now uses the cache: the second query is a cache hit.\n\nPlus:\n- **Live check:** `bin/new graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head --cache-dir <fresh>` succeeds. Pipe the output through `jq` to print only counts and warnings, because it is huge. Do the same for `/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli` with a fresh cache dir, under the lock. Those are main checkouts: read-only use only.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `fix/index-partial-clones`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-partial-clone`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_read_input_tokens":257419,"output_tokens":4303,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":61},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4303,"cache_read_input_tokens":257419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2384},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MDgWcU8PkZgJv8o5eKMoRC":{"description":"G3-Ba: partial-clone indexing","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph correctness fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item B-a (+N2): index partial clones (`blob:none` promisor remotes)\nRead rows B-a and N2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**The problem.** `entire graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head` fails with \"resolve committed HEAD for preindex: refuse Git subprocesses ... its Git config declares a promisor remote (a partial clone) ... indexing falls back to a filesystem walk to stay offline\". The fallback it promises is never reached. The same happens on devenv/cli, which has the promisor remote `https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git` with `blob:none` (not origin). This blocks graph `--head` AND Entire Brain's Graph-owned store on both repos.\n\n**What the reviewer established:**\n- **Short-circuit:** search_cache.go:604-607 (preindex) → resolveCommittedHEAD provider.go:1984 → refusal → index.go:124-129 returns.\n- **The fallback exists only on query paths:** prepareSource E_NO_GIT_HEAD at provider.go:1946, and the uncached build at search_cache.go:296-299. So **every query on a promisor repo rebuilds uncached (N2).**\n- **The message text** at provider.go:18866-18870 is false for `index`.\n- **The guard's rationale** is at git.go:2654-2665: `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` takes effect from git 2.45; the floor is 2.36. Every subprocess already sets `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`. This machine has git 2.54.0.\n\n**Safe fix the reviewer proposes:**\n- admit promisor repos when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, since lazy fetch is provably disabled there;\n- keep the refusal below 2.45, and fix the message text so it is true for every caller.\n\n**This relaxes a security guard: no-network is the invariant.** Before you change anything:\n- run `entire brain recall` on the promisor guard's history;\n- read the ADR or comments that introduced it;\n- run `entire graph impact` on the guard function.\n\nThe PR must argue why offline is still guaranteed.\n\n## Done means\nTests, each weakened to red and restored:\n- (a) A local `blob:none` clone whose remote is deleted or unreachable indexes `--head` fully offline. Simulate it locally with `git clone --filter=blob:none file://...`, then remove or rename the source.\n- (b) A missing blob produces an error, not a fetch: no network attempt, which you assert via `GIT_TRACE` or an unreachable remote URL.\n- (c) An injected git version < 2.45 still refuses, with corrected text.\n- (d) A query on a promisor repo now uses the cache: the second query is a cache hit.\n\nPlus:\n- **Live check:** `bin/new graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head --cache-dir <fresh>` succeeds. Pipe the output through `jq` to print only counts and warnings, because it is huge. Do the same for `/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli` with a fresh cache dir, under the lock. Those are main checkouts: read-only use only.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `fix/index-partial-clones`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-partial-clone`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4fdae5f9-149b-4260-a6d4-e2717719867f","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgMZv55BwUzFkzPrdFBAc","requestRef":"97f11b82-691e-4c2a-8711-823ff96b4fa9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c20f41e6-5809-4c46-88a4-0a4abab2cc76","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:54:01.985Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"c311d250-1aaa-4b45-a000-9cfed7632ce3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2d0bb0ac-82fc-4576-a832-23942242d9f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014rDXmhLsLSB9EsVBcE9Vog","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"acc95ed2-0973-419f-90ad-fd9ba23306ec","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:54:02.528Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md","oldString":"- Build two binaries: `go build -o /tmp-free path` into your worktree's `bin/`. One from `origin/main` (base), one from your branch.","newString":"- Build two binaries into your worktree's `bin/` (not `/tmp`, which other agents share): `bin/base` from `origin/main` and `bin/new` from your branch.","originalFile":"# G3 fix protocol (entire-graph speed and correctness fixes)\n\nEvery G3 fix agent follows this file. The item-specific brief comes in the agent's prompt.\n\n## Inputs\n- Fix list: `GRAPH-SPEEDUPS.md`. Review, which is authoritative where it disagrees: `GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`.\n- Step maps: `PROCESS-MAP.md`, `stepmaps/`. Reviewer tools: `g2-measure.sh`, `g2-strip.py`, `g2-patterns/`, `g2-v2/`, `raw/g2/`.\n- All of these live in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/`.\n\n## Workspace\n- One fresh worktree per fix, off `origin/main`:\n  `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin main && git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph worktree add -b <branch> /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-<short-name> origin/main`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph` is a main checkout. Read from it; never edit, commit, or switch branches there.\n- No `git stash`: one stash is shared across all worktrees, and parallel agents collide.\n- Commit with the repo's configured identity. **Never** pass `-c user.email=...` or `--author`.\n- Conventional commit subject (`perf(sem): ...`, `fix(cli): ...`). **No AI or Claude attribution lines** in commits or PR bodies. No references to people or conversations.\n\n## Tools: graph and brain first\n1. Preflight once:\n   - `entire graph version --json`, `entire graph capabilities --json`\n   - `entire brain version`, `entire brain capabilities --json`\n2. Before editing any exported or shared symbol, run `entire graph impact --repo <worktree> --head --symbol <Name>` and cite the result. Use `def` and `neighbors --direction in` for callers. grep only supplements; it never replaces these.\n3. For why code exists or prior decisions, run `entire brain recall \"<question>\" --json` from `/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph`. An empty result is not proof.\n\n## CPU, measuring and coordination\n- Other agents run in parallel on this machine. **Any timing run, cold index, or test run longer than about a minute must hold the measure lock:**\n  `flock /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/measure.lock -c '<command>'`\n  Keep each locked block short (minutes, not an hour) so the others are not starved.\n- Before a timing block, check two things:\n  - `uptime`: record load1. Don't measure above about 8.\n  - `/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json`: any row with `\"lane\": \"brain\"`, `\"status\": \"doing\"` and a title starting `measuring:` means wait until it clears.\n- Focused tests: `env -u FORCE_COLOR GOMAXPROCS=4 go test ./<pkg> -run '<Regex>' -count=1`. The shell sets FORCE_COLOR=3, which breaks colour-assert tests on correct code.\n- **No full local suites.** CI runs them. Exception: the package you changed may be run whole, under the lock, with `-p 1`.\n- Never `--daemon`, `entire brain setup` or `entire brain refresh`. Never touch `~/.local/share/entire`.\n\n## Before/after timing (speed fixes)\n- Build two binaries: `go build -o /tmp-free path` into your worktree's `bin/`. One from `origin/main` (base), one from your branch.\n- Interleave base/new runs. Use a separate `--cache-dir` per binary, and a fresh one per cold run. 3 reps, report the median. Use the same repos as the study (clones under `timing/repos/`, or `/Users/suhaan/devenv/{entire-graph,entire-brain}`).\n- **Output identity:** compare base vs new JSON outputs byte-for-byte after `g2-strip.py` (it strips timing fields), or the snapshot sha256. If the output is meant to change, say exactly how and test it.\n- The index cache is keyed by tree, not binary, so base and new must never share a cache dir.\n\n## Tests: mutation-proven\n- Add or adjust a test that pins the new behaviour.\n- **Verified by weakening:** temporarily break the guard or fix, show the test goes red (paste the failing line), then restore it and verify the restore by `git diff`.\n- A test that cannot go red is not a test.\n- Watch the Windows traps: filepath separators, CRLF checkouts, and platform branches that nothing executes.\n\n## PR\n- `git push -u origin <branch>`, then `gh pr create --repo entireio/entire-graph --base main`.\n- Body sections:\n  - **Summary:** what and why.\n  - **Measurements:** a base vs new table with medians, reps, load1, repos, and the identity check.\n  - **Test plan:** the tests, and what you weakened to prove them.\n- Do NOT merge, approve, request reviewers, or create an Entire trail by hand.\n- Watch CI with `gh pr checks <n> --repo entireio/entire-graph`. Fix real failures.\n  - A running check has conclusion `\"\"`. It has not failed.\n  - `test (macos-latest)` near 20 minutes is usually the suite timeout, not your diff. Check the log before changing code.\n- If an Entire Gates agent review posts findings on the trail, address the real ones: fix the code, or explain in a PR comment.\n\n## Report (caveman-ultra, ≤ 40 lines)\nInclude:\n- the PR number and branch;\n- the base → new medians with load;\n- the identity check result;\n- the tests and the weakening proof;\n- CI state, enumerated as green, failed, or running;\n- anything you could not finish, and why.\n\nUse RTK for shell (auto-rewritten; `rtk proxy <cmd>` for raw).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":34,"oldLines":7,"newStart":34,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - Never `--daemon`, `entire brain setup` or `entire brain refresh`. Never touch `~/.local/share/entire`."," "," ## Before/after timing (speed fixes)","-- Build two binaries: `go build -o /tmp-free path` into your worktree's `bin/`. One from `origin/main` (base), one from your branch.","+- Build two binaries into your worktree's `bin/` (not `/tmp`, which other agents share): `bin/base` from `origin/main` and `bin/new` from your branch."," - Interleave base/new runs. Use a separate `--cache-dir` per binary, and a fresh one per cold run. 3 reps, report the median. Use the same repos as the study (clones under `timing/repos/`, or `/Users/suhaan/devenv/{entire-graph,entire-brain}`)."," - **Output identity:** compare base vs new JSON outputs byte-for-byte after `g2-strip.py` (it strips timing fields), or the snapshot sha256. If the output is meant to change, say exactly how and test it."," - The index cache is keyed by tree, not binary, so base and new must never share a cache dir."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4fdae5f9-149b-4260-a6d4-e2717719867f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c311d250-1aaa-4b45-a000-9cfed7632ce3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
