{"parentUuid":"26c0e038-0f3b-4ee2-a8fc-2c8952a3bea7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2d0bb0ac-82fc-4576-a832-23942242d9f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JTp7nLC5Gm7pFhgrtvjCA6","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: aed163711fd7846a7 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'aed163711fd7846a7', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/aed163711fd7846a7.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"79420196-7119-48d6-8b69-28c6c4ad5794","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:54:20.217Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"aed163711fd7846a7","description":"G3-2: pipeline window V2","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #2: widen the ordered per-file pipeline window (V2)\nRead row #2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Background.**\n- The main goroutine is blocked about 59% of cold-index wall time in chanrecv inside `runIndexedStreamingPipeline`. The ordered window admits 8 items, so one slow head file stalls the rest, and only about 1.6 of 8 workers stay busy.\n- The original local patch (window 128, buffer 2→4096, tokens taken unordered) is NOT shippable. It fails both existing tests: bound 63,487 vs 8,448, and join started 46-48 vs 8. It also has a hidden deadlock with a bounded buffer.\n\n**The reviewer built V2.** It keeps ordered admission, keeps buffer 2, and widens the window 16×.\n- Source and tests are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/g2-v2/`: `provider_parallel_stream.v2.go`, plus `eg-v2/` and `standalone/`. Raw numbers are in `timing/raw/g2/{v2-measure.txt,sha-check.txt}`.\n- Results: cli 11.5→8.5 s (−26%), brain 14.5→9.6 s (−33%), RSS ±5%.\n- It passes the original tests with `-race`, with the bound scaled to the window. Head-of-line blocking drops from 128 to 7, and 50 reps showed no deadlock.\n- Snapshot sha matches main on cli and brain.\n\n**Port V2 onto fresh main.** Requirements:\n- Run `entire graph impact` on `runIndexedStreamingPipeline` first. It also drives the warm-query pipeline at search.go:1514, which has 7 production callers, and those must not regress.\n- Keep the memory bound explicit and tested: the test's bound must scale with the window, not be deleted.\n- Make cancellation and error propagation correct, with a test that cancels mid-stream and checks no goroutine leak and no deadlock (run it many times, `-count=50 -race`, under the lock).\n- Choose the window constant deliberately (16× workers or fixed) and justify it in a code comment that matches the surrounding comment density.\n\n## Done means\n- **Cold index, base vs new**, interleaved, 3 reps, under the lock, on cli + entire-brain + entire-graph + entiredb clones in `timing/repos/`.\n- Snapshot sha256 equal on all four.\n- A warm query is not slower.\n- Tests weakened to red and then restored.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/pipeline-ordered-window`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-pipeline-window`.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/aed163711fd7846a7.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4fdae5f9-149b-4260-a6d4-e2717719867f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"26c0e038-0f3b-4ee2-a8fc-2c8952a3bea7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"a49e8dcb-faa2-4704-8bf5-f5621003eea2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2d0bb0ac-82fc-4576-a832-23942242d9f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MLwaCyFESbNWuEHF6fRUpT","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: ab445bd129113f33b (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'ab445bd129113f33b', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/ab445bd129113f33b.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"8fe76411-a73b-4d51-ae54-370ee1eafde6","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:54:21.627Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"ab445bd129113f33b","description":"G3-1: alias git grep fix","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #1 (+N1): the alias `git grep` preselect\nRead rows #1, C3 and N1 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first. That review overrides the original list. Summary of what it established:\n- **Route.** search.go:2577-2623, the alias route. It fires when any query term has an abbreviation alias (repository→repo, synchronous→sync). It is not about bare identifiers, and it runs only on a cache HIT. It calls git.go:649-700: `git grep -E -m 1 -f - <commit>` over the whole commit, then filters to `allowed[]` at :2607.\n- **Cost.** About 97% of the 355 s on entire-graph is scanning blobs the graph already excludes from its corpus: the .graphignored tree-sitter `parser.c`/`scanner.c`, 226 MB in total, with one 9.7 MB parser.c taking 24.5 s.\n  - cli: 7.80 s with `-m 1` vs 0.93 s with `-l`.\n  - entire-brain (C3): 45.10 s vs 2.51 s.\n  - Captured patterns are in `timing/g2-patterns/`.\n- **Fix the reviewer endorses:** keep the SAME ERE (do NOT switch to `-F -i -l`, whose substring alias hits and the `-I` asymmetry at :2625 would change results). Then:\n  - restrict the grep to corpus paths, i.e. exclude non-corpus paths by pathspec or by passing the allowed set. That is exact by construction, since those files are filtered out after the grep anyway;\n  - use `-l` for the same file set (count verified on 3 repos by the reviewer);\n  - keep content validation via the existing matcher.\n- **Edge to handle explicitly.** Oversize unreadable hits, e.g. brain `benchmarks/.../SNAPSHOT.json` at 17.6 MB, where `-m1` alone costs 30 s. textMatchesSearchQuery is monotone and line-local, so the result stays exact apart from those. Decide the behaviour, then test and disclose it. The `FilesContentRead` stat may rise; say so in the PR.\n\n## Done means\n- **Base vs new**, interleaved, under the lock:\n  - the exact `SearchRepository` query on entire-graph (base: 1 rep only, it takes about 6 min);\n  - `OpenRepository` on cli;\n  - the C3 query on entire-brain (pattern file `brain.c3.ere`; find the query text that triggers it via the review or `g2-measure.sh` block grep1/e2e1).\n- **Output identity:** JSON byte-compare after `g2-strip.py` on all three. Also cover a fixture with an oversize file.\n- **Tests:**\n  - a test pinning that non-corpus paths are never scanned, and that results are unchanged;\n  - the oversize case;\n  - each weakened to red and then restored.\n- **PR** open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-alias-grep`.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/ab445bd129113f33b.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4fdae5f9-149b-4260-a6d4-e2717719867f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a49e8dcb-faa2-4704-8bf5-f5621003eea2","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"c20f41e6-5809-4c46-88a4-0a4abab2cc76","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2d0bb0ac-82fc-4576-a832-23942242d9f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MDgWcU8PkZgJv8o5eKMoRC","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: aead2ee30e4f0404a (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'aead2ee30e4f0404a', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/aead2ee30e4f0404a.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"8ca01a74-18d6-4469-924e-d50402fea433","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:54:23.027Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","description":"G3-Ba: partial-clone indexing","resolvedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph correctness fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item B-a (+N2): index partial clones (`blob:none` promisor remotes)\nRead rows B-a and N2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**The problem.** `entire graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head` fails with \"resolve committed HEAD for preindex: refuse Git subprocesses ... its Git config declares a promisor remote (a partial clone) ... indexing falls back to a filesystem walk to stay offline\". The fallback it promises is never reached. The same happens on devenv/cli, which has the promisor remote `https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git` with `blob:none` (not origin). This blocks graph `--head` AND Entire Brain's Graph-owned store on both repos.\n\n**What the reviewer established:**\n- **Short-circuit:** search_cache.go:604-607 (preindex) → resolveCommittedHEAD provider.go:1984 → refusal → index.go:124-129 returns.\n- **The fallback exists only on query paths:** prepareSource E_NO_GIT_HEAD at provider.go:1946, and the uncached build at search_cache.go:296-299. So **every query on a promisor repo rebuilds uncached (N2).**\n- **The message text** at provider.go:18866-18870 is false for `index`.\n- **The guard's rationale** is at git.go:2654-2665: `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` takes effect from git 2.45; the floor is 2.36. Every subprocess already sets `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`. This machine has git 2.54.0.\n\n**Safe fix the reviewer proposes:**\n- admit promisor repos when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, since lazy fetch is provably disabled there;\n- keep the refusal below 2.45, and fix the message text so it is true for every caller.\n\n**This relaxes a security guard: no-network is the invariant.** Before you change anything:\n- run `entire brain recall` on the promisor guard's history;\n- read the ADR or comments that introduced it;\n- run `entire graph impact` on the guard function.\n\nThe PR must argue why offline is still guaranteed.\n\n## Done means\nTests, each weakened to red and restored:\n- (a) A local `blob:none` clone whose remote is deleted or unreachable indexes `--head` fully offline. Simulate it locally with `git clone --filter=blob:none file://...`, then remove or rename the source.\n- (b) A missing blob produces an error, not a fetch: no network attempt, which you assert via `GIT_TRACE` or an unreachable remote URL.\n- (c) An injected git version < 2.45 still refuses, with corrected text.\n- (d) A query on a promisor repo now uses the cache: the second query is a cache hit.\n\nPlus:\n- **Live check:** `bin/new graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head --cache-dir <fresh>` succeeds. Pipe the output through `jq` to print only counts and warnings, because it is huge. Do the same for `/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli` with a fresh cache dir, under the lock. Those are main checkouts: read-only use only.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `fix/index-partial-clones`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-partial-clone`.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/aead2ee30e4f0404a.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"4fdae5f9-149b-4260-a6d4-e2717719867f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c20f41e6-5809-4c46-88a4-0a4abab2cc76","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"567cc6f1e01a789a1bb577413f7f3c7aecff90a04a8ee3de9a5b84a32c899604","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014rDXmhLsLSB9EsVBcE9Vog","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md","old_string":"- Build two binaries: `go build -o /tmp-free path` into your worktree's `bin/`. One from `origin/main` (base), one from your branch.","new_string":"- Build two binaries into your worktree's `bin/` (not `/tmp`, which other agents share): `bin/base` from `origin/main` and `bin/new` from your branch."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MLwaCyFESbNWuEHF6fRUpT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-1: alias git grep fix","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #1 (+N1): the alias `git grep` preselect\nRead rows #1, C3 and N1 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first. That review overrides the original list. Summary of what it established:\n- **Route.** search.go:2577-2623, the alias route. It fires when any query term has an abbreviation alias (repository→repo, synchronous→sync). It is not about bare identifiers, and it runs only on a cache HIT. It calls git.go:649-700: `git grep -E -m 1 -f - <commit>` over the whole commit, then filters to `allowed[]` at :2607.\n- **Cost.** About 97% of the 355 s on entire-graph is scanning blobs the graph already excludes from its corpus: the .graphignored tree-sitter `parser.c`/`scanner.c`, 226 MB in total, with one 9.7 MB parser.c taking 24.5 s.\n  - cli: 7.80 s with `-m 1` vs 0.93 s with `-l`.\n  - entire-brain (C3): 45.10 s vs 2.51 s.\n  - Captured patterns are in `timing/g2-patterns/`.\n- **Fix the reviewer endorses:** keep the SAME ERE (do NOT switch to `-F -i -l`, whose substring alias hits and the `-I` asymmetry at :2625 would change results). Then:\n  - restrict the grep to corpus paths, i.e. exclude non-corpus paths by pathspec or by passing the allowed set. That is exact by construction, since those files are filtered out after the grep anyway;\n  - use `-l` for the same file set (count verified on 3 repos by the reviewer);\n  - keep content validation via the existing matcher.\n- **Edge to handle explicitly.** Oversize unreadable hits, e.g. brain `benchmarks/.../SNAPSHOT.json` at 17.6 MB, where `-m1` alone costs 30 s. textMatchesSearchQuery is monotone and line-local, so the result stays exact apart from those. Decide the behaviour, then test and disclose it. The `FilesContentRead` stat may rise; say so in the PR.\n\n## Done means\n- **Base vs new**, interleaved, under the lock:\n  - the exact `SearchRepository` query on entire-graph (base: 1 rep only, it takes about 6 min);\n  - `OpenRepository` on cli;\n  - the C3 query on entire-brain (pattern file `brain.c3.ere`; find the query text that triggers it via the review or `g2-measure.sh` block grep1/e2e1).\n- **Output identity:** JSON byte-compare after `g2-strip.py` on all three. Also cover a fixture with an oversize file.\n- **Tests:**\n  - a test pinning that non-corpus paths are never scanned, and that results are unchanged;\n  - the oversize case;\n  - each weakened to red and then restored.\n- **PR** open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-alias-grep`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JTp7nLC5Gm7pFhgrtvjCA6","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-2: pipeline window V2","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #2: widen the ordered per-file pipeline window (V2)\nRead row #2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Background.**\n- The main goroutine is blocked about 59% of cold-index wall time in chanrecv inside `runIndexedStreamingPipeline`. The ordered window admits 8 items, so one slow head file stalls the rest, and only about 1.6 of 8 workers stay busy.\n- The original local patch (window 128, buffer 2→4096, tokens taken unordered) is NOT shippable. It fails both existing tests: bound 63,487 vs 8,448, and join started 46-48 vs 8. It also has a hidden deadlock with a bounded buffer.\n\n**The reviewer built V2.** It keeps ordered admission, keeps buffer 2, and widens the window 16×.\n- Source and tests are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/g2-v2/`: `provider_parallel_stream.v2.go`, plus `eg-v2/` and `standalone/`. Raw numbers are in `timing/raw/g2/{v2-measure.txt,sha-check.txt}`.\n- Results: cli 11.5→8.5 s (−26%), brain 14.5→9.6 s (−33%), RSS ±5%.\n- It passes the original tests with `-race`, with the bound scaled to the window. Head-of-line blocking drops from 128 to 7, and 50 reps showed no deadlock.\n- Snapshot sha matches main on cli and brain.\n\n**Port V2 onto fresh main.** Requirements:\n- Run `entire graph impact` on `runIndexedStreamingPipeline` first. It also drives the warm-query pipeline at search.go:1514, which has 7 production callers, and those must not regress.\n- Keep the memory bound explicit and tested: the test's bound must scale with the window, not be deleted.\n- Make cancellation and error propagation correct, with a test that cancels mid-stream and checks no goroutine leak and no deadlock (run it many times, `-count=50 -race`, under the lock).\n- Choose the window constant deliberately (16× workers or fixed) and justify it in a code comment that matches the surrounding comment density.\n\n## Done means\n- **Cold index, base vs new**, interleaved, 3 reps, under the lock, on cli + entire-brain + entire-graph + entiredb clones in `timing/repos/`.\n- Snapshot sha256 equal on all four.\n- A warm query is not slower.\n- Tests weakened to red and then restored.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `perf/pipeline-ordered-window`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-pipeline-window`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MDgWcU8PkZgJv8o5eKMoRC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-Ba: partial-clone indexing","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph correctness fix, end to end, as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, measure lock, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item B-a (+N2): index partial clones (`blob:none` promisor remotes)\nRead rows B-a and N2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**The problem.** `entire graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head` fails with \"resolve committed HEAD for preindex: refuse Git subprocesses ... its Git config declares a promisor remote (a partial clone) ... indexing falls back to a filesystem walk to stay offline\". The fallback it promises is never reached. The same happens on devenv/cli, which has the promisor remote `https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git` with `blob:none` (not origin). This blocks graph `--head` AND Entire Brain's Graph-owned store on both repos.\n\n**What the reviewer established:**\n- **Short-circuit:** search_cache.go:604-607 (preindex) → resolveCommittedHEAD provider.go:1984 → refusal → index.go:124-129 returns.\n- **The fallback exists only on query paths:** prepareSource E_NO_GIT_HEAD at provider.go:1946, and the uncached build at search_cache.go:296-299. So **every query on a promisor repo rebuilds uncached (N2).**\n- **The message text** at provider.go:18866-18870 is false for `index`.\n- **The guard's rationale** is at git.go:2654-2665: `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` takes effect from git 2.45; the floor is 2.36. Every subprocess already sets `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`. This machine has git 2.54.0.\n\n**Safe fix the reviewer proposes:**\n- admit promisor repos when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, since lazy fetch is provably disabled there;\n- keep the refusal below 2.45, and fix the message text so it is true for every caller.\n\n**This relaxes a security guard: no-network is the invariant.** Before you change anything:\n- run `entire brain recall` on the promisor guard's history;\n- read the ADR or comments that introduced it;\n- run `entire graph impact` on the guard function.\n\nThe PR must argue why offline is still guaranteed.\n\n## Done means\nTests, each weakened to red and restored:\n- (a) A local `blob:none` clone whose remote is deleted or unreachable indexes `--head` fully offline. Simulate it locally with `git clone --filter=blob:none file://...`, then remove or rename the source.\n- (b) A missing blob produces an error, not a fetch: no network attempt, which you assert via `GIT_TRACE` or an unreachable remote URL.\n- (c) An injected git version < 2.45 still refuses, with corrected text.\n- (d) A query on a promisor repo now uses the cache: the second query is a cache hit.\n\nPlus:\n- **Live check:** `bin/new graph index --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entiredb --head --cache-dir <fresh>` succeeds. Pipe the output through `jq` to print only counts and warnings, because it is huge. Do the same for `/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli` with a fresh cache dir, under the lock. Those are main checkouts: read-only use only.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch: `fix/index-partial-clones`. Worktree: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-partial-clone`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
