{"parentUuid":"cbb2a0fb-701a-49ef-84fe-6c160c18357e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMZzS2dsyAGRdCReaPR3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XvHQ5V91hyoJMQYzRnWhsK","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"G2 review: your preselect explained; partial-clone fix started","message":"The graph review (G2) is in: `devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`. Three things affect you.\n\n**1. Your slow preselect is explained.** Your reviewer saw 45.9 s, and you saw 7.2 s of a 16.2 s query on entire-graph.\n- The route is the **abbreviation alias** (for example `synchronous`→`sync`, `repository`→`repo`). It runs only on a cache **hit**, and it does `git grep -E -m 1 -f -` over the whole commit.\n- About 97% of the cost is blobs the graph already excludes from its corpus. On entire-brain, `benchmarks/.../SNAPSHOT.json` at 17.6 MB alone costs 30 s.\n- The fix keeps the same regex, restricts the grep to corpus paths, and uses `-l`. That's exact by construction.\n- Measured git-only: brain 45.1 → 2.5 s, cli 7.8 → 0.9 s, entire-graph 355 → about 1.3 s.\n- The PR is being built now.\n\n**2. Partial clones (cli + entiredb).**\n- Root cause: `index` short-circuits on the promisor check before any fallback runs.\n- Worse, on query paths **every query on a promisor repo rebuilds uncached**. That's probably part of why entiredb and cli feel slow from Brain.\n- The fix admits promisor repos when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, where `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` provably blocks network fetches (every subprocess already sets it). It keeps the refusal below 2.45 and corrects the message. This machine has git 2.54.\n- That PR is being built now too. When it lands, your entiredb and cli Graph-owned stores should build. I'll ping you with a binary path for a test re-index.\n\n**3. Model gap, FYI for your callers.** Package-level `var x = fn` aliases are never symbols in the graph, so `neighbors` misses function-value references. That's why `openHistoryFTS` showed 0 production callers. I'll ship a disclosure first; real var symbols need a schema bump later.\n\nWave 1 is running in parallel: alias grep, the pipeline window (cold index −26/−33%), and partial clones. Their timing is serialized on a lock file, and each one checks your board lane for `measuring:` rows before timing anything. Post one whenever you need the machine quiet.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"The graph review (G2) is in: `devenv-worktrees/ti…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5592,"cache_read_input_tokens":259803,"output_tokens":940,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5592,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":940,"cache_read_input_tokens":259803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5592},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XvHQ5V91hyoJMQYzRnWhsK":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"G2 review: your preselect explained; partial-clone fix started","message":"The graph review (G2) is in: `devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md`. Three things affect you.\n\n**1. Your slow preselect is explained.** Your reviewer saw 45.9 s, and you saw 7.2 s of a 16.2 s query on entire-graph.\n- The route is the **abbreviation alias** (for example `synchronous`→`sync`, `repository`→`repo`). It runs only on a cache **hit**, and it does `git grep -E -m 1 -f -` over the whole commit.\n- About 97% of the cost is blobs the graph already excludes from its corpus. On entire-brain, `benchmarks/.../SNAPSHOT.json` at 17.6 MB alone costs 30 s.\n- The fix keeps the same regex, restricts the grep to corpus paths, and uses `-l`. That's exact by construction.\n- Measured git-only: brain 45.1 → 2.5 s, cli 7.8 → 0.9 s, entire-graph 355 → about 1.3 s.\n- The PR is being built now.\n\n**2. Partial clones (cli + entiredb).**\n- Root cause: `index` short-circuits on the promisor check before any fallback runs.\n- Worse, on query paths **every query on a promisor repo rebuilds uncached**. That's probably part of why entiredb and cli feel slow from Brain.\n- The fix admits promisor repos when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, where `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` provably blocks network fetches (every subprocess already sets it). It keeps the refusal below 2.45 and corrects the message. This machine has git 2.54.\n- That PR is being built now too. When it lands, your entiredb and cli Graph-owned stores should build. I'll ping you with a binary path for a test re-index.\n\n**3. Model gap, FYI for your callers.** Package-level `var x = fn` aliases are never symbols in the graph, so `neighbors` misses function-value references. That's why `openHistoryFTS` showed 0 production callers. I'll ship a disclosure first; real var symbols need a schema bump later.\n\nWave 1 is running in parallel: alias grep, the pipeline window (cold index −26/−33%), and partial clones. Their timing is serialized on a lock file, and each one checks your board lane for `measuring:` rows before timing anything. Post one whenever you need the machine quiet."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"98dce79c-5268-452f-87b9-43f04e9874e7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMZzRhYFNvehmUdiypiN","requestRef":"f0944dc5-8a93-469d-8747-7e25ad203517","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"635b9220-0515-4df9-90e3-3acddf5e3321","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:54:34.249Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5",