{"parentUuid":"8aa80c8d-e6c9-4916-a318-eff4e49a7b93","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMa7GowieHSAfFFYqGqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Brain session's two points on the partial-clone fix are right: prove the no-fetch setting by removing it, and enumerate every place git gets launched. Forwarding both to that agent as requirements:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_input_tokens":269066,"output_tokens":1588,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1588,"cache_read_input_tokens":269066,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"b4752994-68f2-41e7-b4ff-9fdd9f1cb36b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMa7GT76ZZ8bLNbsipBu","requestRef":"af932869-6829-4e2b-a29b-c59c32eb5a2d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"551b636c-9077-4f2b-a9df-069e18f704e7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:56:00.179Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"551b636c-9077-4f2b-a9df-069e18f704e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMa7GowieHSAfFFYqGqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RdLsSJoZZPDGyJ2BK46GN5","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"Two added requirements for B-a safety proof","message":"Two added requirements for B-a, both mandatory before you open the PR. The fix's whole safety argument rests on \"every git subprocess already sets GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1\", and that kind of claim tends to be true for the paths someone enumerated and false for the one they missed.\n\n1. **Prove the env var is load-bearing by weakening it.**\n   - Set up a promisor (`blob:none`) clone whose remote IS reachable: a local `file://` source repo that still exists, with a blob deliberately missing from the clone.\n   - Index it with `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` removed from the subprocess environment, and show a lazy fetch IS attempted. Use `GIT_TRACE=1` / `GIT_TRACE_PACKET`, or watch the source repo's objects get read. Then restore it and show no fetch happens and the missing blob errors cleanly.\n   - If removing it changes nothing, the env var is not what protects us. Stop, and report what does.\n   - Put this in a test if feasible. At minimum, paste the evidence in the PR.\n\n2. **Enumerate every git subprocess site; don't trust \"already sets it\".**\n   - Find every place the code launches git: `exec.Command*`, any wrapper, `cat-file --batch-command`, `grep`, `log`, `rev-parse`, `ls-tree`, and anything that builds its own `cmd.Env`.\n   - Use `entire graph neighbors --direction in` on the wrapper(s), plus a supplementary `grep -rn 'exec.Command' --include=*.go` for anything that bypasses the wrapper.\n   - If the env is set per call site today, move it to the single place the environment is constructed, if that is a small change. Either way, add a test asserting that EVERY git invocation carries `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`. For example, a fake `git` first on PATH that records its env and fails if either is missing, run across index + query + snapshot on a fixture repo.\n   - Weaken that test too: drop the var at one site and show it goes red.\n\nList the sites you found in the PR body.","type":"message","recipient":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Two added requirements for B-a, both mandatory be…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_input_tokens":269066,"output_tokens":1588,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1588,"cache_read_input_tokens":269066,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RdLsSJoZZPDGyJ2BK46GN5":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"Two added requirements for B-a safety proof","message":"Two added requirements for B-a, both mandatory before you open the PR. The fix's whole safety argument rests on \"every git subprocess already sets GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1\", and that kind of claim tends to be true for the paths someone enumerated and false for the one they missed.\n\n1. **Prove the env var is load-bearing by weakening it.**\n   - Set up a promisor (`blob:none`) clone whose remote IS reachable: a local `file://` source repo that still exists, with a blob deliberately missing from the clone.\n   - Index it with `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` removed from the subprocess environment, and show a lazy fetch IS attempted. Use `GIT_TRACE=1` / `GIT_TRACE_PACKET`, or watch the source repo's objects get read. Then restore it and show no fetch happens and the missing blob errors cleanly.\n   - If removing it changes nothing, the env var is not what protects us. Stop, and report what does.\n   - Put this in a test if feasible. At minimum, paste the evidence in the PR.\n\n2. **Enumerate every git subprocess site; don't trust \"already sets it\".**\n   - Find every place the code launches git: `exec.Command*`, any wrapper, `cat-file --batch-command`, `grep`, `log`, `rev-parse`, `ls-tree`, and anything that builds its own `cmd.Env`.\n   - Use `entire graph neighbors --direction in` on the wrapper(s), plus a supplementary `grep -rn 'exec.Command' --include=*.go` for anything that bypasses the wrapper.\n   - If the env is set per call site today, move it to the single place the environment is constructed, if that is a small change. Either way, add a test asserting that EVERY git invocation carries `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` and `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=`. For example, a fake `git` first on PATH that records its env and fails if either is missing, run across index + query + snapshot on a fixture repo.\n   - Weaken that test too: drop the var at one site and show it goes red.\n\nList the sites you found in the PR body."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b4752994-68f2-41e7-b4ff-9fdd9f1cb36b","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMa7GT76ZZ8bLNbsipBu","requestRef":"af932869-6829-4e2b-a29b-c59c32eb5a2d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a81611cf-f3e7-4276-83c7-0c0eb3c2dcda","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:56:08.349Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"a81611cf-f3e7-4276-83c7-0c0eb3c2dcda","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMa7GowieHSAfFFYqGqV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LTinVvRSkuE1RcRkEXhmtt","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Promisor proof requirements forwarded; ping on binary","message":"Both of your promisor points are now hard requirements on the B-a agent, before it opens the PR:\n- **Weakening:** a `blob:none` clone with a reachable `file://` remote and a missing blob. Remove `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` and show a fetch IS attempted, then restore it and show none happens. If removing it changes nothing, the agent must stop and report what actually protects us.\n- **Enumeration:** list every git subprocess site, including anything that builds its own `cmd.Env`. Then a fake `git` on PATH that fails if either `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` or `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` is missing, run across index, query and snapshot. That test is itself weakened at one site, and the agent moves the env to the single construction point where that's small.\n\nI've noted your `#474` reconciliation. Your `grep -rn \"symbol[^(]\"` check goes into the C1 disclosure text, so it tells a reader how to check whether the gap affects their own symbol.\n\nI'll ping you with a binary path for the entiredb re-index once B-a's tests are green, and not before. And noted that your entiredb B2 numbers came from the uncached path, so they aren't a baseline.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Both of your promisor points are now hard require…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_read_input_tokens":269066,"output_tokens":1588,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":157},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1588,"cache_read_input_tokens":269066,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2814,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2814},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LTinVvRSkuE1RcRkEXhmtt":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Promisor proof requirements forwarded; ping on binary","message":"Both of your promisor points are now hard requirements on the B-a agent, before it opens the PR:\n- **Weakening:** a `blob:none` clone with a reachable `file://` remote and a missing blob. Remove `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` and show a fetch IS attempted, then restore it and show none happens. If removing it changes nothing, the agent must stop and report what actually protects us.\n- **Enumeration:** list every git subprocess site, including anything that builds its own `cmd.Env`. Then a fake `git` on PATH that fails if either `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` or `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` is missing, run across index, query and snapshot. That test is itself weakened at one site, and the agent moves the env to the single construction point where that's small.\n\nI've noted your `#474` reconciliation. Your `grep -rn \"symbol[^(]\"` check goes into the C1 disclosure text, so it tells a reader how to check whether the gap affects their own symbol.\n\nI'll ping you with a binary path for the entiredb re-index once B-a's tests are green, and not before. And noted that your entiredb B2 numbers came from the uncached path, so they aren't a baseline."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b4752994-68f2-41e7-b4ff-9fdd9f1cb36b","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgMa7GT76ZZ8bLNbsipBu","requestRef":"af932869-6829-4e2b-a29b-c59c32eb5a2d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-