{"parentUuid":"d16ee00c-66ac-47e4-9fa8-d071f8ad5a6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMa98MG6dYvHh74FsoGi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've added the Brain session's two safety requirements to the partial-clone fix. It can't open a PR until both are proven:\n- **Show the no-fetch setting actually matters.** Use a partial clone with a reachable remote and a missing file. With the setting removed, git must attempt a network fetch. With it restored, there must be no fetch and a clean error instead. If removing it changes nothing, the agent stops and reports what is really protecting us.\n- **Cover every place the graph launches git**, not just the ones someone remembered. A fake `git` on the path fails the test if either no-network setting is missing, across index, query and snapshot. That test is itself checked by removing the setting at one call site and confirming it fails.\n\nThe Brain session also confirmed that the \"function passed as a value\" gap didn't affect one of its own already-shipped PRs, and it gave a one-line grep for checking whether the gap affects a given symbol. That goes into the disclosure fix.\n\nAll three fix agents are still running. I'll report when they finish."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":521,"cache_read_input_tokens":273828,"output_tokens":328,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":521,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":328,"cache_read_input_tokens":273828,"cache_creation_input_tokens":521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":521},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_