{"parentUuid":"6fcef7f1-cda1-4765-bd87-c26f24c081ca","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMaMpS765HKckLoqfbWp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Brain session is right, and it measured it. My fixture would never have had a missing blob, so removing the guard would \"change nothing\" for the wrong reason. Both guards also block a fetch independently, so they have to be tested one at a time. Sending the corrected fixture and matrix to the agent now:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2204,"cache_read_input_tokens":274349,"output_tokens":1932,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":116},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2204,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1932,"cache_read_input_tokens":274349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2204},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"562072ec-63c8-491b-a70c-e16ddd7fcbac","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMaMp5WtdL7z5UKqNkzw","requestRef":"ecc4ac8e-955f-44b0-ae95-0cb3d86f1f7f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"503885a6-c403-41a9-ac53-b68827f8be52","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:59:18.272Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"503885a6-c403-41a9-ac53-b68827f8be52","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMaMpS765HKckLoqfbWp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YEVQw5G1vKdvLVDSssn7Ku","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"CORRECTION: B-a fixture inert; use this one","message":"**CORRECTION to my last message. Read this before running the weakening.** The fixture I specified is inert, and the weakening had a confound. This was measured on this machine (git 2.54.0).\n\n## 1. The fixture I specified never has a missing blob\n`git clone --filter=blob:none --no-local file://...src` either warns \"filtering not recognized by server\", or, with `uploadpack.allowFilter=true` set, records promisor=true but STILL sends the blob. In-pack shows 3 objects, `rev-list --objects --all --missing=print | grep -c '^?'` returns 0, and the blob sizes match. So no lazy fetch is ever possible. **Do not use it. Do NOT take the \"stop and report what protects us\" branch on the basis of that fixture.**\n\n## 2. Use this fixture\nClone normally, declare the promisor by hand, then repack without the blob:\n```sh\ngit clone --no-local \"file://$SRC\" cl && cd cl\ngit config remote.origin.promisor true\ngit config remote.origin.partialclonefilter blob:none\nBLOB=$(git rev-parse HEAD:big.txt)\ngit rev-list --objects HEAD | awk -v b=\"$BLOB\" '$1!=b {print $1}' > keep.txt\nrm -f .git/objects/pack/*.pack .git/objects/pack/*.idx\ngit pack-objects --non-empty .git/objects/pack/pack < keep.txt\n```\nVerify before trusting it: in-pack must be 2, and `--missing=print | grep -c '^?'` must be **1**.\n\n**Copy the tree fresh for every probe**, because one successful fetch repairs it and every later probe then measures nothing. Keep `keep.txt` out of the repo, in a temp dir of your own, not shared `/tmp`.\n\n## 3. The matrix. Remove ONE guard at a time, and assert exit code plus stderr, not just \"failed\"\nExpected (measured):\n\n| env | exit | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` only | 1 | refused silently: **fetch never attempted** |\n| no guards | 0 | fetch succeeded; proves the fixture is live |\n| `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` only | 128 | `fatal: transport 'file' not allowed` / `could not fetch ... from promisor remote`: **attempted, blocked at transport** |\n| both | 1 | the lazy-fetch guard refuses first |\n\nRemoving `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` while `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` is still set stays blocked. That is not evidence that the lazy-fetch guard is inert: both guards protect independently, so test each one in isolation.\n\n## 4. What the fix must rest on\nAdmit promisor repos on the basis of `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` (**never attempted**), and keep `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` as the second layer. \"Attempted but blocked\" is weaker: it is only as good as the protocol allowlist covering every transport git may add. **The PR must say which guard does the work.** The env-enumeration test (fake git asserting both vars at every site) still applies.\n\n## 5. Harness trap\nCapture git's exit code BEFORE any pipe (`git ...; rc=$?`, or `set -o pipefail`). Piping into `head` and reading `$?` reports head's status, and the whole matrix then reads as uniform success.","type":"message","recipient":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"**CORRECTION to my last message. Read this before…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2204,"cache_read_input_tokens":274349,"output_tokens":1932,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":116},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2204,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1932,"cache_read_input_tokens":274349,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2204},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YEVQw5G1vKdvLVDSssn7Ku":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"CORRECTION: B-a fixture inert; use this one","message":"**CORRECTION to my last message. Read this before running the weakening.** The fixture I specified is inert, and the weakening had a confound. This was measured on this machine (git 2.54.0).\n\n## 1. The fixture I specified never has a missing blob\n`git clone --filter=blob:none --no-local file://...src` either warns \"filtering not recognized by server\", or, with `uploadpack.allowFilter=true` set, records promisor=true but STILL sends the blob. In-pack shows 3 objects, `rev-list --objects --all --missing=print | grep -c '^?'` returns 0, and the blob sizes match. So no lazy fetch is ever possible. **Do not use it. Do NOT take the \"stop and report what protects us\" branch on the basis of that fixture.**\n\n## 2. Use this fixture\nClone normally, declare the promisor by hand, then repack without the blob:\n```sh\ngit clone --no-local \"file://$SRC\" cl && cd cl\ngit config remote.origin.promisor true\ngit config remote.origin.partialclonefilter blob:none\nBLOB=$(git rev-parse HEAD:big.txt)\ngit rev-list --objects HEAD | awk -v b=\"$BLOB\" '$1!=b {print $1}' > keep.txt\nrm -f .git/objects/pack/*.pack .git/objects/pack/*.idx\ngit pack-objects --non-empty .git/objects/pack/pack < keep.txt\n```\nVerify before trusting it: in-pack must be 2, and `--missing=print | grep -c '^?'` must be **1**.\n\n**Copy the tree fresh for every probe**, because one successful fetch repairs it and every later probe then measures nothing. Keep `keep.txt` out of the repo, in a temp dir of your own, not shared `/tmp`.\n\n## 3. The matrix. Remove ONE guard at a time, and assert exit code plus stderr, not just \"failed\"\nExpected (measured):\n\n| env | exit | meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` only | 1 | refused silently: **fetch never attempted** |\n| no guards | 0 | fetch succeeded; proves the fixture is live |\n| `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` only | 128 | `fatal: transport 'file' not allowed` / `could not fetch ... from promisor remote`: **attempted, blocked at transport** |\n| both | 1 | the lazy-fetch guard refuses first |\n\nRemoving `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` while `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` is still set stays blocked. That is not evidence that the lazy-fetch guard is inert: both guards protect independently, so test each one in isolation.\n\n## 4. What the fix must rest on\nAdmit promisor repos on the basis of `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` (**never attempted**), and keep `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` as the second layer. \"Attempted but blocked\" is weaker: it is only as good as the protocol allowlist covering every transport git may add. **The PR must say which guard does the work.** The env-enumeration test (fake git asserting both vars at every site) still applies.\n\n## 5. Harness trap\nCapture git's exit code BEFORE any pipe (`git ...; rc=$?`, or `set -o pipefail`). Piping into `head` and reading `$?` reports head's status, and the whole matrix then reads as uniform success."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"562072ec-63c8-491b-a70c-e16ddd7fcbac","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMaMp5WtdL7z5UKqNkzw","requestRef":"ecc4ac8e-955f-44b0-ae95-0cb3d86f1f7f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b6cff195-b0a8-4f8d-a1db-b0991b318d50","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:59:29.024Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
