{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01PqDMp44x938Dn847VmmdtN","lastSequenceNum":0,"noHistoryBackfill":true,"ownerAccountUuid":"1adeeb49-de49-49d0-b362-b9b5f0bc27ed","ownerOrganizationUuid":"46041b3e-8c7e-4659-a2cb-1751292663c4"}
{"parentUuid":"a1502c33-b71d-45d1-9def-f1bde17fdc73","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Wa1cFaSDrikaVjW6N2BQrn","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"f=/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test.md; rtk read \\\"$f\\\" | head -30\",\"description\":\"Read the existing memory on unfired mutations\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":12},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f1fd9257-0cf5-4c46-a3ba-bad5eb32bfe7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:59:38.140Z","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"a1502c33-b71d-45d1-9def-f1bde17fdc73","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f2bbc9ca-06d3-4de5-913c-db6876c6b435","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Wa1cFaSDrikaVjW6N2BQrn","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test\ndescription: When a mutation that should obviously break a test doesn't, the fault is almost always my fixture — twice in one session I nearly reported a guard as unholdable\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n**A mutation that should bite and doesn't is evidence about the TEST first, the code second.**\nTwice in one session I broke a guard on purpose, watched the suite stay green, and was one step\nfrom reporting that the guard could not be held:\n\n1. **The fixture was never added.** Two `map[string]string` entries I \"added\" matched no anchor —\n   gofmt had realigned the map — so the edit silently did nothing. I then reported the fixture to\n   a reviewer as present. They checked and it was absent.\n2. **The fixture was empty.** An ordering test drove a real run over a synthetic repo whose doc\n   comments were too short for the benchmark's own eight-word filter, so it produced ZERO cases.\n   Every assertion quantified over an empty list and all five printed green.\n\n**Why:** both look identical to \"this guard is unfalsifiable\", which sends you rewriting correct\ncode or deleting a good test.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- after adding a fixture, **grep for it** — never trust that the edit reported success. Make edit\n  scripts `assert` their anchor.\n- start any test that quantifies over a collection with a **non-vacuity assertion**: `len(x) > 0`.\n- when a mutation doesn't fire, first prove the mutation *applied* (`assert anchor in src`), then\n  prove the fixture is non-empty, and only then suspect the guard.\n\nRelated: [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]], [[logic-in-the-call-site]], [[containment-for-exactness]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3b988afc-b446-404b-ae95-7658645f871e","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:59:40.690Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: mutation-didnt-fire-suspect-the-test\ndescription: When a mutation that should obviously break a test doesn't, the fault is almost always my fixture — twice in one session I nearly reported a guard as unholdable\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n**A mutation that should bite and doesn't is evidence about the TEST first, the code second.**\nTwice in one session I broke a guard on purpose, watched the suite stay green, and was one step\nfrom reporting that the guard could not be held:\n\n1. **The fixture was never added.** Two `map[string]string` entries I \"added\" matched no anchor —\n   gofmt had realigned the map — so the edit silently did nothing. I then reported the fixture to\n   a reviewer as present. They checked and it was absent.\n2. **The fixture was empty.** An ordering test drove a real run over a synthetic repo whose doc\n   comments were too short for the benchmark's own eight-word filter, so it produced ZERO cases.\n   Every assertion quantified over an empty list and all five printed green.\n\n**Why:** both look identical to \"this guard is unfalsifiable\", which sends you rewriting correct\ncode or deleting a good test.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- after adding a fixture, **grep for it** — never trust that the edit reported success. Make edit\n  scripts `assert` their anchor.\n- start any test that quantifies over a collection with a **non-vacuity assertion**: `len(x) > 0`.\n- when a mutation doesn't fire, first prove the mutation *applied* (`assert anchor in src`), then\n  prove the fixture is non-empty, and only then suspect the guard.\n\nRelated: [[green-suite-is-not-evidence]], [[logic-in-the-call-site]], [[containment-for-exactness]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"classifierBoundary":true,"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"93cb3840-15b4-412a-aad0-bd4c7f548cec","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":243},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a1502c33-b71d-45d1-9def-f1bde17fdc73","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
