{"parentUuid":"5d07f1e4-dcd1-4c06-809e-c77923e9a4fc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14701605 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"256a0e9b-921c-4342-bc00-8f0be051f1b7","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:59:50.735Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14701605 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"256a0e9b-921c-4342-bc00-8f0be051f1b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMaQaWHXSDDfP2cUW53y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Brain session caught a real flaw in the safety test I'd specified for the partial-clone fix, and the corrected version has gone to the agent.\n\n**What was wrong**\n- **The test repo never had a missing file.** A local partial clone still downloads every file. That means git could never fetch anything, so removing the no-fetch setting would have \"changed nothing\". I had told the agent to treat exactly that outcome as \"stop and investigate what really protects us\", so it would have gone hunting for the wrong problem.\n- **Two separate settings each block the fetch on their own.** Removing one while the other is still set also blocks it, and that looks like \"the first setting does nothing\".\n\n**What the agent does now**\n- **Build the test repo the other way round:** clone it normally, then delete one file's data, and confirm the file really is missing before using it.\n- **Remove one setting at a time** and check for the exact expected error, not just \"it failed\".\n- **Rest the fix on the stronger setting.** One setting means git never attempts a fetch at all. The other means git attempts it and is refused. The fix relies on \"never attempts\", the refusal stays as a second layer, and the PR has to say which one is doing the work.\n\nI've added this case to my note on tests that fail for the wrong reason: before telling an agent to break a safety check, confirm the test setup actually reaches that check.\n\nAll three fix agents are still running."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1039,"cache_read_input_tokens":279747,"output_tokens":443,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1039,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":443,"cache_read_input_tokens":279747,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1039,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1039},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"fd7f2e44-21f2-400f-ad0f-934ede3c72e3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMaQaCBgc2E5rKMJdqS9","requestRef":"50a91573-4062-4ba4-ada5-6d28805aa318","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"25e8d60c-acc4-468f-92fe-1ebb0a3b9a2f","timestamp":"2026-10-24T18:59:57.594Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
