{"parentUuid":"19f6da2a-c99c-4fc2-b345-86bad9aa3d3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMefGpnoEHQWKnvAHb2M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016zAVCTxTDE1xuzxUveb5YF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"- **No full local suites.**\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"- **CI runs tests with `-race`.** Run your focused tests with `-race` too, under mlock, before trusting a local green. Watch for anything that reads a subprocess's captured `Stdout`/`Stderr` (a `bytes.Buffer` or `strings.Builder`) before `cmd.Wait()`: os/exec copies into it from its own goroutine, so that is a data race.\\n- If CI shows a broad cascade of unrelated failures, **grep the log for `DATA RACE` first.** One race poisons the whole run and looks exactly like resource exhaustion.\\n\"+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Add the race-detector rule to the protocol"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_read_input_tokens":300786,"output_tokens":1645,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":165},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1645,"cache_read_input_tokens":300786,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_016zAVCTxTDE1xuzxUveb5YF":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"- **No full local suites.**\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"- **CI runs tests with `-race`.** Run your focused tests with `-race` too, under mlock, before trusting a local green. Watch for anything that reads a subprocess's captured `Stdout`/`Stderr` (a `bytes.Buffer` or `strings.Builder`) before `cmd.Wait()`: os/exec copies into it from its own goroutine, so that is a data race.\\n- If CI shows a broad cascade of unrelated failures, **grep the log for `DATA RACE` first.** One race poisons the whole run and looks exactly like resource exhaustion.\\n\"+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Add the race-detector rule to the protocol"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"6bc88892-aab1-4b5a-9970-dc896ba40e4c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMefGP18QJ61VbkgSi2C","requestRef":"10a8acbd-02cb-4500-9d0a-859a6ba8526f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"171b2aa2-455a-4477-acb5-1caf85b59caf","timestamp":"2026-10-24T19:55:44.204Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"171b2aa2-455a-4477-acb5-1caf85b59caf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMefGpnoEHQWKnvAHb2M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AGHFfrjDFVVr251hdiLmnm","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"Run -race locally; subprocess-output race shape","message":"One more protocol rule, now in G3-PROTOCOL.md. **CI runs tests with `-race`.** Run your focused tests with `-race` too, under mlock, before trusting a local green.\n\nYour change touches git subprocess environments, so check for this bug shape, which the Brain session just shipped and fixed: `cmd.Stderr = &buf` (a `bytes.Buffer` or `strings.Builder`) read before `cmd.Wait()`. `os/exec` copies into a non-`*os.File` sink from its own goroutine, so that read is a data race. The fake-git env test and any probe that reads stderr early are the likely spots.\n\nIf CI shows a broad cascade of unrelated failures, grep the log for `DATA RACE` before assuming resource exhaustion.","type":"message","recipient":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"One more protocol rule, now in G3-PROTOCOL.md. **…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_read_input_tokens":300786,"output_tokens":1645,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":165},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1645,"cache_read_input_tokens":300786,"cache_creation_input_tokens":868,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":868},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null