lerLocale). Callers came from graph neighbors plus grep and are listed in the PR body. No per-site fix needed.\n\nTests, all weakened to red and restored (each restore confirmed with a clean git diff):\n- (a) Offline index after the remote is deleted. Red when the guard is reverted, and red when `show -s` is restored.\n- (b) Missing blob gives E_FILE_READ with no child git at all (spy git via GIT_EXEC_PATH, plus a control showing the spy does catch a fetch). Red when noLazyFetchEnv is dropped.\n- (c) A fake git 2.44 still refuses, with the new text. Red under admit-always, and red with the old message.\n- (d) The second `query --head` is a cache hit. Red when the guard is reverted.\n- Env test: a logging git on PATH across 11 CLI commands plus grep; both vars present on every call. Red when either var is dropped, and red when only the grep constructor is unguarded.\n- Static AST test: no process launch outside the two constructors and the allowlist. Red on an added exec.Command, and red on a non-literal program.\n- Also: parse threshold, sem gate/diagnosis/probe-cost tests, and a Windows UNC admit test (it only runs on Windows CI).\n\nLocal: whole gitutil, sem (288s) and cli (282s) packages green, -p 1, under the lock. Focused tests green under -race via mlock. All locked runs used a python fcntl wrapper on measure.lock, the same lock mlock takes. The one `flock` call errored and nothing ran.\n\nLive (main checkouts, read-only, fresh cache):\n- entiredb: base fails with exit 1; new indexes 2542 files / 36068 symbols, completeness ok, 15 partial failures (all parse/minified, none from missing blobs).\n- cli: base exit 1; new indexes 1427 files / 28619 symbols, ok.\n- A trace build of cli made 19 git calls and 0 fetches.\n\nN2 query --head, base → new medians, 3 interleaved reps, load1 8.6-10.2:\n- cli: 32.59s → 3.38s\n- entiredb: 7.96s → 2.37s\n- Identity: the result lists are identical. Only provenance changes: commit/tree are set and the fallback warnings are gone.\n- Caveat: on entiredb a query containing \"repository\" takes the slow alias route (review #1) on a cache hit, 15.6s vs 8.8s. That is pre-existing for every non-partial repo and documented in the PR.\n\nCI, all pass: build×3, lint, test ubuntu (git 2.55), test macos (git 2.56), test windows + 8 shards, CodeQL, others.\nCI, failed: Entire Gates, on the Approvals sub-gate only. Findings sub-gate passed (0 findings) and Checks passed.\nCI, running: none.\n\nNot done:\n- Brain fact not recorded: the protocol forbids touching ~/.local/share/entire. Candidate fact: \"partial clones admitted only with Git ≥2.45; GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH is the load-bearing guard; avoid `git show -s` on partial clones.\"\n- Known limitation, in the PR body: co-change `git log --name-only` fails on blob:none-of-origin history with inexact renames, and FILE_CHANGES_WITH is dropped silently. This is pre-existing and does not affect entiredb or cli.\n- Scratchpad clash acknowledged. My files are now in <worktree>/.g3 (untracked). The #372 body was verified as mine and complete."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
