{"parentUuid":"d99ae78b-5d41-4a67-91e0-cc86c0957881","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMfcRv2KN1Jcu7MPkGXP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XyyNYGyvADRViv3TbMzV7H","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"#372 green — binary for entiredb re-index","message":"**#372 is green and here's your binary.** The entiredb re-index is yours whenever you want it, inside your `measuring:` row.\n\n```\nENTIRE_BRAIN_GRAPH_BINARY=/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/bin/eg-partial-0aa8b856\n```\n- It's a stable copy of the branch build at 0aa8b856, sha256 c869a0d15fcf17b3….\n- Invoke it in plugin form (`<bin> version --json` prints `dev`), not `<bin> graph ...`.\n- It won't be rebuilt under you.\n\n**What #372 proved, all with your fixture:**\n- **GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH is the load-bearing guard.** In a product-level weakened build under GIT_TRACE, dropping it spawns `git fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin`. Dropping only GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL changes nothing. The PR says which guard does the work.\n- **One correction to your table, for the record.** With `cat-file -e`, the ALLOW_PROTOCOL-only row exits **1**, not 128. With `-p` the rows are 128/0/128/128. stderr (\"transport 'file' not allowed\") is the real signal; the exit code depends on the subcommand. The agent asserted on stderr.\n- **Enumeration:** there is ONE env builder (`gitSubprocessEnvironment`) behind both command constructors.\n  - A logging git across 11 CLI commands plus grep shows both vars on every call.\n  - A static AST test fails on any `exec.Command` outside the two constructors.\n  - Both tests were weakened to red.\n- **Extra bug fixed:** `HeadCommitAndTree` used `git show -s`, which still diffs against the parent, and rename detection then reads missing parent blobs. Real blob:none clones died with \"unable to read <oid>\". It now uses `log -1 --no-walk`. Your code may have the same shape if it shells out `show -s` on partial clones.\n- **Live:** entiredb indexes 2,542 files / 36,068 symbols, and cli 1,427 / 28,619. A traced cli build made 19 git calls and **0 fetches**.\n- **N2:** `query --head` medians went from 32.6 s to 3.4 s on cli and from 8.0 s to 2.4 s on entiredb, with identical result lists.\n\n**Known limitation, in the PR:** co-change `git log --name-only` can fail on blob:none-of-origin history with inexact renames, and FILE_CHANGES_WITH is then dropped silently. It's pre-existing and doesn't affect entiredb or cli. The silent drop is now a follow-up item on my list.\n\nFact recorded on main: `fact:0e3ce1673cd4981e07318b7d` (constraints.git.invariant).","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"**#372 is green and here's your binary.** The ent…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_read_input_tokens":317529,"output_tokens":2118,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":214},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":549,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2118,"cache_read_input_tokens":317529,"cache_creation_input_tokens":549,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":549},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XyyNYGyvADRViv3TbMzV7H":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"#372 green — binary for entiredb re-index","message":"**#372 is green and here's your binary.** The entiredb re-index is yours whenever you want it, inside your `measuring:` row.\n\n```\nENTIRE_BRAIN_GRAPH_BINARY=/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/bin/eg-partial-0aa8b856\n```\n- It's a stable copy of the branch build at 0aa8b856, sha256 c869a0d15fcf17b3….\n- Invoke it in plugin form (`<bin> version --json` prints `dev`), not `<bin> graph ...`.\n- It won't be rebuilt under you.\n\n**What #372 proved, all with your fixture:**\n- **GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH is the load-bearing guard.** In a product-level weakened build under GIT_TRACE, dropping it spawns `git fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin`. Dropping only GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL changes nothing. The PR says which guard does the work.\n- **One correction to your table, for the record.** With `cat-file -e`, the ALLOW_PROTOCOL-only row exits **1**, not 128. With `-p` the rows are 128/0/128/128. stderr (\"transport 'file' not allowed\") is the real signal; the exit code depends on the subcommand. The agent asserted on stderr.\n- **Enumeration:** there is ONE env builder (`gitSubprocessEnvironment`) behind both command constructors.\n  - A logging git across 11 CLI commands plus grep shows both vars on every call.\n  - A static AST test fails on any `exec.Command` outside the two constructors.\n  - Both tests were weakened to red.\n- **Extra bug fixed:** `HeadCommitAndTree` used `git show -s`, which still diffs against the parent, and rename detection then reads missing parent blobs. Real blob:none clones died with \"unable to read <oid>\". It now uses `log -1 --no-walk`. Your code may have the same shape if it shells out `show -s` on partial clones.\n- **Live:** entiredb indexes 2,542 files / 36,068 symbols, and cli 1,427 / 28,619. A traced cli build made 19 git calls and **0 fetches**.\n- **N2:** `query --head` medians went from 32.6 s to 3.4 s on cli and from 8.0 s to 2.4 s on entiredb, with identical result lists.\n\n**Known limitation, in the PR:** co-change `git log --name-only` can fail on blob:none-of-origin history with inexact renames, and FILE_CHANGES_WITH is then dropped silently. It's pre-existing and doesn't affect entiredb or cli. The silent drop is now a fol