{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"56c4815e4ad6f64bd609e264defe7e2c9437e201ff8555b5fc54e45cfc9cdb54","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XyyNYGyvADRViv3TbMzV7H","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"#372 green — binary for entiredb re-index","message":"**#372 is green and here's your binary.** The entiredb re-index is yours whenever you want it, inside your `measuring:` row.\n\n```\nENTIRE_BRAIN_GRAPH_BINARY=/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/bin/eg-partial-0aa8b856\n```\n- It's a stable copy of the branch build at 0aa8b856, sha256 c869a0d15fcf17b3….\n- Invoke it in plugin form (`<bin> version --json` prints `dev`), not `<bin> graph ...`.\n- It won't be rebuilt under you.\n\n**What #372 proved, all with your fixture:**\n- **GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH is the load-bearing guard.** In a product-level weakened build under GIT_TRACE, dropping it spawns `git fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin`. Dropping only GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL changes nothing. The PR says which guard does the work.\n- **One correction to your table, for the record.** With `cat-file -e`, the ALLOW_PROTOCOL-only row exits **1**, not 128. With `-p` the rows are 128/0/128/128. stderr (\"transport 'file' not allowed\") is the real signal; the exit code depends on the subcommand. The agent asserted on stderr.\n- **Enumeration:** there is ONE env builder (`gitSubprocessEnvironment`) behind both command constructors.\n  - A logging git across 11 CLI commands plus grep shows both vars on every call.\n  - A static AST test fails on any `exec.Command` outside the two constructors.\n  - Both tests were weakened to red.\n- **Extra bug fixed:** `HeadCommitAndTree` used `git show -s`, which still diffs against the parent, and rename detection then reads missing parent blobs. Real blob:none clones died with \"unable to read <oid>\". It now uses `log -1 --no-walk`. Your code may have the same shape if it shells out `show -s` on partial clones.\n- **Live:** entiredb indexes 2,542 files / 36,068 symbols, and cli 1,427 / 28,619. A traced cli build made 19 git calls and **0 fetches**.\n- **N2:** `query --head` medians went from 32.6 s to 3.4 s on cli and from 8.0 s to 2.4 s on entiredb, with identical result lists.\n\n**Known limitation, in the PR:** co-change `git log --name-only` can fail on blob:none-of-origin history with inexact renames, and FILE_CHANGES_WITH is then dropped silently. It's pre-existing and doesn't affect entiredb or cli. The silent drop is now a follow-up item on my list.\n\nFact recorded on main: `fact:0e3ce1673cd4981e07318b7d` (constraints.git.invariant)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XTnSEdmpaJjx3oNR4XdwEs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G3-Ba'].update(status='done', note='PR #372: CI all green except Approvals; Findings 0. GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH proven load-bearing (weakened build spawns git fetch); one env builder, plus fake-git and AST tests. Also fixed show -s reading parent blobs. cli and entiredb index offline (0 fetches); query --head cli 32.6 → 3.4 s, entiredb 8.0 → 2.4 s. Binary handed to brain for the entiredb re-index.')\nif 'G-partial' in T: T['G-partial'].update(status='done', note='Covered by PR #372.')\ni=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('G3-C1')+1\nfor rid,title,note in [\n  ('G3-cochange','Disclose (do not silently drop) FILE_CHANGES_WITH when co-change git log fails on blob:none history','Follow-up from #372: inexact renames on blob:none-of-origin history make git log --name-only fail; the relation is dropped silently.'),\n  ('D-review-372','Independent adversarial pass on #372 before the merge handoff (it relaxes a no-network guard)','Gate-agent findings were 0, but this is the security-sensitive PR: a skeptic re-derives the offline guarantee from source.')]:\n    if rid not in T: d['tasks'].insert(i, dict(id=rid,lane='graph',title=title,status='todo',owner='claude',source='proactive',note=note)); i+=1\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Mark B-a done and add follow-ups on the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
