{"parentUuid":"5eed83fd-f302-4ea2-a065-f9d53ce5ab6a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMfdv6TRbGtDZ7cQt95q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two of the three fixes are done:\n\n| PR | Fix | CI | Result |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [#371](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/371) | alias search | tests still running when last checked | entire-graph 224 s → 5 s |\n| [#372](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/372) | partial clones | green; only the Approvals gate is open | cli and entiredb index offline; their queries are about 3–10× faster |\n\n**Proving #372 is safe offline**\n- The agent proved which setting stops git fetching over the network by removing it. A traced build then made 19 git calls and no network fetches.\n- It confirmed every git launch goes through one place, and added a test that fails if new code ever launches git another way.\n- It also found and fixed a second bug that crashed indexing on real partial clones.\n\n**Handed to the Brain session**\n- A stable copy of the #372 binary, so it can finish re-indexing entiredb (that repo was 90% done and blocked only on this).\n- One lesson recorded in Brain's memory: partial clones are allowed only on git 2.45 or newer, and it's the no-fetch setting that protects us.\n\n**Added to the board**\n- **A second check of #372 before the final merge handoff.** It loosens a safety guard, so a separate reviewer will rebuild the offline argument from the code.\n- **A follow-up fix:** on some partial clones, the graph silently drops \"files that change together\" data instead of saying it's missing.\n\nThe pipeline-speedup agent is finishing its timing runs. The next wave starts after that, so it doesn't disturb those measurements: the history cache fix, the selective-view write, and tool detection."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2344,"cache_read_input_tokens":318078,"output_tokens":855,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":293},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2344,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":855,"cache_read_input_tokens":318078,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2344},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8e150523-afe8-4294-8783-8aeb80d5b7cf","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMfduP34nw6fK4ZM6ihE","requestRef":"94fed5cd-3b42-4a11-b365-ac07b9fd95b7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"919daf02-eef5-4656-964e-4e590f925af2","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:08:39.577Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
