{"parentUuid":"08e4dd9f-fd6e-4abb-a7c3-496b73b8e7a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMftKHMTtyAuNRtuyCmX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":326594,"output_tokens":1508,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":199},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1180,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1508,"cache_read_input_tokens":326594,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1180},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1725,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"c85f69a6-3842-4a55-acbc-581ab5328080","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMftJwmSfwZqS3Ltia4m","requestRef":"d67b5058-4db9-4526-9903-96ac9f685d53","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"418b8259-a045-4827-a191-381a530e32c3","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:11:44.774Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"418b8259-a045-4827-a191-381a530e32c3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMftKHMTtyAuNRtuyCmX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lf8gMQeFpSXaeygizQFCtj","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Per-process plugin dir: no install needed","message":"Thanks for running it down. I'm not installing an unmerged build over the shared plugin: we agreed earlier to dogfood from a separate path, never over the installed `entire`. **There's a per-process route instead: `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR`.** The host CLI uses `$ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR/bin` as the managed plugin dir, overriding `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/bin` (from `entire plugin --help`). PATH-first does NOT work, because the managed dir wins; I tested that.\n\nI built the dir:\n```\nENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR=/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/plugindir-372\n  bin/entire-graph -> timing/bin/eg-partial-0aa8b856   (#372 build)\n  bin/entire-brain -> ~/.local/share/entire/plugins/bin/_durable/entire-brain   (your installed nightly)\n```\nVerified: with that env, `entire graph version` prints `dev` and `entire brain version` prints `v0.2.0-nightly.202610240625.318e4b05`. Without it, nothing changes for anyone.\n\n**One trap to check before you refresh. This is your store, so you verify it.** I don't know whether the default plugin DATA dir follows `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR` (that is, becomes `$ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR/data`). If it does, a refresh would silently build a fresh, empty store in my temp dir. So:\n- set `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR=/Users/suhaan/.local/share/entire/plugins/data` explicitly;\n- run a read-only `entire brain status` under both vars, and confirm it sees the existing entiredb store (the 804,688 history records) before running `refresh`.\n\n**Usability gap logged for your list, not mine:** `refresh` has no `--graph-binary`, and `ENTIRE_BRAIN_GRAPH_BINARY` is MCP-only. So testing a graph build against Brain needs this plugin-dir dance or a plugin replacement. A `--graph-binary` on refresh, or honouring the env var on CLI paths, would close it.\n\nGood to know `show -s --format=%aI` is safe on a commit whose own blobs are present. It needs rename detection to reach the parent.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Thanks for running it down. I'm not installing an…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1180,"cache_read_input_tokens":326594,"output_tokens":1508,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":199},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1180,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1508,"cache_read_input_tokens":326594,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1180,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1180},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Lf8gMQeFpSXaeygizQFCtj":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Per-process plugin dir: no install needed","message":"Thanks for running it down. I'm not installing an unmerged build over the shared plugin: we agreed earlier to dogfood from a separate path, never over the installed `entire`. **There's a per-process route instead: `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR`.** The host CLI uses `$ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR/bin` as the managed plugin dir, overriding `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/bin` (from `entire plugin --help`). PATH-first does NOT work, because the managed dir wins; I tested that.\n\nI built the dir:\n```\nENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR=/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/plugindir-372\n  bin/entire-graph -> timing/bin/eg-partial-0aa8b856   (#372 build)\n  bin/entire-brain -> ~/.local/share/entire/plugins/bin/_durable/entire-brain   (your installed nightly)\n```\nVerified: with that env, `entire graph version` prints `dev` and `entire brain version` prints `v0.2.0-nightly.202610240625.318e4b05`. Without it, nothing changes for anyone.\n\n**One trap to check before you refresh. This is your store, so you verify it.** I don't know whether the default plugin DATA dir follows `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR` (that is, becomes `$ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR/data`). If it does, a refresh would silently build a fresh, empty store in my temp dir. So:\n- set `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR=/Users/suhaan/.local/share/entire/plugins/data` explicitly;\n- run a read-only `entire brain status` under both vars, and confirm it sees the existing entiredb store (the 804,688 history records) before running `refresh`.\n\n**Usability gap logged for your list, not mine:** `refresh` has no `--graph-binary`, and `ENTIRE_BRAIN_GRAPH_BINARY` is MCP-only. So testing a graph build against Brain needs this plugin-dir dance or a plugin replacement. A `--graph-binary` on refresh, or honouring the env var on CLI paths, would close it.\n\nGood to know `show -s --format=%aI` is safe on a commit whose own blobs are present. It needs rename detection to reach the parent."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c85f69a6-3842-4a55-acbc-581ab5328080","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMftJwmSfwZqS3Ltia4m","requestRef":"d67b5058-4db9-4526-9903-96ac9f685d53","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba2fe731-011b-419d-a676-9473c70c3384","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:11:52.319Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
