{"parentUuid":"44f6deda-9335-4b6a-95d1-6f54a75622d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMfuSumUJG9w5VoNYv9Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Brain session couldn't use the test binary I gave it. Brain's binary override only applies to its MCP server, not to the refresh command it needed. Finishing entiredb's re-index would therefore have meant installing the unmerged fix over the shared graph plugin. That's what you and both sessions run, and my earlier plan said to test from a separate path, never over the installed `entire`. So I didn't install it.\n\nI found a per-process route instead: setting `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DIR` makes the `entire` command load plugins from a different folder. I built a folder with the fixed graph build and the normal Brain build, and checked that both load correctly with the variable set. Without it, nothing changes for anyone.\n\nI told the Brain session to confirm two things before refreshing:\n- that Brain still finds its real data with that variable set;\n- that it isn't writing to a fresh, empty copy instead.\n\nThe Brain session also found that one of its own git calls has the same shape as the bug #372 fixed. It turned out to be safe, confirmed on a real partial clone.\n\nThe pipeline-speedup agent is on its final measurements."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1728,"cache_read_input_tokens":327774,"output_tokens":366,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1728,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":366,"cache_read_input_tokens":327774,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1728,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":17