{"parentUuid":"f60913cd-e8e6-4ccf-96a1-2e59b82ada34","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMgJDwoN3LvRR1npAsQV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016v375P8hE94DnxvbDeeDZw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"- A test that cannot go red is not a test.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n- **Fake subprocesses that answer and exit must drain stdin** (`cat >/dev/null &` … `wait`). Otherwise the caller's write to stdin races the exit and fails with EPIPE (\"broken pipe\") on CI while passing locally. Fake `git` used with `grep -f -` is exactly this shape.\n- **When a guard depends on goroutine timing, make the fixture force the order.** For example, a fake that closes stdout first, sleeps, then writes its reason. Don't hope the race lands the same way on CI: on macOS one side may win every time, so the weakening passes locally and only CI disagrees.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Add fake-subprocess and race-forcing rules to protocol"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1317,"cache_read_input_tokens":333184,"output_tokens":950,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":167},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1317,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":950,"cache_read_input_tokens":333184,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1317,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1317},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu