{"parentUuid":"197a8dbe-d8a4-4d95-9634-a5e175978535","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMgzq7zytievvwfCMG3r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CEBVhHuzCJxEdHfaGUsvJt","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-4/5: history splice + selective view","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement TWO entire-graph speed fixes as two separate open PRs, each in its own worktree off origin/main. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock` for timing and long tests, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch files in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK. Both fixes touch search_cache.go, so keep each diff minimal and on a different hunk to keep merge conflicts small.\n\nRead rows #4, #5 and #10 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n## Fix A, item #4: cache-hit history refresh splice\nBranch `perf/history-refresh-splice`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-history-splice`.\n\n**Today.** Every full-profile cache hit reruns `git log -256` and fully re-sorts ALL relations with a string-concat comparator. That costs 172-184 ms, and it is why warm def/neighbors/impact regressed from 0.45 s to 0.66 s on cli and brain. It was added in a902231f / 07c7d0fe (2026-10-16). The rationale is in the ADR 0002 addendum and search_cache.go:1345-1385.\n\n**Reviewer verdict:**\n- Memoizing per commit is UNSAFE: a shallow deepen changes history for the same commit. It is also useless per process. Do NOT memoize.\n- Instead SPLICE: FILE_CHANGES_WITH relations are contiguous (no relation type is a prefix of another), and keys are unique after dedupeRelations (provider.go:28963). So replace that contiguous block in place, and skip the whole step when history is unchanged.\n\n**TRAP.** Any allocation-free comparator must emulate the CONCAT order exactly. A tuple compare reorders prefix IDs (Foo vs FooBar) and changes bytes. See also provider.go:1065 and 4633.\n\n**Saving:** −0.15 to −0.18 s per warm full-profile op.\n\n**Proof:**\n- byte-identical def/neighbors/impact/snapshot output, base vs new, on cli + entire-brain (after `g2-strip.py`);\n- a test with history that changes between two hits (proves the splice is correct);\n- a test with unchanged history (proves the skip);\n- a test with Foo/FooBar-style prefix IDs;\n- each weakened to red.\n\n## Fix B, item #5: stop persisting the derived selective view on every novel warm query\nBranch `perf/skip-selective-view-persist`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-selective-view`.\n\n**Reviewer verdict (CONFIRMED):**\n- the write is at search_cache.go:378-382;\n- its only reader is the identical OnlyFiles key at :351-357;\n- derive already returns hit=true;\n- the diagnostic header is the same (search.go:2134).\n\n**Saving:** −0.5 to −0.7 s per novel warm query, with repeat queries about neutral. MEASURE BOTH: a novel query and the same query repeated. If repeats regress materially, say so and consider persisting only on the second sighting of a key, but only if that is simple.\n\nThree tests are expected to need rewriting: `search_cache_force_test`, `cache_generation_marker_test`, `search_cache_test`. Rewrite them to pin the new behaviour. Do not just delete assertions.\n\nOutput: stripped JSON byte-identical base vs new.\n\n## Report\nFor BOTH PRs: number, medians (warm def/neighbors/impact for A; novel + repeat warm query for B), identity, weakening proof, and CI enumerated green/failed/running."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":340385,"output_tokens":5395,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1064},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5395,"cache_read_input_tokens":340385,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CEBVhHuzCJxEdHfaGUsvJt":{"description":"G3-4/5: history splice + selective view","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement TWO entire-graph speed fixes as two separate open PRs, each in its own worktree off origin/main. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock` for timing and long tests, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch files in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK. Both fixes touch search_cache.go, so keep each diff minimal and on a different hunk to keep merge conflicts small.\n\nRead rows #4, #5 and #10 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n## Fix A, item #4: cache-hit history refresh splice\nBranch `perf/history-refresh-splice`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-history-splice`.\n\n**Today.** Every full-profile cache hit reruns `git log -256` and fully re-sorts ALL relations with a string-concat comparator. That costs 172-184 ms, and it is why warm def/neighbors/impact regressed from 0.45 s to 0.66 s on cli and brain. It was added in a902231f / 07c7d0fe (2026-10-16). The rationale is in the ADR 0002 addendum and search_cache.go:1345-1385.\n\n**Reviewer verdict:**\n- Memoizing per commit is UNSAFE: a shallow deepen changes history for the same commit. It is also useless per process. Do NOT memoize.\n- Instead SPLICE: FILE_CHANGES_WITH relations are contiguous (no relation type is a prefix of another), and keys are unique after dedupeRelations (provider.go:28963). So replace that contiguous block in place, and skip the whole step when history is unchanged.\n\n**TRAP.** Any allocation-free comparator must emulate the CONCAT order exactly. A tuple compare reorders prefix IDs (Foo vs FooBar) and changes bytes. See also provider.go:1065 and 4633.\n\n**Saving:** −0.15 to −0.18 s per warm full-profile op.\n\n**Proof:**\n- byte-identical def/neighbors/impact/snapshot output, base vs new, on cli + entire-brain (after `g2-strip.py`);\n- a test with history that changes between two hits (proves the splice is correct);\n- a test with unchanged history (proves the skip);\n- a test with Foo/FooBar-style prefix IDs;\n- each weakened to red.\n\n## Fix B, item #5: stop persisting the derived selective view on every novel warm query\nBranch `perf/skip-selective-view-persist`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-selective-view`.\n\n**Reviewer verdict (CONFIRMED):**\n- the write is at search_cache.go:378-382;\n- its only reader is the identical OnlyFiles key at :351-357;\n- derive already returns hit=true;\n- the diagnostic header is the same (search.go:2134).\n\n**Saving:** −0.5 to −0.7 s per novel warm query, with repeat queries about neutral. MEASURE BOTH: a novel query and the same query repeated. If repeats regress materially, say so and consider persisting only on the second sighting of a key, but only if that is simple.\n\nThree tests are expected to need rewriting: `search_cache_force_test`, `cache_generation_marker_test`, `search_cache_test`. Rewrite them to pin the new behaviour. Do not just delete assertions.\n\nOutput: stripped JSON byte-identical base vs new.\n\n## Report\nFor BOTH PRs: number, medians (warm def/neighbors/impact for A; novel + repeat warm query for B), identity, weakening proof, and CI enumerated green/failed/running."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"22ceceec-75cc-4851-b0c4-912db93b1aab","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgMgzpkgjCr1HopLakh8j","requestRef":"fcec0e49-d034-4997-9edb-2352581071c9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6ba1f0ab-3e9a-4918-a227-6c55746eeb5e","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:26:45.885Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"6ba1f0ab-3e9a-4918-a227-6c55746eeb5e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMgzq7zytievvwfCMG3r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KvS9FmWZszhbM6LL4fpcuB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-3: cold query uses warm preselection","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed + consistency fix as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: graph/brain-first, `mlock` for timing and long tests, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch files in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #3: a cold query uses the same preselection as a warm one\nRead rows #3 and N3 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Today.**\n- A cold query first runs a go-content preselect scan (`scoreSearchPaths`; 4.2 s on cli, 6.3 s on brain), then builds the complete snapshot anyway.\n- Preselect output feeds OnlyFiles/rank scope, sparse handling, termPostings/IDF and stats (search.go:1351-1412), so skipping it is NOT free.\n- **Cold and warm answers differ TODAY** (N3, pre-existing). On cli query q1, cold go-content picks 384 files / 5 results, while warm git-tree-grep picks 1,418 files / 6 results, and the 5th result differs.\n\n**The fix the reviewer endorses.** When the cold path will build the complete snapshot anyway, use the warm git-tree-grep selection (search_cache.go:434) instead of the go-content scan. Then:\n- cold == warm, byte for byte after `g2-strip.py`;\n- a 0-hit query still does not build.\n\nSaving: about −3.9 s per first query on cli, about −5.5 s on brain, net of the larger rank set.\n\n**This MUST land after #1** (PR #371, branch `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`): without #1, a cold alias query would inherit the 355 s grep. So **stack it**:\n- worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-cold-preselect`, new branch `perf/cold-query-warm-preselect`, created from `origin/perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths` (fetch it first);\n- open the PR with `--base perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`, and say in the body that it is stacked on #371.\n\n## Done means\n- **Base vs new**, cold first query on cli + entire-brain + entire-graph, 3 reps, fresh cache dir per run. Base = the #371 branch tip, not main, so only this change is measured.\n- **Identity:** new cold == new warm (stripped JSON) for each query. Report how the cold output changed vs base (expected: it now matches warm).\n- **Tests:**\n  - a cold==warm test (N3, pinned in its own test);\n  - a 0-hit no-build test;\n  - each weakened to red.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":340385,"output_tokens":5395,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1064},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5395,"cache_read_input_tokens":340385,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01KvS9FmWZszhbM6LL4fpcuB":{"description":"G3-3: cold query uses warm preselection","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph speed + consistency fix as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: graph/brain-first, `mlock` for timing and long tests, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch files in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item #3: a cold query uses the same preselection as a warm one\nRead rows #3 and N3 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Today.**\n- A cold query first runs a go-content preselect scan (`scoreSearchPaths`; 4.2 s on cli, 6.3 s on brain), then builds the complete snapshot anyway.\n- Preselect output feeds OnlyFiles/rank scope, sparse handling, termPostings/IDF and stats (search.go:1351-1412), so skipping it is NOT free.\n- **Cold and warm answers differ TODAY** (N3, pre-existing). On cli query q1, cold go-content picks 384 files / 5 results, while warm git-tree-grep picks 1,418 files / 6 results, and the 5th result differs.\n\n**The fix the reviewer endorses.** When the cold path will build the complete snapshot anyway, use the warm git-tree-grep selection (search_cache.go:434) instead of the go-content scan. Then:\n- cold == warm, byte for byte after `g2-strip.py`;\n- a 0-hit query still does not build.\n\nSaving: about −3.9 s per first query on cli, about −5.5 s on brain, net of the larger rank set.\n\n**This MUST land after #1** (PR #371, branch `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`): without #1, a cold alias query would inherit the 355 s grep. So **stack it**:\n- worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-cold-preselect`, new branch `perf/cold-query-warm-preselect`, created from `origin/perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths` (fetch it first);\n- open the PR with `--base perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`, and say in the body that it is stacked on #371.\n\n## Done means\n- **Base vs new**, cold first query on cli + entire-brain + entire-graph, 3 reps, fresh cache dir per run. Base = the #371 branch tip, not main, so only this change is measured.\n- **Identity:** new cold == new warm (stripped JSON) for each query. Report how the cold output changed vs base (expected: it now matches warm).\n- **Tests:**\n  - a cold==warm test (N3, pinned in its own test);\n  - a 0-hit no-build test;\n  - each weakened to red.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"22ceceec-75cc-4851-b0c4-912db93b1aab","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgMgzpkgjCr1HopLakh8j","requestRef":"fcec0e49-d034-4997-9edb-2352581071c9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6bde9369-5c2e-4122-b66f-8dcbc6af8ca3","timestamp":"2026-10-24T20:26:54.886Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"6bde9369-5c2e-4122-b66f-8dcbc6af8ca3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMgzq7zytievvwfCMG3r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TNHhFgVTqv7Jp8fqFPPQse","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-C2: tool-handler heuristic fix","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph correctness fix as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock` for long tests and cold builds, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch files in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item C2: spurious `kind=tool` symbols from the tool-handler heuristic\nRead row C2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Today.**\n- `looksLikeToolHandler` (provider.go:28824) uses a bag of tokens that INCLUDES string literals. So a function whose vocabulary contains \"tool\" and \"schema\" (for example entire-brain's `historyTerms`, history.go:2442) is emitted as a synthetic `kind=tool` symbol via syntheticBoundarySymbols (:2181).\n- That makes `impact`/`def` ambiguous (a duplicate definition).\n- Counts: entire-brain 56 tool symbols, entire-graph 22 (SymbolRecord, searchRepository, main, tests…), cli 5. The reviewer estimates at most 2 are genuine.\n\n**Fix direction:** decide on identifier-only tokens, a real registration signal (for example an MCP/tool registration call, or a handler signature), or both. Then:\n- run `entire brain recall` and `git log -S looksLikeToolHandler` first, to learn what genuine cases it was built for;\n- keep every genuine case;\n- run `entire graph impact` on `looksLikeToolHandler` and on syntheticBoundarySymbols.\n\n**This changes output intentionally.**\n- Produce a per-repo table (entire-brain, entire-graph, cli, entiredb clones in `timing/repos/`) of tool symbols before vs after, each one classified genuine or false. Put it in the PR body.\n- Check whether the snapshot/cache identity needs a version bump so stale caches don't keep the old symbols. Find how producer changes invalidate caches (identity_revision / schema), and follow the existing convention.\n\n## Done means\n- Tests:\n  - historyTerms-style false positive gone;\n  - genuine handler kept;\n  - each weakened to red.\n- `entire graph def historyTerms` (via `bin/new`, fresh cache) on entire-brain is no longer ambiguous.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch `fix/tool-handler-heuristic`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-tool-heuristic`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_read_input_tokens":340385,"output_tokens":5395,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1064},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5395,"cache_read_input_tokens":340385,"cache_creation_input_tokens":473,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":473},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TNHhFgVTqv7Jp8fqFPPQse":{"description":"G3-C2: tool-handler heuristic fix","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph correctness fix as one open PR. First read `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` and follow it exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock` for long tests and cold builds, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch files in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Item C2: spurious `kind=tool` symbols from the tool-handler heuristic\nRead row C2 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` in full first.\n\n**Today.**\n- `looksLikeToolHandler` (provider.go:28824) uses a bag of tokens that INCLUDES string literals. So a function whose vocabulary contains \"tool\" and \"schema\" (for example entire-brain's `historyTerms`, history.go:2442) is emitted as a synthetic `kind=tool` symbol via syntheticBoundarySymbols (:2181).\n- That makes `impact`/`def` ambiguous (a duplicate definition).\n- Counts: entire-brain 56 tool symbols, entire-graph 22 (SymbolRecord, searchRepository, main, tests…), cli 5. The reviewer estimates at most 2 are genuine.\n\n**Fix direction:** decide on identifier-only tokens, a real registration signal (for example an MCP/tool registration call, or a handler signature), or both. Then:\n- run `entire brain recall` and `git log -S looksLikeToolHandler` first, to learn what genuine cases it was built for;\n- keep every genuine case;\n- run `entire graph impact` on `looksLikeToolHandler` and on syntheticBoundarySymbols.\n\n**This changes output intentionally.**\n- Produce a per-repo table (entire-brain, entire-graph, cli, entiredb clones in `timing/repos/`) of tool symbols before vs after, each one classified genuine or false. Put it in the PR body.\n- Check whether the snapshot/cache identity needs a version bump so stale caches don't keep the old symbols. Find how producer changes invalidate caches (identity_revision / schema), and follow the existing convention.\n\n## Done means\n- Tests:\n  - historyTerms-style false positive gone;\n  - genuine handler kept;\n  - each weakened to red.\n- `entire graph def historyTerms` (via `bin/new`, fresh cache) on entire-brain is no longer ambiguous.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol.\n\nBranch `fix/tool-handler-heuristic`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-tool-heuristic`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"