{"parentUuid":"d147c583-ce4b-4867-bd11-db50db36495d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMh4W58zxGpidAr1omVh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The pipeline-speedup PR, [#373](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/373), is open. Its final numbers (middle of three runs, old vs new build back to back):\n\n| Repo | Cold index before | After | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| cli | 12.2 s | 8.8 s | −28% |\n| entire-brain | 16.2 s | 10.4 s | −35% |\n| entire-graph | 10.8 s | 7.5 s | −30% |\n| entiredb | 13.6 s | 9.5 s | −30% |\n\n- **Same output:** the index is byte-identical on all four repos, and warm queries are no slower.\n- **Tested:** all nine deliberate breakages fail their tests.\n- **CI:** nothing has failed. 15 checks pass and the main test runs are still going.\n\nOne warm query on entire-brain takes 51 s on both the old and new builds. That's the alias-search problem #371 fixes, and with it the same kind of query dropped from 52 s to 9.6 s.\n\n**Wave 2 is now running, three agents:**\n- the history-cache fix plus the \"stop writing a derived file on every new question\" fix, as two separate PRs;\n- making the first query in a repo use the same file selection as later ones, which saves about 4–5 s and makes first and later answers identical (stacked on #371);\n- the tool-detection bug that creates about 54 false \"tool\" symbols on entire-brain."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9241,"cache_read_input_tokens":340858,"output_tokens":570,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":89},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9241,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":570,"cache_read_input_tokens":340858,"cache_creation_