{"parentUuid":"2172d230-497c-499e-b2b1-55b2c82f948f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMticzT2spnTvKRWfhvW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[#377](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/377) is open, stacked on #371, so #371 has to merge first.\n\n| First query in a repo | Change |\n|---|---|\n| cli | 2.8 s faster |\n| entire-brain | 3.3–3.9 s faster |\n| entire-graph (plain query) | 2.5 s faster |\n| any repo, no results | 1.7 s faster |\n| entire-graph, alias query (\"Repository\") | **0.8 s slower** |\n\n- **What changed:** a repo's first query now gives exactly the same answer as later ones. Before, the first answer differed in 20 to 59 fields.\n- **Why one query got slower:** that query was already cheap, and it now pays the same cost its later repeats always paid. A faster alias route on warm queries would fix both. That's a possible follow-up, not a blocker.\n- **Checks:** five deliberate breakages each fail a test, and the full package tests pass locally. CI is partly through, with nothing failed so far. I told the agent to stop watching CI, which saves usage; I'm tracking it myself.\n\nThe other two wave-2 agents are still running: the history cache plus derived-file write, and the tool detection fix."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":380585,"output_tokens":401,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":401,"cache_read_input_tokens":380585,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":335},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fall