{"parentUuid":"410364dd-a36f-4e91-a5f2-adede708801a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMuF6WkgDivR2dNivQHK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014m9CYaTCrnU6WyuayZ5T3s","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,60p /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md","description":"Read the trail finding pitfalls memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":373,"cache_read_input_tokens":391513,"output_tokens":138,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":373,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":138,"cache_read_input_tokens":391513,"cache_creation_input_tokens":373,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":373},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014m9CYaTCrnU6WyuayZ5T3s":{"command":"sed -n 1,60p /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls.md","description":"Read the trail finding pitfalls memory"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"b08d3b85-b208-48c2-8daa-e254bc4bc077","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgMuF69BEi2pgrcZQuGqW","requestRef":"f8c86992-1421-4337-841e-26eec4f385e6","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c5c2452-a15d-4cdb-ad3e-7bc163ef14dd","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:06:54.715Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"9c5c2452-a15d-4cdb-ad3e-7bc163ef14dd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d6b1d054-6323-43b9-9fce-5b62c16ffa5d","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014m9CYaTCrnU6WyuayZ5T3s","type":"tool_result","content":"---\nname: trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls\ndescription: \"Two ways a finding sweep silently reports zero: scoping to the trails you happen to be working, and grepping ^01M when the CLI indents its IDs — use --json\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37\n  modified: 2026-09-04T06:00:35.108Z\n---\n\nReporting \"0 open findings\" twice in one session when the real count was **142** cost\ncredibility both times. Two independent causes, both silent:\n\n1. **Scope.** I swept only the ~15 trails I had been working. Findings live on *every*\n   trail, including ones whose PRs merged months ago — and those matter more, because they\n   describe defects already on `main`. Sweep the full trail-number range, both repos.\n2. **Parsing.** `entire trail finding list` **indents** its rows, so\n   `grep -cE \"^01M\"` matches nothing and prints a confident `0`. The correct filter is\n   `grep -cE \"^[[:space:]]+01M.*open\"`, and better still `--json` — the human table also\n   wraps long `LOCATION` values, which silently corrupts column-based `awk`.\n\nAlso: `--repo` requires an explicit trail selector, so `finding show <id>` alone fails —\nkeep the trail number paired with every id. Default `--freshness` is `current`; stale\nfindings are hidden unless asked for.\n\n**A third silent zero, found 2026-10-04:** the findings sub-gate can read zero because\n**no agent review has ever run for the current head** — its summary says so in words\n(`No agent review has run for the current head`), but the sub-gate still reads as not-failing,\nso a sweep sees a clean PR that was never reviewed. The driver's `action` field caught it\n(`retrigger_gate`). An empty `chore:` push made the review run; it posted a medium finding\nwithin 20 minutes. The inverse trap fired on the same PR immediately after: the new gate read\n`Findings: passed` while that finding was open, because the review posted *after* the check\ncompleted. **Both gate readings were wrong, in opposite directions, on one PR inside 20\nminutes. Only `trail finding list` was right.**\n\n**A fourth, worse one — stale local worktrees.** Before merging main forward, check the\nworktree against its OWN PR head, not just against main: one worktree here was **76 commits\nbehind `origin/<its-own-branch>`** (0 ahead). Merging main from that tree and pushing would\nhave silently reverted the PR's own work with no conflict and a green build.\n`git merge --ff-only origin/<branch>` first, every time.\n\n**Why:** all of these produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\nprompts a re-check. This is the [[mechanism-endpoint-caught-a-false-headline]] shape — the\nnumber moved the way I wanted, so I stopped looking.\n\n**How to apply:** derive counts from `--json`, sweep the whole range, and before reporting\na zero, verify the pipeline on a trail *known* to have findings. State the scope of any\ncount out loud (\"trails 1-210, both repos\"), so a scoped number can never read as a global\none. Related: [[per-loser-forensics-doctrine]], [[reproduce-proven-results-doctrine]].","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"bb690026-73db-40a9-ad25-544c298dab49","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:06:55.838Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"---\nname: trail-finding-sweep-pitfalls\ndescription: \"Two ways a finding sweep silently reports zero: scoping to the trails you happen to be working, and grepping ^01M when the CLI indents its IDs — use --json\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 27642e0f-a981-4143-aea0-6f4f8cb34d37\n  modified: 2026-09-04T06:00:35.108Z\n---\n\nReporting \"0 open findings\" twice in one session when the real count was **142** cost\ncredibility both times. Two independent causes, both silent:\n\n1. **Scope.** I swept only the ~15 trails I had been working. Findings live on *every*\n   trail, including ones whose PRs merged months ago — and those matter more, because they\n   describe defects already on `main`. Sweep the full trail-number range, both repos.\n2. **Parsing.** `entire trail finding list` **indents** its rows, so\n   `grep -cE \"^01M\"` matches nothing and prints a confident `0`. The correct filter is\n   `grep -cE \"^[[:space:]]+01M.*open\"`, and better still `--json` — the human table also\n   wraps long `LOCATION` values, which silently corrupts column-based `awk`.\n\nAlso: `--repo` requires an explicit trail selector, so `finding show <id>` alone fails —\nkeep the trail number paired with every id. Default `--freshness` is `current`; stale\nfindings are hidden unless asked for.\n\n**A third silent zero, found 2026-10-04:** the findings sub-gate can read zero because\n**no agent review has ever run for the current head** — its summary says so in words\n(`No agent review has run for the current head`), but the sub-gate still reads as not-failing,\nso a sweep sees a clean PR that was never reviewed. The driver's `action` field caught it\n(`retrigger_gate`). An empty `chore:` push made the review run; it posted a medium finding\nwithin 20 minutes. The inverse trap fired on the same PR immediately after: the new gate read\n`Findings: passed` while that finding was open, because the review posted *after* the check\ncompleted. **Both gate readings were wrong, in opposite directions, on one PR inside 20\nminutes. Only `trail finding list` was right.**\n\n**A fourth, worse one — stale local worktrees.** Before merging main forward, check the\nworktree against its OWN PR head, not just against main: one worktree here was **76 commits\nbehind `origin/<its-own-branch>`** (0 ahead). Merging main from that tree and pushing would\nhave silently reverted the PR's own work with no conflict and a green build.\n`git merge --ff-only origin/<branch>` first, every time.\n\n**Why:** all of these produce a *plausible* clean result rather than an error, so nothing\nprompts a re-check. This is the [[mechanism-endpoint-caught-a-false-headline]] shape — the\nnumber moved the way I wanted, so I stopped looking.\n\n**How to apply:** derive counts from `--json`, sweep the whole range, and before reporting\na zero, verify the pipeline on a trail *known* to have findings. State the scope of any\ncount out loud (\"trails 1-210, both repos\"), so a scoped number can never read as a global\none. Related: [[per-loser-forensics-doctrine]], [[reproduce-proven-results-doctrine]].","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"b08d3b85-b208-48c2-8daa-e254bc4bc077","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"entireio","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"},{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9c5c2452-a15d-4cdb-ad3e-7bc163ef14dd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-5