{"parentUuid":"081e909e-f457-4a27-9c50-6d57a4f38d09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMuJ9omzpJwM136Ktbs2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019K1RTxZJGBo3dTLWXwVASC","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G-142: rescope wall-clock PR","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You rescope ONE existing entire-graph PR: #142 (`security/enforce-wall-clock-budget`, \"fix(sem,cli): enforce a wall-clock ceiling on indexing\"). It is open and mergeable; another session just resolved its conflicts against main and handed it back. Follow `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` exactly (graph/brain-first, `mlock`, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch in the worktree, report format), EXCEPT that you work on #142's existing branch instead of a fresh one. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Workspace\n- `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin security/enforce-wall-clock-budget main`\n- `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph worktree add /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-142-rescope origin/security/enforce-wall-clock-budget`, then `git switch -c` a local branch that tracks it.\n- **Check that the worktree is at the PR's own head** (`git rev-parse HEAD` == `gh pr view 142 --json headRefOid`) before touching anything. A stale worktree once silently reverted a PR's own work.\n- Push new commits to the same branch. **Never force-push.**\n\n## Rescope (decided earlier; do exactly this)\n- **DROP:**\n  - the `--max-seconds` flag and the wall-clock ceiling;\n  - the partial-snapshot path. A run that hits a time limit must not write or serve a partial snapshot.\n- **KEEP:**\n  - **cancellation**: context cancellation propagates and a cancelled run stops cleanly;\n  - **`refuseTruncatedSnapshot` in ALL THREE snapshot writers**, plus `TestEverySearchSnapshotWriterRefusesATruncatedSnapshot`;\n  - **the `filterActive` guard**;\n  - **the TestTF142R6 allowlist entry** for `readSearchSnapshotPreferringStore`.\n\nBefore deleting anything:\n- run `entire graph impact` on each symbol you remove or change, and cite each one;\n- run `entire brain recall` on #142's history (why a wall-clock ceiling, and why it is being dropped);\n- read the PR's own discussion: `gh pr view 142 --comments` and `gh pr diff 142`.\n\nUpdate the PR title and body to match the rescoped change. The title must no longer promise a wall-clock ceiling. Say plainly what was dropped and why: a partial snapshot is a correctness hazard, and the alias-grep, pipeline and partial-clone fixes (#371-#373) removed the slow paths that motivated it.\n\n## Done means\n- `go build ./...` passes.\n- Focused tests pass, then `internal/sem` with `-parallel 4 -timeout 40m -p 1` under mlock. Run the focused ones with `-race`.\n- Weakening, each red then restored:\n  - (a) remove `refuseTruncatedSnapshot` from one writer → `TestEverySearchSnapshotWriterRefusesATruncatedSnapshot` goes red;\n  - (b) break cancellation → a cancellation test goes red;\n  - (c) drop the filterActive guard → red.\n- Confirm no leftover reference to `--max-seconds` in docs, help text or the changelog. Use grep for the text occurrences.\n- Push, then watch CI to a result. Address any Entire Gates findings.\n- Report per the protocol: commits added, symbols removed/kept with their impact results, weakening proof, CI enumerated."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1778,"cache_read_input_tokens":394342,"output_tokens":2816,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1778,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2816,"cache_read_input_tokens":394342,