{"parentUuid":"f84508b1-cf00-43b2-9639-bc0c6ed722a7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMuJ9omzpJwM136Ktbs2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01T1uJGXKFrNUHbp2NNwNS1A","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G3-C1: disclose unmodelled references","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph correctness fix (disclosure of two silent gaps) as one open PR. Follow `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock`, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\nBranch `fix/disclose-unmodelled-references`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-disclose-refs`.\n\nRead row C1 of `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-SPEEDUPS-REVIEW.md` first.\n\n## Gap 1 (C1): function-value references are not modelled, and `neighbors`/`impact` stay silent about it\n- **Example.** In entire-brain, `var openHistoryFTSForRanking = openHistoryFTS` (history_fts.go:824). `entire graph neighbors --symbol openHistoryFTS --direction in` reports 4 test callers and 0 production callers, which is wrong.\n- **Root cause.** `entityFromNode` (parser.go:5663) has no Go `var_spec`/`const_spec` handling, so package-level vars are never symbols, and there is no REFERENCES relation type. A real fix (var symbols plus REFERENCES) needs a schema/cache bump and is OUT OF SCOPE.\n- **What to do now:** make the gap visible where an agent reads the answer.\n  - When `neighbors` (direction in) and `impact` results are rendered, add a disclosure stating that references to the symbol as a value (assigned to a var, passed as an argument, stored in a struct or map) are not modelled.\n  - Include a self-check the reader can run: `grep -rn '<Symbol>[^(a-zA-Z0-9_]'`; any non-comment hit that is not a call is a value reference the graph cannot see.\n  - Find the existing disclosure/warning mechanism. Look at how `--format agent` emits VERIFY lines and coverage warnings, and how JSON carries warnings. Reuse it. Do not invent a new channel.\n  - Keep it SHORT; agent output is byte-budgeted.\n  - It is better to emit it only when it could matter, e.g. only for Go function or method symbols. Check whether the budget accounting (`--max-context-bytes`) charges for it, and keep the existing budget tests green.\n- Run `entire graph impact` on the render functions you touch.\n\n## Gap 2: co-change history silently dropped\n- On a `blob:none` partial clone whose history has inexact renames, the co-change `git log --name-only` fails, and FILE_CHANGES_WITH relations are dropped with no warning. This is known from PR #372's body; read it with `gh pr view 372`.\n- When co-change collection fails, emit a warning in the index/snapshot warnings (the same mechanism as other `W_*` warnings) instead of dropping silently.\n- Add a test that forces the failure. A fixture or an injected git failure is fine; reuse #372's repack-without-blob fixture approach if it helps.\n\n## Done means\n- **Tests:**\n  - gap 1: the disclosure appears for a Go function symbol in both agent and JSON output, and stays within budget;\n  - gap 2: a co-change failure yields the warning;\n  - each weakened to red and then restored.\n- **Live check:** `bin/new graph neighbors --repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain --head --symbol openHistoryFTS --direction in --format agent` (fresh cache dir, under mlock) shows the disclosure. That repo is a main checkout: read-only use only.\n- **Golden files:** if goldens exist for agent output, regenerate them deliberately and explain the diff in the PR.\n- PR open, CI watched, and the report per the protocol."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1778,"cache_read_input_tokens":394342,"output_tokens":281