{"parentUuid":"2fcf0c56-a36e-44a0-a4ef-cf28daeb6ddb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMuLKsKs9U5JgtBmjgGU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two more graph PRs are open, both with all CI checks passing and only the Approvals gate open:\n- **[#375](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/375), history cache:** warm `def`/`neighbors`/`impact` drops from about 0.62 s to 0.44–0.52 s, faster than the September build's 0.45 s.\n- **[#376](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/376), stop writing a derived file on every new question:** warm queries are 0.16–0.38 s faster, and repeated queries got faster too.\n\nOutputs are byte-identical in both.\n\n**The \"0 findings\" doubt.** I made sure the findings query itself works: an older trail correctly shows its 2 findings. Our trails show zero findings of any kind, and each gate says the review ran and found nothing blocking, so I believe the zeros. Reviews can post after the gate passes, so I'll recheck every trail right before handing you the merge list.\n\n**Now running:**\n- the tool-detection fix (wave 2);\n- **#142 rescope:** drop the time limit and the partial-snapshot path, but keep cancellation and the three \"refuse a truncated snapshot\" guards. The fixes so far removed the slow paths that limit was guarding against;\n- **disclose the two silent gaps:** `neighbors`/`impact` will say when references to a function used as a value aren't modelled, with a one-line grep to check; and indexing will warn instead of silently dropping \"files that change together\" data on some partial clones.\n\n**Status:** 7 graph PRs are open (#370–#373, #375–#377) and none has failed CI."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3646,"cache_read_input_tokens":396120,"output_tokens":539,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"we