ounts as a tool handler when it is a function/method/class/struct/type, not a test, not a predicate name (is/has/looks/should/can/must/needs), and one of:\n- its own name has `tool` plus handle/handler(s)/execute/executor/invoke/dispatch(er);\n- it is a bare action on a container whose head noun is `tool`/`tools` (`SearchTool.execute`);\n- its signature takes an MCP `CallToolRequest`.\n\n`call` and `schema` are not action words: `call` would flag tool-call data types, and a schema declares a tool rather than running one. `syntheticBoundarySymbols` no longer slices and tokenizes every symbol body.\n\nCache: bumped `provider-records` v21→v22 and `search-snapshot` v26→v27, following 5991211a; the sqlite store path moves with v27. Proved on entire-brain with a shared cache seeded by base: a no-bump build (via `-overlay`) still served `tool historyTerms`; with the bump it does not.\n\nTool symbols, base → new:\n| repo | before | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| brain | 56 | 1 |\n| eg | 22 | 0 |\n| cli | 5 | 2 |\n| entiredb | 1 | 0 |\n- Total 84 → 3. False positives 83 → 1; genuine handlers 1 → 2.\n- Kept genuine: brain `handleMCPToolCall`. Newly found genuine: cli `handleMCPToolCall`, which base missed.\n- Residual false positive: cli `handleLifecycleToolUse` (a hook handler). Its name has the same shape as a real `handleToolUse` executor, so names can't separate them. Disclosed in the PR.\n- Judgment call: brain `mcpToolDefinitions` (the reviewer's \"maybe\") is dropped. It declares tool schemas and handles no call.\n- The full classified table of all 86 rows is in the PR body.\n\nIdentity: full `symbols` and `edges` streams on all 4 repos, re-run on the final commit. After removing tool symbols and the edges touching them, the rest is byte-identical (sorted JSON). On brain the removed edges include 403 CALLS that hung off the fake symbols.\n\n`def historyTerms` and `impact historyTerms` (bin/new, fresh cache, entire-brain): one function, not ambiguous.\n\nTiming (secondary, not claimed): cold `symbols`, 3 interleaved reps, medians base→new.\n- brain 13.56→13.18 s\n- eg 9.97→9.83 s\n- cli 11.19→10.97 s\n- entiredb 11.82→11.36 s\n- New was faster in 10 of 12 pairs, but load1 was 14.2 at the start and 7.2 at the end, above the ceiling at the start. Indicative only.\n\nTests:\n- `TestToolBoundaryComesFromIdentifiersNotBodyText`: end to end; historyTerms-style fixture plus a genuine dispatcher, asserts one historyTerms definition and the dispatcher's tool + HANDLES_TOOL.\n- `TestLooksLikeToolHandler`: table test, 6 genuine and 12 false cases.\n- `TestIdentifierWords`.\n- Existing tool tests still green. Focused tests green with `-race` under mlock. Whole `internal/sem` package green locally (`-p 1`, 202 s).\n\nWeakening: 13 mutations, all red, each restored and checked with `git diff`.\n- old body heuristic OR-ed back in → `historyTerms definitions = [function tool]`\n- predicate, test-name, kind and CallToolRequest guards each removed; signature matched as substring\n- `handle` dropped from actions\n- 4 container-rule variants\n- acronym split broken\n- `call` added to actions\n- Failing lines are in the PR body.\n\nCI: 34 checks green, including test macos, ubuntu and windows. Entire Gates is red only on the Approvals sub-gate (no reviewers yet), which needs a human; Checks, Findings and Up-to-date pass. Nothing is running.\n\nGates review: 1 low finding (`ToolServer.handleHealth` would be flagged through the container). It was real: fixed in 0bc831e8 with tests and mutations, and the finding is resolved.\n- Resolving it with the installed `entire` (Aug 19 build) gave a 404, the known stale-CLI bug. I built a fresh CLI from cli main into `.g3/entire` to resolve it, then removed the temp cli worktree.\n\nNot done:\n- `brain remember`: skipped, because writes to the shared brain store are off-limits under the protocol.\n- No merge, approval or reviewer request.\n- Not covered, same as before: Python `@mcp.tool()` decorators and anonymous TS `server.tool()` callbacks. A follow-up would need registration-site detection.\n\nScratch files in the worktree (untracked):\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-tool-heuristic/.g3/table.md`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-tool-heuristic/.g3/pr-body-final.md`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-tool-heuristic/.g3/mutate.py`\n- `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-tool-heuristic/.g3/timing.out`"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
