{"parentUuid":"f18b86c3-aa35-4eeb-8b5c-9009e0d78275","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eccff0ee-9811-47a7-954f-dcafe005e2dc","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RiTs85gEg4TgixMw3GqPfa","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n \"id\": \"01M5R28EWN8CX2C6Y1Q2FGEPXC\",\n \"severity\": \"low\",\n \"status\": \"open\",\n \"title\": null,\n \"summary\": null,\n \"body\": \"`coldCompleteEligible` only mirrors some of the conditions under which `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting` builds the complete snapshot. It doesn't cover an unknown generation, an uncacheable-policy fallback, or a failed or invalid complete build. In those cases `preselectSearchFiles` uses the uncapped warm git-grep selection, but the build falls back to a selective one over every matched file (up to 3000), where the old content scan was bounded by the default pool. Consider keeping the bounded selection whenever the complete build isn't guaranteed to follow, or capping the grep result when it falls back.\",\n \"location\": {\n  \"id\": \"01M5R28EWNSNKYYXF85GHHBZ5Q\",\n  \"reviewCommentId\": \"01M5R28EWN8CX2C6Y1Q2FGEPXC\",\n  \"codeVersionId\": \"01M5R28EW6YXFTD5EV9WK95DRE\",\n  \"granularity\": \"line\",\n  \"filePath\": \"internal/sem/search.go\",\n  \"startLine\": 1227,\n  \"startColumn\": null,\n  \"endLine\": null,\n  \"endColumn\": null,\n  \"selectedText\": \"\\toptions.coldCompleteEligible = !preindexCacheHit && !options.Worktree && !searchCacheDisabled &&\",\n  \"nearbyText\": null,\n  \"language\": null\n },\n \"file\": null,\n \"path\": null,\n \"line\": null,\n \"description\": null\n}\n---\n#374 (repo 287): {'Open': 0, 'OpenHigh': 0, 'OpenMedium': 0, 'OpenLow': 0, 'Resolved': 0, 'Dismissed': 0, 'Stale': 0}\n## Summary\n\n`looksLikeToolHandler` decided whether a symbol is an agent-tool handler by tokenizing its **whole body, comments and string literals included**: `tool` plus any of `handler` / `execute` / `schema`. Every symbol it matched got a synthetic `kind=tool` symbol carrying the handler's own name, so `def`, `neighbors` and `impact` on that name came back ambiguous. For example, entire-brain's `historyTerms` has a stop-word list containing `\"tool\"` and `\"schema\"`, and `entire graph def historyTerms` returned a function **and** a tool. The same happened to `looksLikeToolHandler` itself, `syntheticBoundarySymbols`, `SymbolRecord` (through its field comments) and `main` in this repo. Across four of our own repositories, 84 tool symbols were emitted and one was a real handler.\n\nThe decision now reads only identifiers: the symbol's name, qualified name and signature. Its body is never read. A symbol is a tool handler when it is a function, method, class, struct or type, is not a test, is not named as a predicate (`is…`, `has…`, `looks…`, `should…`, `can…`, `must…`, `needs…`), and either:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5632a72f-7da2-4682-aeba-6ffb4589855a","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:17:53.339Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"{\n \"id\": \"01M5R28EWN8CX2C6Y1Q2FGEPXC\",\n \"severity\": \"low\",\n \"status\": \"open\",\n \"title\": null,\n \"summary\": null,\n \"body\": \"`coldCompleteEligible` only mirrors some of the conditions under which `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting` builds the complete snapshot. It doesn't cover an unknown generation, an uncacheable-policy fallback, or a failed or invalid complete build. In those cases `preselectSearchFiles` uses the uncapped warm git-grep selection, but the build falls back to a selective one over every matched file (up to 3000), where the old content scan was bounded by the default pool. Consider keeping the bounded selection whenever the complete build isn't guaranteed to follow, or capping the grep result when it falls back.\",\n \"location\": {\n  \"id\": \"01M5R28EWNSNKYYXF85GHHBZ5Q\",\n  \"reviewCommentId\": \"01M5R28EWN8CX2C6Y1Q2FGEPXC\",\n  \"codeVersionId\": \"01M5R28EW6YXFTD5EV9WK95DRE\",\n  \"granularity\": \"line\",\n  \"filePath\": \"internal/sem/search.go\",\n