-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"c2856614-4da3-48c2-a509-7d24aa32ce9c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMv5sHPn2HgGRqMjgw5Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P4otQwGSa9SyHrtn5Qe1n2","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a390d327408305b2f","summary":"Fix open review finding on #377","message":"#377 has an open LOW review finding. It's real and needs a fix before handoff. Finding `01M5R28EWN8CX2C6Y1Q2FGEPXC`, at internal/sem/search.go:1227 (`options.coldCompleteEligible = ...`):\n\n> `coldCompleteEligible` only mirrors some of the conditions under which `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting` builds the complete snapshot. It doesn't cover an unknown generation, an uncacheable-policy fallback, or a failed or invalid complete build. In those cases `preselectSearchFiles` uses the uncapped warm git-grep selection, but the build falls back to a selective one over every matched file (up to 3000), where the old content scan was bounded by the default pool.\n\nFix it. Prefer whichever is exact and simple, and justify the choice in the PR:\n- (a) Derive eligibility from the same decision the builder uses, so the two can't drift; for example, compute the decision once and pass it down. That's the \"logic in the call site\" trap.\n- (b) Keep the bounded content-scan selection whenever the complete build isn't guaranteed.\n- (c) Cap the grep result on the fallback path.\n\nTests, each weakened to red and then restored:\n- each fallback case (unknown generation, uncacheable policy, failed or invalid complete build) keeps a bounded selection;\n- the cold==warm parity still holds on the normal path.\n\nRe-run your focused tests with `-race` and the sem package under mlock, push to the same branch, and watch CI.\n\n**Resolving the finding.** The installed CLI at `~/.local/bin/entire` is now a fresh build of cli main (e7c03937). It addresses findings by the **org-level trail number**, which is **2516** for #377 (from the PR body link `trails/2516/changes/entire-graph/290`), NOT 290:\n- `entire trail finding list 2516 --json`\n- `entire trail finding resolve 2516 <id> ...`; check `entire agent-help trail finding` for the exact flags.\n\nResolve the finding only after the fix is pushed, and say how it was fixed. Report when CI has a result.","type":"message","recipient":"a390d327408305b2f","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"#377 has an open LOW review finding. It's real an…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1636,"cache_read_input_tokens":410086,"output_tokens":2498,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":478},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1636,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2498,"cache_read_input_tokens":410086,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1636,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1636},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01P4otQwGSa9SyHrtn5Qe1n2":{"to":"a390d327408305b2f","summary":"Fix open review finding on #377","message":"#377 has an open LOW review finding. It's real and needs a fix before handoff. Finding `01M5R28EWN8CX2C6Y1Q2FGEPXC`, at internal/sem/search.go:1227 (`options.coldCompleteEligible = ...`):\n\n> `coldCompleteEligible` only mirrors some of the conditions under which `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting` builds the complete snapshot. It doesn't cover an unknown generation, an uncacheable-policy fallback, or a failed or invalid complete build. In those cases `preselectSearchFiles` uses the uncapped warm git-grep selection, but the build falls back to a selective one over every matched file (up to 3000), where the old content scan was bounded by the default pool.\n\nFix it. Prefer whichever is exact and simple, and justify the choice in the PR:\n- (a) Derive eligibility from the same decision the builder uses, so the two can't drift; for example, compute the decision once and pass it down. That's the \"logic in the call site\" trap.\n- (b) Keep the bounded content-scan selection whenever the complete build isn't guaranteed.\n- (c) Cap the grep result on the fallback path.\n\nTests, each weakened to red and then restored:\n- each fallback case (unknown generation, uncacheable policy, failed or invalid complete build) keeps a bounded selection;\n- the cold==warm parity still holds on the normal path.\n\nRe-run your focused tests with `-race` and the sem package under mlock, push to the same branch, and watch CI.\n\n**Resolving the finding.** The installed CLI at `~/.local/bin/entire` is now a fresh build of cli main (e7c03937). It addresses findings by the **org-level trail number**, which is **2516** for #377 (from the PR body link `trails/2516/changes/entire-graph/290`), NOT 290:\n- `entire trail finding list 2516 --json`\n- `entire trail finding resolve 2516 <id> ...`; check `entire agent-help trail finding` for the exact flags.\n\nResolve the finding only after the fix is pushed, and say how it was fixed. Report when CI has a result."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"c2def140-6177-434b-838d-b9b6cfaaab32","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMv5rv4Ec97DcV2Ffbvb","requestRef":"2e414b37-286f-4209-92f0-3b6212113cee","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3d7f9e3a-b192-43d9-b21c-fce47f65f6cb","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:18:08.610Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"l