{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"8d9e629f12f2422a4a1b2f1d8d179af9cbd4be53c28a3328119ab0018f3fd834","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed: #377's fallback paths (unknown cache generation or failed build) now pull from an uncapped list of up to 3,000 files instead of the old capped scan, which could slow those rare cases. I'm resuming the agent to fix this and logging the trail-number trap in the protocol.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01P4otQwGSa9SyHrtn5Qe1n2","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a390d327408305b2f","summary":"Fix open review finding on #377","message":"#377 has an open LOW review finding. It's real and needs a fix before handoff. Finding `01M5R28EWN8CX2C6Y1Q2FGEPXC`, at internal/sem/search.go:1227 (`options.coldCompleteEligible = ...`):\n\n> `coldCompleteEligible` only mirrors some of the conditions under which `loadOrBuildSearchSnapshotPersisting` builds the complete snapshot. It doesn't cover an unknown generation, an uncacheable-policy fallback, or a failed or invalid complete build. In those cases `preselectSearchFiles` uses the uncapped warm git-grep selection, but the build falls back to a selective one over every matched file (up to 3000), where the old content scan was bounded by the default pool.\n\nFix it. Prefer whichever is exact and simple, and justify the choice in the PR:\n- (a) Derive eligibility from the same decision the builder uses, so the two can't drift; for example, compute the decision once and pass it down. That's the \"logic in the call site\" trap.\n- (b) Keep the bounded content-scan selection whenever the complete build isn't guaranteed.\n- (c) Cap the grep result on the fallback path.\n\nTests, each weakened to red and then restored:\n- each fallback case (unknown generation, uncacheable policy, failed or invalid complete build) keeps a bounded selection;\n- the cold==warm parity still holds on the normal path.\n\nRe-run your focused tests with `-race` and the sem package under mlock, push to the same branch, and watch CI.\n\n**Resolving the finding.** The installed CLI at `~/.local/bin/entire` is now a fresh build of cli main (e7c03937). It addresses findings by the **org-level trail number**, which is **2516** for #377 (from the PR body link `trails/2516/changes/entire-graph/290`), NOT 290:\n- `entire trail finding list 2516 --json`\n- `entire trail finding resolve 2516 <id> ...`; check `entire agent-help trail finding` for the exact flags.\n\nResolve the finding only after the fix is pushed, and say how it was fixed. Report when CI has a result."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KBMgLYiMxhYnzaK9wp1VQ8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"- If an Entire Gates agent review posts findings on the trail, address the real ones: fix the code, or explain in a PR comment.\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,a+\"\"\"\n  - The installed `~/.local/bin/entire` is a fresh build of cli main. Finding commands take the **org-level trail number** from the PR body link `trails/<ORG>/changes/entire-graph/<REPO>`, so use `<ORG>`, e.g. `entire trail finding list 2516 --json`. The per-repo number (the gate link's `trails/290`) selects a DIFFERENT trail in the new CLI.\n  - Don't trust the gate's \"Findings: passed\": a review can post after the check completes. `entire trail finding list <ORG> --status any --freshness any --json` is the source of truth.\n  - Keep the Entire trail link block at the top of the PR body when you rewrite it.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G3-C2'].update(status='done', note='PR #374: tool symbols 84 → 3 across 4 repos (83 false → 1 disclosed; genuine 1 → 2, one newly found); cache bumped; the rest of the index byte-identical; 13 mutations red; the one gate finding fixed and resolved; CI 34 green, only Approvals pending.')\nT['G3-3'].update(status='doing', note=T['G3-3']['note']+' | OPEN low finding 01M5R28E (fallback paths use the uncapped grep selection): agent resumed to fix it.')\nT['D-review-372']['note']+=' | Finding sweep done with the fresh CLI by org trail number: #370-#376 have 0 findings; #377 has 1 low (being fixed). #374 body lost its trail link (org number not in the body).'\nif 'cli-refresh' not in T:\n    i=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('D-review-372')+1\n    d['tasks'].insert(i, dict(id='cli-refresh',lane='graph',title='Installed entire CLI was an Aug 19 dev build (finding resolve 404s)',status='done',owner='claude',source='proactive',note='Replaced ~/.local/bin/entire with a clean build of cli main e7c03937 (atomic mv); old binary kept at ~/.local/bin/entire.bak-20260819. The new CLI uses ORG trail numbers for finding commands.'))\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('board ok')\nEOF","description":"Add trail-number rules to protocol and update board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
