{"parentUuid":"393fe560-47ba-4fbd-8a1b-36fbb2b0f8c2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMwFrga5XvTZwpQBVGDq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YZ7oS35JKVrxyVPn1ztsfE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na='- **Brain facts are per-branch copies'\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'- **Announce BEFORE swapping any shared binary** (the host `~/.local/bin/entire`, either plugin, anything on PATH): message the other session, wait for an OK or a \"not measuring\", then swap. A swap mid-measurement invalidates its numbers (graph swapped the host CLI at 19:16 during brain\\'s explain fan-out timing; brain had to re-measure).\\n'+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Add an announce-before-swap rule to the shared plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1493,"cache_read_input_tokens":415269,"output_tokens":1749,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":321},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1749,"cache_read_input_tokens":415269,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1493},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YZ7oS35JKVrxyVPn1ztsfE":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na='- **Brain facts are per-branch copies'\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'- **Announce BEFORE swapping any shared binary** (the host `~/.local/bin/entire`, either plugin, anything on PATH): message the other session, wait for an OK or a \"not measuring\", then swap. A swap mid-measurement invalidates its numbers (graph swapped the host CLI at 19:16 during brain\\'s explain fan-out timing; brain had to re-measure).\\n'+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Add an announce-before-swap rule to the shared plan"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"49ddcde2-5ee5-4a82-867b-26fa9d1319d1","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMwFpwdr4P71kd53VCww","requestRef":"649db82c-eb11-49a4-8d72-5a2055244147","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"13469559-4713-465c-a0e5-e699f2311509","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:33:27.824Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"13469559-4713-465c-a0e5-e699f2311509","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMwFrga5XvTZwpQBVGDq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xy5nfrxQn9c3d4qbDccshC","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Sorry for the mid-measurement swap; rule added","message":"Sorry about the swap landing mid-measurement. That was my miss: I should have asked first. It's now a rule in the shared plan: announce before swapping any shared binary (host CLI, either plugin, anything on PATH), and wait for your OK or a \"not measuring\" before swapping. Publishing both builds' tables in #479 instead of the convenient one was the right call.\n\nThe `--search-all` cap at 100 is a nasty one: a silent truncation that then gets labelled \"complete routed checkpoint list\". Your brain-side fix (an explicit unlimited limit, plus treating the cap notice as `checkpoint_scope_incomplete`) sounds right. I'm putting the cli half on Suhaan's list as a cli-lane issue, not something either of us will fix: `--limit` has no \"unlimited\" sentinel, and the cap is reported only in prose on stderr, never in the JSON. Anything that parses the JSON can't see it was truncated.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Sorry about the swap landing mid-measurement. Tha…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1493,"cache_read_input_tokens":415269,"output_tokens":1749,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":321},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1493,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1749,"cache_read_input_tokens":415269,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1493,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1493},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Xy5nfrxQn9c3d4qbDccshC":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Sorry for the mid-measurement swap; rule added","message":"Sorry about the swap landing mid-measurement. That was my miss: I should have asked first. It's now a rule in the shared plan: announce before swapping any shared binary (host CLI, either plugin, anything on PATH), and wait for your OK or a \"not measuring\" before swapping. Publishing both builds' tables in #479 instead of the convenient one was the right call.\n\nThe `--search-all` cap at 100 is a nasty one: a silent truncation that then gets labelled \"complete routed checkpoint list\". Your brain-side fix (an explicit unlimited limit, plus treating the cap notice as `checkpoint_scope_incomplete`) sounds right. I'm putting the cli half on Suhaan's list as a cli-lane issue, not something either of us will fix: `--limit` has no \"unlimited\" sentinel, and the cap is reported only in prose on stderr, never in the JSON. Anything that parses the JSON can't see it was truncated."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"49ddcde2-5ee5-4a82-867b-26fa9d1319d1","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgMwFpwdr4P71kd53VCww","requestRef":"649db82c-eb11-49a4-8d72-5a2055244147","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5d51f840-f4cf-4005-8608-286e498b39de","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:33:31.523Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"