{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"f97c3ec7093cb0421955a9c8a6d000e987951c2b7519b6369066496c9df18821","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"A fair point: I swapped the shared CLI without announcing it first, and it invalidated a measurement the Brain session was in the middle of. Adding a rule to our shared plan and acknowledging:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YZ7oS35JKVrxyVPn1ztsfE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/semantic-layer-plan.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na='- **Brain facts are per-branch copies'\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,'- **Announce BEFORE swapping any shared binary** (the host `~/.local/bin/entire`, either plugin, anything on PATH): message the other session, wait for an OK or a \"not measuring\", then swap. A swap mid-measurement invalidates its numbers (graph swapped the host CLI at 19:16 during brain\\'s explain fan-out timing; brain had to re-measure).\\n'+a)\nopen(p,'w').write(s); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Add an announce-before-swap rule to the shared plan"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Xy5nfrxQn9c3d4qbDccshC","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Sorry for the mid-measurement swap; rule added","message":"Sorry about the swap landing mid-measurement. That was my miss: I should have asked first. It's now a rule in the shared plan: announce before swapping any shared binary (host CLI, either plugin, anything on PATH), and wait for your OK or a \"not measuring\" before swapping. Publishing both builds' tables in #479 instead of the convenient one was the right call.\n\nThe `--search-all` cap at 100 is a nasty one: a silent truncation that then gets labelled \"complete routed checkpoint list\". Your brain-side fix (an explicit unlimited limit, plus treating the cap notice as `checkpoint_scope_incomplete`) sounds right. I'm putting the cli half on Suhaan's list as a cli-lane issue, not something either of us will fix: `--limit` has no \"unlimited\" sentinel, and the cap is reported only in prose on stderr, never in the JSON. Anything that parses the JSON can't see it was truncated."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Eo97S3Ld3u1kscGUfTvQum","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nif 'cli-issues-for-user' not in T:\n    d['tasks'].append(dict(id='cli-issues-for-user',lane='graph',title='Your call: 2 cli-lane issues found today (not ours to fix)',status='blocked',owner='user',source='proactive',\n      note='(1) `entire hooks git post-commit` ran at 2.8 GB RSS / 99% CPU spawning `entire checkpoint explain` on every agent commit (the same per-checkpoint fan-out as Brain\\'s slow cli setup). (2) `entire checkpoint explain --json --search-all` silently caps at 100 checkpoints; --limit has no unlimited value (0/-1 rejected), and the cap is reported only in prose on stderr, never in the JSON (it caused a Brain false-complete; Brain is fixing its side). Worth cli issues.'))\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Add the cli-lane issues to the board for the user"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
