{"parentUuid":"f476a223-52a6-4479-9100-c57050dd8cb7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMwHQwojXpteKZ5GmXjC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0138PfZjRfPpWBcurv2jQJGE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries\ndescription: Swapping the host entire CLI or a plugin while the other session is timing invalidates its numbers; ask first, swap after an OK\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n**Before replacing any shared binary, ask the other session and wait for an OK or a \"not measuring\".** This covers the host `~/.local/bin/entire`, the graph/brain plugins, and anything on PATH. On 2026-10-24 I replaced a stale Aug 19 `~/.local/bin/entire` with a fresh cli-main build. The swap itself was correct: atomic `mv`, backup kept. But it landed in the middle of the Brain session's `entire checkpoint explain` fan-out timing, and the measured knee moved (P=8 12.6 s → 14.4 s). Brain had to re-measure, and it changed a PR's cap from 8 to 4.\n\n**Why:** a binary is shared state just like the Brain store and the plugins. The fact that \"it's an upgrade\" doesn't make it invisible to someone who is measuring.\n\n**How to apply:** message the other session (SendMessage), and add an AGENT-COMMS line if anything long-running could be affected. Swap only after a reply. Name the old and new build hashes in the message.\n\nRelated: [[shared-tmp-contended-across-agents]], [[load-pressure-is-an-arm-confound]], [[stale-entire-binary-finding-404]].\nEOF\necho '- [Announce before swapping shared binaries](announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries.md) — swapping ~/.local/bin/entire mid-timing invalidated the other session'\"'\"'s numbers; ask first' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md; tail -1 /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Save the announce-before-swap lesson to memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2005,"cache_read_input_tokens":416762,"output_tokens":923,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":129},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2005,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":923,"cache_read_input_tokens":416762,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2005},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0138PfZjRfPpWBcurv2jQJGE":{"command":"cat > /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries.md <<'EOF'\n---\nname: announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries\ndescription: Swapping the host entire CLI or a plugin while the other session is timing invalidates its numbers; ask first, swap after an OK\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\n**Before replacing any shared binary, ask the other session and wait for an OK or a \"not measuring\".** This covers the host `~/.local/bin/entire`, the graph/brain plugins, and anything on PATH. On 2026-10-24 I replaced a stale Aug 19 `~/.local/bin/entire` with a fresh cli-main build. The swap itself was correct: atomic `mv`, backup kept. But it landed in the middle of the Brain session's `entire checkpoint explain` fan-out timing, and the measured knee moved (P=8 12.6 s → 14.4 s). Brain had to re-measure, and it changed a PR's cap from 8 to 4.\n\n**Why:** a binary is shared state just like the Brain store and the plugins. The fact that \"it's an upgrade\" doesn't make it invisible to someone who is measuring.\n\n**How to apply:** message the other session (SendMessage), and add an AGENT-COMMS line if anything long-running could be affected. Swap only after a reply. Name the old and new build hashes in the message.\n\nRelated: [[shared-tmp-contended-across-agents]], [[load-pressure-is-an-arm-confound]], [[stale-entire-binary-finding-404]].\nEOF\necho '- [Announce before swapping shared binaries](announce-before-swapping-shared-binaries.md) — swapping ~/.local/bin/entire mid-timing invalidated the other session'\"'\"'s numbers; ask first' >> /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md; tail -1 /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/memory/MEMORY.md","description":"Save the announce-before-swap lesson to memory"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a48d4ef3-9401-435d-bed4-6a863000c722","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgMwHQcxzbbBVZ1j6fYdQ","requestRef":"622bd82c-02c5-495e-ab4d-af3b70232731","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2ee4cbe3-21a3-4872-b5a4-d3232db7c451","timestamp":"2026-10-24T23:33:47.758Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
