6bmMbf8jZmN":{"command":"D=/Users/suhaan/.claude/dev-mods/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/todo-live; [ \"$(basename $D)\" = todo-live ] && rm -rf \"$D\" && echo deleted; ls /Users/suhaan/.claude/dev-mods/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/ 2>/dev/null; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['todo-live-mod'].update(status='done', note='Session dev-mod copy deleted (B4); the permanent .claude/mods/todo-board carries the live band.')\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Delete the session todo-live dev mod and mark B4 done"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9050cf27-9737-4a8c-beda-04d23be0770c","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgMzzbkvpwK6UzwDDz5hB","requestRef":"b3f74a22-8854-43b2-a743-05f6040f0adb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8d2e80d6-da43-4b19-af17-94b8fd606e4f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:22:23.918Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"8d2e80d6-da43-4b19-af17-94b8fd606e4f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMzzc6XjVgmcayJfE2kf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SzNb11VRRQw9xSzj94iRdy","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Adversarial review of PR #372","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are an independent adversarial security reviewer. Default stance: the PR is UNSAFE until you independently re-derive its safety claim from source and from your own reproduction. Do not trust the PR body's evidence; re-run it. Output: caveman-ultra compressed, keeping every file:line, command and exit code. Use RTK for shell.\n\n## Target\nentireio/entire-graph **PR #372**, \"fix(sem): index partial clones offline when Git honours GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH\". Branch `fix/index-partial-clones`, head 0aa8b856 (confirm the head with `gh pr view 372 --json headRefOid`). Read it with `gh pr view 372` and `gh pr diff 372`.\n\n**What it does.** Before #372, entire-graph refused to run git subprocesses on any repo with a promisor remote (partial clone), so it could never trigger a network fetch. #372 admits partial clones when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, arguing that `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` (set on every git subprocess) provably prevents lazy fetches, with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` as a second layer. Its invariant is that **entire-graph never causes network egress**. The PR also changed `HeadCommitAndTree` from `git show -s` to `git log -1 --no-walk`.\n\n## Workspace\n`git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin fix/index-partial-clones && git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph worktree add /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review origin/fix/index-partial-clones` (detached is fine). Read-only review: no commits, no pushes, no PR comments. Keep scratch files in the worktree's `.g3/`.\n\n## Attack it. Each item needs a reproduction or a source citation\n1. **Version gate.**\n   - Can the version probe be fooled? Look at a vendor suffix (`2.45.0.windows.1`, `2.39.5 (Apple Git-154)`), a `GIT_EXEC_PATH` / PATH swap between the probe and later calls, a cached result keyed by path+size+mtime against a binary swapped with the same size and mtime, and a symlinked git.\n   - Is \"unknown → refuse\" actually fail-closed on every parse path?\n2. **Env coverage.** The PR claims ONE env builder (`gitSubprocessEnvironment`) behind both command constructors, plus an AST test against stray `exec.Command`.\n   - Find any git invocation that escapes it: `os/exec` via another package, `syscall.Exec`, go-git or another library reading objects (would a library path lazily fetch?), a git *hook* or `core.fsmonitor` / `core.sshCommand` / `credential.helper` / `uploadpack` config in the TARGET repo's `.git/config` that git itself would run.\n   - Is the repo-config attack surface handled? Does the safety preflight still refuse dangerous repo configs?\n3. **Does GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH cover everything that can fetch?**\n   - Check against the Git docs or source for 2.45+: `git grep` on a promisor repo, `cat-file --batch-command`, `log --name-only` with renames, `diff` rename detection, submodules (`submodule.recurse`, `fetch.recurseSubmodules`), `fetch` triggered by `maintenance`/`gc --auto` (does indexing ever run anything that triggers auto-gc or auto-maintenance with a prefetch task?), and alternates.\n4. **Reproduce the core claim yourself on git 2.54** (this machine). Build a working partial-clone fixture:\n   ```sh\n   git clone --no-local file://$SRC cl\n   git -C cl config remote.origin.promisor true\n   git -C cl config remote.origin.partialclonefilter blob:none\n   # build keep.txt = every object except one blob\n   git pack-objects to a new pack FIRST, then delete the old pack\n   ```\n   Deleting the old pack first triggers a refetch. Verify `rev-list --objects --all --missing=print | grep -c '^?'` = 1.\n   Then, with the PR's binary (`go build -o .g3/eg ./cmd/entire-graph` in the worktree; invoke it as `.g3/eg index --repo cl --head --cache-dir <fresh>`), run under `GIT_TRACE=1 GIT_TRACE_PACKET=1`. Assert that zero `fetch`/`upload-pack` processes appear, and that the missing blob produces an error or warning, not a fetch.\n   Also run index, query, snapshot, neighbors and impact on that fixture.\n   **Capture exit codes before any pipe.**\n5. **Weaken and confirm the guard is load-bearing.** Remove `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` from the env builder in a scratch build and show a fetch IS attempted (`git fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin` in the trace). If not, the fixture is inert: fix the fixture, not the conclusion.\n6. **`show -s` → `log -1 --no-walk`.** Is the output (commit + tree) byte-identical on normal repos, root commits, merge commits, and repos with `log.showSignature` or a `format.pretty` config? A user config could change the output, so check that `-c` overrides or `--format` pin it.\n7. **Message and docs.** Is every refusal and warning message true for every caller now?\n\n## Report (≤ 50 lines)\n- A verdict: SAFE TO MERGE / SAFE WITH CHANGES / UNSAFE.\n- For each item above: verdict | evidence (command + exit code, or file:line) | the required change if any.\n- Anything you could not test, and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2344,"cache_read_input_tokens":437264,"output_tokens":3668,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":131},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2344,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3668,"cache_read_input_tokens":437264,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2344,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2344},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SzNb11VRRQw9xSzj94iRdy":{"description":"Adversarial review of PR #372","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You are an independent adversarial security reviewer. Default stance: the PR is UNSAFE until you independently re-derive its safety claim from source and from your own reproduction. Do not trust the PR body's evidence; re-run it. Output: caveman-ultra compressed, keeping every file:line, command and exit code. Use RTK for shell.\n\n## Target\nentireio/entire-graph **PR #372**, \"fix(sem): index partial clones offline when Git honours GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH\". Branch `fix/index-partial-clones`, head 0aa8b856 (confirm the head with `gh pr view 372 --json headRefOid`). Read it with `gh pr view 372` and `gh pr diff 372`.\n\n**What it does.** Before #372, entire-graph refused to run git subprocesses on any repo with a promisor remote (partial clone), so it could never trigger a network fetch. #372 admits partial clones when the runtime git is ≥ 2.45, arguing that `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1` (set on every git subprocess) provably prevents lazy fetches, with `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL=` as a second layer. Its invariant is that **entire-graph never causes network egress**. The PR also changed `HeadCommitAndTree` from `git show -s` to `git log -1 --no-walk`.\n\n## Workspace\n`git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin fix/index-partial-clones && git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph worktree add /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review origin/fix/index-partial-clones` (detached is fine). Read-only review: no commits, no pushes, no PR comments. Keep scratch files in the worktree's `.g3/`.\n\n## Attack it. Each item needs a reproduction or a source citation\n1. **Version gate.**\n   - Can the version probe be fooled? Look at a vendor suffix (`2.45.0.windows.1`, `2.39.5 (Apple Git-154)`), a `GIT_EXEC_PATH` / PATH swap between the probe and later calls, a cache