pack` processes appear, and that the missing blob produces an error or warning, not a fetch.\n   Also run index, query, snapshot, neighbors and impact on that fixture.\n   **Capture exit codes before any pipe.**\n5. **Weaken and confirm the guard is load-bearing.** Remove `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` from the env builder in a scratch build and show a fetch IS attempted (`git fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin` in the trace). If not, the fixture is inert: fix the fixture, not the conclusion.\n6. **`show -s` → `log -1 --no-walk`.** Is the output (commit + tree) byte-identical on normal repos, root commits, merge commits, and repos with `log.showSignature` or a `format.pretty` config? A user config could change the output, so check that `-c` overrides or `--format` pin it.\n7. **Message and docs.** Is every refusal and warning message true for every caller now?\n\n## Report (≤ 50 lines)\n- A verdict: SAFE TO MERGE / SAFE WITH CHANGES / UNSAFE.\n- For each item above: verdict | evidence (command + exit code, or file:line) | the required change if any.\n- Anything you could not test, and why."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9050cf27-9737-4a8c-beda-04d23be0770c","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgMzzbkvpwK6UzwDDz5hB","requestRef":"b3f74a22-8854-43b2-a743-05f6040f0adb","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"34adfe41-481b-4914-a192-e2a58d6b8f5a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:22:44.358Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"34adfe41-481b-4914-a192-e2a58d6b8f5a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgMzzc6XjVgmcayJfE2kf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SyTEUiHTdZSHSXGY4XP3mR","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Find superseded open graph PRs","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only sweep: decide which OPEN PRs on entireio/entire-graph are superseded by work already merged to `main`. Do NOT close, comment on, push to or edit anything; just report. Output: caveman-ultra compressed (a dense table). Use RTK for shell (`rtk proxy <cmd>` for raw).\n\n## Steps\n1. `gh pr list --repo entireio/entire-graph --state open --limit 200 --json number,title,headRefName,author,createdAt,updatedAt,isDraft,baseRefName`.\n2. **EXCLUDE** these PRs, which are current work and must stay open: #142, #370, #371, #372, #373, #374, #375, #376, #377, and any PR created on or after 2026-10-24.\n3. For every other open PR:\n   - `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin main pull/<N>/head:refs/remotes/pr/<N>`. That's a main checkout: use fetch only, never checkout, commit or branch switches there.\n   - Classify it:\n     - **MERGED-EQUIVALENT:** `git cherry origin/main refs/remotes/pr/<N>` shows every commit as `-` (patch already on main), or the PR head is an ancestor of origin/main (`git merge-base --is-ancestor`).\n     - **SUPERSEDED-LIKELY:** not patch-equivalent, but its title or feature clearly landed via another merged PR. Find which with `gh pr list --state merged --search \"<keywords>\"` and `git log origin/main --oneline --grep=<keyword>`. Cite the merged PR number and commit.\n     - **STALE-CONFLICTING:** `gh pr view <N> --json mergeable` is CONFLICTING and its base is far behind. Note how many commits behind.\n     - **STILL-RELEVANT:** none of the above.\n   - For stacked PRs (base ≠ main), note the base, and whether the base branch is merged or gone.\n4. Count th