{"parentUuid":"ec4fbde5-478b-446b-8f6b-248f70c0b688","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN13UKnN5PVK7AoFcSpF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[#142](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/142) is rescoped and green, with only Approvals open.\n- **What it does now:** indexing stops cleanly when cancelled and never caches a partial snapshot.\n- **What it dropped:** the time limit and the partial-snapshot path. The other fixes removed the slow paths those were for, and the PR shrank from 76 to 62 files.\n- **Tests:** five deliberate breakages each fail a test.\n- **Review findings:** one is resolved. The other is dismissed with reasoning, since the code it flags is what lets Ctrl-C through a stalled pipe.\n\n**Graph scorecard:** 9 PRs are open (#142, #370–#377), all CI-green with no open review findings, each waiting only on approval. The last fix, the silent-gap disclosure, is still being built.\n\n**Close-out now running:**\n- **Independent security review of #372.** It loosens the \"never touch the network\" guard, so a separate reviewer is attacking it: reproducing the no-fetch proof itself, looking for any git call that escapes the protection, checking repo-config tricks, and spoofing the version check.\n- **Old-PR sweep:** finding open graph PRs already superseded by merged work. It only reports. I'll close only the clear duplicates, and anything uncertain goes on your list.\n- **Housekeeping:** deleted my session-only copy of the live board mod; the permanent one shows the same band."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4504,"cache_read_input_tokens":439608,"output_tokens":482,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4504,"ephemeral_5m_in