TORY_UNAVAILABLE` carrying Git's reason. This covers:\n    - the direct build;\n    - the records-cache transaction (it used to keep only an `unavailable` flag and dropped the reason);\n    - derived selective views.\n  - A cache hit drops the warning once its history refresh succeeds.\n  - `impact` now says \"Co-change coupling unknown\" instead of \"No co-change coupling found\".\n  - **Real repro:** an inexact rename plus the old blob repacked away. Base gives `co_changes 0, warnings []`; new gives the warning with `unable to read <oid>`.\n  - `entire graph impact` was run on all 12 touched symbols; the table is in the PR body.\n  \n  ### Timing and identity (correctness fix, no speed claim)\n  - **Cold** neighbors on brain: base 15053ms, new 15023ms (load1 about 5.7).\n  - **Warm**, 3 interleaved reps: median base 1354ms, new 1401ms. The ranges overlap; the new code only appends a warning.\n  - **Agent output:** 2314 → 2474 bytes, +160, which is the disclosure line.\n  - **Identity** (`g2-strip.py` on brain):\n    - neighbors-out, a type query, and `query`: byte-identical;\n    - neighbors-in and impact for a function: identical once the one added warning is removed.\n  \n  ### Tests\n  - 7 new cli tests in `internal/cli/value_refs_test.go` and `impact_text_test.go`; 4 new sem tests in `internal/sem/cochange_history_warning_test.go`. The sem tests use a git stub that fails only `--name-only` and drains stdin, plus the real missing-blob fixture.\n  - **Mutation-proven:** 18 mutations, all red, each restored with `git diff --stat` clean. Script `.g3/mutate.py`, output `.g3/mutation-final.txt`. One mutation (stream warning) first went red only on a compile error; I redid it as a behavioural mutation and it went red on the test.\n  - **`-race` under mlock:** 99 related cli tests and 117 related sem tests green. Full suites left to CI, which passed them.\n  \n  ### Housekeeping and follow-ups\n  - I had appended `.g3/` and `bin/` to the main checkout's shared `.git/info/exclude`. Both lines are reverted.\n  - **Brain fact not recorded:** `brain remember` writes to `~/.local/share/entire`, which the protocol forbids. Candidate fact: the naive grep pattern misses end-of-line refs.\n  - **Follow-ups listed in the PR:**\n    - the real fix (Go var symbols plus a REFERENCES relation, with a schema/cache bump);\n    - `--no-renames` in `FileCochanges` would let co-change work on blob:none clones;\n    - a pre-existing perf issue: when the history refresh keeps failing, every warm query is a cache miss and rebuilds.\n  ","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"## Report: PR #378 (one correctness fix for two silent gaps)\n\n**PR #378** is open: https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/378. Branch `fix/disclose-unmodelled-references` (1 commit `fix(cli,sem): ...`). Worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-disclose-refs`, scratch in `.g3/` (not committed).\n\n**CI:** 30+ checks green, including:\n- `test (ubuntu/macos/windows)`, all 8 Windows shards, lint, CodeQL.\n- Entire Gates: fail on the **Approvals** sub-gate only (\"no reviewers approved\"). Its other sub-gates passed: Checks, Up to date, and Findings (\"Agent review found no blocking issues\"; 0 findings on trail #291).\n- Nothing is running. Nothing to fix.\n\n**Preflight:** graph `v0.5.1-nightly…d4a0c186` and brain `v0.2.0-nightly…318e4b05`, both available. Brain recall on co-change found only the #372 fact. On disclosure it found nothing on main (it pointed at 2 other branches).\n\n### Gap 1: value references not modelled\n- **Live check (entire-brain, fresh cache, under mlock):** `neighbors openHistoryFTS --direction in --format agent` now prints, right after `Callers:`:\n  `Value refs unmodelled (var/arg/struct/map): grep -rnE '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])openHistoryFTS([^(A-Za-z0-9_]|$)' --include='*.go' . ; non-call hits are missed callers`\n- **The brief's grep pattern misses the motivating case.** `X[^(a-zA-Z0-9_]` needs a character after the name, so it never matches a reference at end of line. On brain it returns only 4 comment lines and misses `history_fts.go:824`. I switched to the `([^(…]|$)` form, which finds :824. A test pins that it finds all 6 value-ref shapes and not the call.\n- **Where it appears:**\n  - JSON: one `W_VALUE_REFERENCES_UNMODELLED` warning in the existing `warnings` array.\n  - Agent/text: the line after `Callers:`.\n  - `impact`: a Summary bullet, plus after the `IMPACT DEGENERATE` line (the marker prefix is unchanged).\n  - Compact neighbors: 3 variants placed ahead of the edges.\n- **Gated to:** a single Go func/method with a Go-identifier name (so the shell command stays safe), `--relation CALLS`, direction in/both, and impact.\n- **Budget:** the line is charged against `--max-context-bytes`. It is kept out of the completeness banner count and out of `completeness_scope`.\n- **No goldens** exist for neighbors/impact output; the search VERIFY goldens are untouched.\n- **Correction to your command:** `bin/new graph neighbors` is invalid (\"unknown command graph\"). The binary is the plugin itself, so the working form is `bin/new neighbors …`.\n\n### Gap 2: co-change dropped silently\n- A failed history read now yields `W_COCHANGE_HISTORY_UNAVAILABLE` carrying Git's reason. This covers:\n  - the direct build;\n  - the records-cache transaction (it used to keep only an `unavailable` flag and dropped the reason);\n  - derived selective views.\n- A cache hit drops the warning once its history refresh succeeds.\n- `impact` now says \"Co-change coupling unknown\" instead of \"No co-change coupling found\".\n- **Real repro:** an inexact rename plus the old blob repacked away. Base gives `co_changes 0, warnings []`; new gives the warning with `unable to read <oid>`.\n- `entire graph impact` was run on all 12 touched symbols; the table is in the PR body.\n\n### Timing and identity (correctness fix, no speed claim)\n- **Cold** neighbors on brain: base 15053ms, new 15023ms (load1 about 5.7).\n- **Warm**, 3 interleaved reps: median base 1354ms, new 1401ms. The ranges overlap; the new code only appends a warning.\n- **Agent output:** 2314 → 2474 bytes, +160, which is the disclosure line.\n- **Identity** (`g2-strip.py` on brain):\n  - neighbors-out, a type query, and `query`: byte-identical;\n  - neighbors-in and impact for a function: identical once the one added warning is removed.\n\n### Tests\n- 7 new cli tests in `internal/cli/value_refs_test.go` and `impact_text_test.go`; 4 new sem tests in `internal/sem/cochange_history_warning_test.go`. The sem tests use a git stub that fails only `--name-only` and drains stdin, plus the real missing-blob fixture.\n- **Mutation-proven:** 18 mutations, all red, each restored with `git diff --stat` clean. Script `.g3/mutate.py`, output `.g3/mutation-final.txt`. One mutation (stream warning) first went red only on a compile error; I redid it as a behavioural mutation and it went red on the test.\n- **`-race` under mlock:** 99 related cli tests and 117 related sem tests green. Full suites left to CI, which passed them.\n\n### Housekeeping and follow-ups\n- I had appended `.g3/` and `bin/` to the main checkout's shared `.git/info/exclude`. Both lines are reverted.\n- **Brain fact not recorded:** `brain remember` writes to `~/.local/share/entire`, which the protocol forbids. Candidate fact: the naive grep pattern misses end-of-line refs.\n- **Follow-ups listed in the PR:**\n  - the real fix (Go var symbols plus a REFERENCES relation, with a schema/cache bump);\n  - `--no-renames` in `FileCochanges` would let co-change work on blob:none clones;\n  - a pre-existing perf issue: when the history refresh keeps failing, every warm query is a cache miss and rebuilds.\n"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
