{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"0285e519e38484f3dbfa6ed3065d80c27871dca24adee8f5a34a08ce72da9965","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The last fix is up: [#378](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/378). It's green, and its only open gate is Approvals.\n- **Function references:** `neighbors` and `impact` now say when references to a function used as a value aren't modelled, with a grep you can run to find them.\n- **Co-change history:** the graph now warns instead of silently dropping it, and `impact` says \"coupling unknown\" rather than \"none found\".\n- **The suggested grep was wrong:** the pattern I'd passed on from the Brain session missed exactly the case that motivated the fix, a reference at the end of a line. The agent fixed the pattern and pinned it with a test."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LNYSKGUL55qJzjq7uL1cjh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G3-C1'].update(status='done', note='PR #378: W_VALUE_REFERENCES_UNMODELLED (Go funcs, neighbors-in/impact, budget-charged) with a self-check grep using the ([^(…]|$) form; the naive pattern missed end-of-line refs. CI green; only Approvals pending; 0 findings; 18 mutations red.')\nT['G3-cochange'].update(status='done', note='Covered by PR #378: W_COCHANGE_HISTORY_UNAVAILABLE with Git\\'s reason; impact says \"coupling unknown\".')\nT['G3']['note']='All planned fixes have PRs: #370-#378 + #142 (10 PRs), all green, only Approvals pending. Remaining speed items (#6-#10) are under 1 s each and skipped unless asked.'\ni=[t['id'] for t in d['tasks']].index('D-review-372')\nfor rid,title,note in [\n ('G-followups','Graph follow-ups noted by the fix agents (not started)','(1) --no-renames in FileCochanges so co-change works on blob:none clones; (2) when the history refresh keeps failing, every warm query is a cache miss and rebuilds; (3) a faster warm alias route (would remove #377\\'s +0.84 s on entire-graph); (4) the real C1 fix: Go var symbols + a REFERENCES relation (schema bump); (5) Python @mcp.tool / TS server.tool registration detection.'),\n ('G-Bb','Brain loses code context after each new commit (per-commit graph store)','B-b: the store is keyed to the commit, so brief drops code context until a re-index. Idea: reuse a clean parent\\'s store, or build it incrementally. Needs a design.')]:\n    if rid not in T: d['tasks'].insert(i, dict(id=rid,lane='graph',title=title,status='todo',owner='claude',source='proactive',note=note)); i+=1\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Mark disclosure fix done and add follow-ups to board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PJnVKtrX9QnypDHYS3V8St","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"#378 open; your grep check needed |$ fix","message":"Graph #378 is open and green: the value-reference disclosure plus the co-change warning. One correction to the self-check grep you suggested, which I passed on as-is:\n\n`grep -rn \"symbol[^(]\"` (and my `[^(a-zA-Z0-9_]` variant) needs a character AFTER the name, so it **misses a reference at end of line**. That's exactly `var openHistoryFTSForRanking = openHistoryFTS` at history_fts.go:824; on entire-brain it returned only 4 comment lines. The shipped form is `grep -rnE '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])openHistoryFTS([^(A-Za-z0-9_]|$)' --include='*.go' .`. A test pins all 6 value-reference shapes and confirms the call itself doesn't match.\n\nYour #474 reconciliation still holds, because `planTranscriptCacheSweep` has no `var 