{"parentUuid":"891ceab1-1912-4b44-b177-7bad4585d2b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2GUcNdavYBpm9VeT8B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the security review runs, I'm starting the design for the \"Brain loses code context after each commit\" fix. It touches both products, so the first step is a design doc, not code:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_read_input_tokens":455190,"output_tokens":1818,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":351},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":827,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1818,"cache_read_input_tokens":455190,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":827},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"aec96c3f-10b0-4cc2-b452-b20add1bd8d0","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgN2GUFZ19rVkGGkPRQ3j","requestRef":"0f143b78-acd8-4e41-8b36-b4e0b1fd6807","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"eebcb00d-833e-4500-a72a-67e569f1e092","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:39:05.267Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"eebcb00d-833e-4500-a72a-67e569f1e092","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2GUcNdavYBpm9VeT8B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Cs7FPPgs2oZe4g2a8sTJ3t","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Design: per-commit graph store gap","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Design task, no implementation. Produce a short design doc for one entire-graph ↔ entire-brain gap, with a recommendation. Output: caveman-ultra compressed report; the doc itself in plain, clear prose. Use RTK for shell.\n\n## The gap\n- Entire Brain's `brief` reads code context from the entire-graph **search store** (a sqlite store beside the gz cache, PRs #356/#360/#361). Brain reads it through `entire graph context` / `entire graph store`.\n- The store is keyed to the commit (tree) and is built only when Brain runs its index step, `runGraphOwnedIndex` in entire-brain's `graph_store.go:235`. That step sets `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1` on `entire graph index`.\n- So after every new commit, `brief` warns \"search store not built for this commit\" and drops code context until something re-indexes. On an active branch, that is most of the time.\n\n## What to find out (graph/brain-first; cite file:line)\n1. Preflight: `entire graph version --json`, `entire graph capabilities --json`, `entire brain version`, `entire brain capabilities --json`.\n2. In entire-graph (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph`; read-only, it's a main checkout):\n   - how the store key is derived;\n   - what `graph store` / `graph context` do when the exact key is missing;\n   - how the committed-tree gz cache already handles \"a clean tree can reuse HEAD\" and cross-worktree scope reuse (#323).\n   Use `entire graph def|neighbors|impact --head` on the store open/lookup functions.\n3. In entire-brain (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain`; read-only, it's another session's main checkout, so do not edit):\n   - where `brief` calls graph context;\n   - how it reacts to a missing store;\n   - whether anything (a watch daemon, a post-commit hook, the memory worker) could trigger a rebuild.\n   Run `entire brain recall \"search store per commit\"` and similar for prior decisions.\n4. Measure, light only (warm caches, no full suites, no cold rebuilds of big repos; check `uptime`):\n   - how long a store build takes on entire-graph and entire-brain;\n   - whether an incremental update from the parent commit is plausible. What fraction of a typical commit's files change? Check `git log --stat` on the last ~20 commits.\n\n## Options to evaluate (add any better one)\n- **(a) Ancestor fallback.** On a missing key, serve the nearest ancestor commit's store, with an explicit staleness marker plus the list of files changed since, so callers can distrust those. Cheapest; correctness depends on the disclosure.\n- **(b) Incremental build.** Derive the new store from the parent's store plus the diff (re-index only changed files). Fast, but how complex is it given cross-file relations?\n- **(c) Trigger.** Rebuild in the background on commit: a Brain watch or worker, or a git hook. Does the Brain worker or daemon already exist for this?\n- **(d) Lazy.** Build on the first `brief` after a commit, with a time bound, falling back to (a).\n\nFor each: user-visible effect, correctness risk (stale relations), cost, which repo it lives in (graph lane or brain lane), and what tests would prove it.\n\n## Deliverable\n- Write the doc to `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md`: problem, current behaviour with citations, measurements, options table, recommendation, and a split into graph-side and brain-side PRs.\n- Report back in ≤ 30 lines.\n- Do not edit either repo, open PRs, touch `~/.local/share/entire`, or run `entire brain setup|refresh|--daemon`."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_read_input_tokens":455190,"output_tokens":1818,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":351},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":827,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1818,"cache_read_input_tokens":455190,"cache_creation_input_tokens":827,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":827},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Cs7FPPgs2oZe4g2a8sTJ3t":{"description":"Design: per-commit graph store gap","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Design task, no implementation. Produce a short design doc for one entire-graph ↔ entire-brain gap, with a recommendation. Output: caveman-ultra compressed report; the doc itself in plain, clear prose. Use RTK for shell.\n\n## The gap\n- Entire Brain's `brief` reads code context from the entire-graph **search store** (a sqlite store beside the gz cache, PRs #356/#360/#361). Brain reads it through `entire graph context` / `entire graph store`.\n- The store is keyed to the commit (tree) and is built only when Brain runs its index step, `runGraphOwnedIndex` in entire-brain's `graph_store.go:235`. That step sets `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1` on `entire graph index`.\n- So after every new commit, `brief` warns \"search store not built for this commit\" and drops code context until something re-indexes. On an active branch, that is most of the time.\n\n## What to find out (graph/brain-first; cite file:line)\n1. Preflight: `entire graph version --json`, `entire graph capabilities --json`, `entire brain version`, `entire brain capabilities --json`.\n2. In entire-graph (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph`; read-only, it's a main checkout):\n   - how the store key is derived;\n   - what `graph store` / `graph context` do when the exact key is missing;\n   - how the committed-tree gz cache already handles \"a clean tree can reuse HEAD\" and cross-worktree scope reuse (#323).\n   Use `entire graph def|neighbors|impact --head` on the store open/lookup functions.\n3. In entire-brain (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-brain`; read-only, it's another session's main checkout, so do not edit):\n   - where `brief` calls graph context;\n   - how it reacts to a missing store;\n   - whether anything (a watch daemon, a post-commit hook, the memory worker) could trigger a rebuild.\n   Run `entire brain recall \"search store per commit\"` and similar for prior decisions.\n4. Measure, light only (warm caches, no full suites, no cold rebuilds of big repos; check `uptime`):\n   - how long a store build takes on entire-graph and entire-brain;\n   - whether an incremental update from the parent commit is plausible. What fraction of a typical commit's files change? Check `git log --stat` on the last ~20 commits.\n\n## Options to evaluate (add any better one)\n- **(a) Ancestor fallback.** On a missing key, serve the nearest ancestor commit's store, with an explicit staleness marker plus the list of files changed since, so callers can distrust those. Cheapest; correctness depends on the disclosure.\n- **(b) Incremental build.** Derive the new store from the parent's store plus the diff (re-index only changed files). Fast, but how complex is it given cross-file relations?\n- **(c) Trigger.** Rebuild in the background on commit: a Brain watch or worker, or a git hook. Does the Brain worker or daemon already exist for this?\n- **(d) Lazy.** Build on the first `brief` after a commit, with a time bound, falling back to (a).\n\nFor each: user-visible effect, correctness risk (stale relations), cost, which repo it lives in (graph lane or brain lane), and what tests would prove it.\n\n## Deliverable\n- Write the doc to `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md`: problem, current behaviour with citations, measurements, options table, recommendation, and a split into graph-side and brain-side PRs.\n- Report back in ≤ 30 lines.\n- Do not edit either repo, open PRs, touch `~/.local/share/entire`, or run `entire brain setup|refresh|--daemon`."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"aec96c3f-10b0-4cc2-b452-b20add1bd8d0","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgN2GUFZ19rVkGGkPRQ3j","requestRef":"0f143b78-acd8-4e41-8b36-b4e0b1fd6807","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"f2ac8e9f-2c41-4099-b4ea-9edfc8153239","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:39:18.707Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
