s` (ChangedFiles, git.go:1164).\n  - Impact: the PR's invariant \"≥2.45 ⇒ no fetch process ever started\" is false. On Git for Windows 2.45.0.windows.1 (admitted by the parser), the spawned fetch runs v2.45.0 transport.c:1144 `is_file(url)` (a stat) before the :1147 `transport_check_allowed`. A UNC promisor URL therefore means SMB egress. That is exactly the bug the old refusal existed for.\n  - **Required change:**\n    - Raise the floor to 2.45.1. This means parsing the patch level: refuse 2.45.0, 2.45.0.windows.1 and 2.45.0.rcN; admit 2.45.1.windows.1.\n    - Fix the test pins `lazy_fetch_guard_test.go:77 {\"2.45.0\", true}` and `:24`, and add a test that refuses 2.45.0.\n    - Fix the citation, and point `lazy_fetch_guard.go:15-23`, docs/trust-and-security.md:40-41, docs/semantic-provider-requirements.md:432, CHANGELOG.md:22 and provider.go:18957-18959 at 2.45.1.\n    - Optional: admit the maint backports (2.44.1+ and the others listed above). Refusing them is safe, just over-strict.\n  \n  ## Item by item\n  **1. Version gate: FAIL**\n  - Floor: the 2.45.0 defect above.\n  - Vendor suffixes parse correctly: `2.45.2.windows.1`, `2.39.5 (Apple Git-154)` and rc forms (test :24-41 green, `go test ./internal/gitutil -run …LazyFetch…` exit 0). Local /usr/bin/git is 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155) and honours the variable (raw probes a1/a2: no fetch).\n  - Unknown versions fail closed on every path (LookPath, Stat, run, timeout, parse all return the zero value with Effective=false; lazy_fetch_guard.go:63-89).\n  - **Probe/use cwd mismatch, new, medium-low.** The probe runs in `os.TempDir()` (lazy_fetch_guard.go:78) while real calls run in the repo. A cwd-sensitive shim (asdf/mise-style `.tool-versions`) can probe 2.54 and then execute a different Git in the repo.\n    - Repro: `.g3/shim/git` plus `.tool-versions` set to `git 2.44.0` in the clone. eg exit 0. Shim log: `2.54.0 cwd=/var/folders/…/T argv: version`, then every repo call is `2.44.0`, and a `run_command: git -c fetch… fetch origin` child appears (stopped only by GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL; missing stays 1).\n    - Fix: probe with Dir set to the repo root and key the cache by dir, or pin the resolved binary.\n  - PATH swap within a process: not possible (both lookups use the process PATH; nothing calls Setenv PATH).\n  - Same size+mtime binary swap or symlink retarget: needs write access to the toolchain, so outside the threat model. The cache lives only for the process, which is a short-lived CLI. Optionally add inode/ctime to the key.\n  \n  **2. Env coverage: PASS (with a weak static test)**\n  - The only launch sites are git.go:2712 and :2898. No go-git. `entireio/cli` is imported only for `palette`.\n  - No `git grep`, gc, maintenance or upload-pack ever appeared in any spy log.\n  - Hostile repo config on an admitted partial clone:\n    - Config tried: core.fsmonitor, sshCommand, credential.helper, uploadpack.packObjectsHook, diff.external, textconv/filter clean/smudge/process via `.gitattributes`, core.hooksPath hooks (incl. pre-auto-gc), protocol.ext.allow=always, gitProxy, askPass, gpg.program with showSignature, gc.auto=1, maintenance.auto, an `ext::` promisor URL.\n    - Ran index, query (head and worktree), snapshot, snapshot --worktree, commit, neighbors, impact on 2.54: **0 PWN files**, missing stays 1.\n    - Control: raw unguarded git on the same fixture creates PWN-ext, PWN-fsmonitor and PWN-process, so the fixture is live.\n  - Includes are still refused (provider.go:18072). Alternates are still checked (provider.go:18593+). Neither path changed.\n  - Static test weakness: `TestEveryGitSubprocessIsBuiltByTheGuardedConstructors` misses an aliased import and package-level func values. Adding `internal/sem/zz_evade.go` with `import ex \"os/exec\"; var launch = ex.CommandContext; ex.Command(\"git\",\"fetch\")` leaves the test green (exit 0); file then removed. Suggested fix: match on the import path or use go/types, and scan package-level var initializers. Low severity: it is a tripwire, not a proof.\n  \n  **3. Coverage on ≥2.45.1: PASS.** Spy runs on 2.54 found 0 fetches each for:\n  - cat-file --batch-command, ls-tree -l, git grep over a tree with a missing blob, log --name-only with an inexact rename, diff --find-renames.\n  - Missing objects become errors: `lazy fetching disabled…` / `could not fetch <oid>`.\n  - Submodules: `submodule.recurse=false` is pinned and grep uses `--no-recurse-submodules`. No read command auto-runs gc or maintenance.\n  - On 2.45.0, grep and cat-file are also clean (fetch_if_missing); only the rename and diff prefetch leaks.\n  - Upstream master (lazy-fetch trusted-bit, 2026-10-22) still checks the variable before spawn (promisor-remote.c:328). `uploadpack.lazyFetchTrusted` is protected config used by upload-pack only, so it does not affect eg.\n  \n  **4. Core repro on 2.54: PASS.** Fixtures via `.g3/mkfix.sh`, `--missing=print` count = 1 each.\n  - cl1 (HEAD blob missing) and cl2 (history rename blob missing), production binary through the PATH and GIT_EXEC_PATH spy: index, query --head, query (worktree), snapshot, neighbors, impact all exit 0, 0 fetch children, every call carries `NLF=1 GAP=`, missing_after=1.\n  - cl1 index reports `E_FILE_READ` for gone.go.\n  - `snapshot --head` is not a flag; I used `snapshot` (HEAD) and `--worktree`.\n  - **Warning for anyone repeating this:** the prescribed parent `GIT_TRACE=1` check proves nothing. git.go:2785 strips `GIT_TRACE*`, and no trace file was produced. That is why I used the spy plus a build with a trace variable injected.\n  \n  **5. Weakened builds: PASS.** The guard is load-bearing:\n  - Trace build, both guards: 0 fetches.\n  - Without NLF: `run_command: git -c fetch.negotiationAlgorithm=noop fetch origin … --filter=blob:none --stdin`, missing stays 1.\n  - Without NLF and GAP: missing goes to **0**, files=2.\n  - Source restored (`git status` clean).\n  \n  **6. `show -s` → `log -1 --no-walk`: PASS**\n  - Byte-identical under eg's exact pins on root, merge and SSH-signed+notes commits. 18 hostile repo configs tried (showSignature, format.pretty, decorate, color.ui=always, abbrev, follow, diffMerges, notes, …); 51/51 rows exact against `rev-parse` (.g3/cmp6.sh).\n  - On the partial clone with a rename+edit HEAD: show exits 128, log exits 0 with exact output.\n  - Pre-existing, not a regression: repo `i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-16` re-encodes the output under both forms. eg fails closed: `git log returned malformed HEAD commit/tree metadata`, exit 1, which is a DoS only. Optional fix: pin `i18n.logOutputEncoding`.\n  \n  **7. Messages and docs: FAIL**\n  - \"Git 2.45 or newer reads partial clones offline\" is false for 2.45.0.\n  - \"predates 2.45, so it ignores GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH\" is false for 2.44.1+ and the other maint releases. For an unknown version it asserts \"predates\" without knowing (provider.go:18952-18959).\n  - Diagnosis re-probes on its own (provider.go:18930). A transient probe timeout in the safety check followed by a successful probe in the diagnosis produces a diagnosis that blames nothing.\n  - The CHANGELOG says partial clones \"now work\", but `commit HEAD` on 2.54 exits 1 on the rename fixture, and co-change is silently dropped (the PR notes the co-change case).\n  \n  **Not tested:** a real Windows / Git for Windows 2.45.0 UNC SMB stat; that rests on a source citation only (transport.c:1144 vs :1147). macOS autofs `/net` stat egress. A real asdf/mise install (simulated with a shim instead). The full package test suites were not run (CPU discipline). I recorded nothing in the Brain store because it is shared state. Worth recording: the GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH chokepoint arrived in 2.45.1 and the 2024-04 maint releases, not in 2.45.0.\n  ","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"## PR #372 adversarial review. head 0aa8b856 (confirmed via `gh pr view 372 --json headRefOid`)\nWorktree: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review. Scratch: .g3/. Source tree left clean (`git status` shows only .g3/).\n\n**VERDICT: UNSAFE as written.** It becomes SAFE WITH CHANGES once the version floor is 2.45.1. That fix is small but blocking.\n\n**Core finding: the 2.45.0 floor is wrong.** Git 2.45.0 does not check GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH before it spawns `git fetch`.\n- The check that matters, `fetch_objects()` returning early when the env var is set, comes from 7b70e9efb18c (\"upload-pack: disable lazy-fetching by default\"). It shipped in the 2024-04 security releases: 2.39.4, 2.40.2, 2.41.1, 2.42.2, 2.43.4, 2.44.1 and **2.45.1**. It is not in 2.45.0.\n  - Evidence: `gh api repos/git/git/contents/promisor-remote.c?ref=<tag>` grep NO_LAZY_FETCH gives v2.45.0=0, v2.44.0=0, v2.44.1=2, v2.44.4=2, v2.39.4=2, v2.45.1=1, v2.46.0=1, v2.54.0=1.\n  - The PR's citation `2c206fc` does not resolve (GitHub 422).\n- In 2.45.0 the variable only sets `fetch_if_missing=0` (environment.c:211). That covers direct object reads only.\n  - Rename-detection prefetch calls `promisor_remote_get_direct` without checking it: v2.45.0 diffcore-rename.c:125/897, reached via :988/:1574; diff.c:6960.\n- Repro with git 2.45.0 built from source (.g3/git245):\n  - Raw `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 git log -z --name-only` on the rename fixture: exit 0, missing 1→**0**. The blob was actually fetched.\n  - With both guards set: exit 128, `fatal: transport 'file' not allowed`. The fetch child was spawned and stopped only by the allowlist. The same happens with an `ext::` URL (`transport 'ext' not allowed`).\n- Product-level repro: PR binary plus git 2.45.0 on the PATH.\n  - `.g3/prod.sh eg git245 cl2 … index --head`: exit 0, spy log shows `[-c] [fetch.negotiationAlgorithm=noop] [fetch] [origin] … [--filter=blob:none] [--stdin]`. Its parent is `log --name-only` (FileCochanges, git.go:1248).\n  - `commit HEAD`: same spawn, parent `diff --find-renames` (ChangedFiles, git.go:1164).\n- Impact: the PR's invariant \"≥2.45 ⇒ no fetch process ever started\" is false. On Git for Windows 2.45.0.windows.1 (admitted by the parser), the spawned fetch runs v2.45.0 transport.c:1144 `is_file(url)` (a stat) before the :1147 `transport_check_allowed`. A UNC promisor URL therefore means SMB egress. That is exactly the bug the old refusal existed for.\n- **Required change:**\n  - Raise the floor to 2.45.1. This means parsing the patch level: refuse 2.45.0, 2.45.0.windows.1 and 2.45.0.rcN; admit 2.45.1.windows.1.\n  - Fix the test pins `lazy_fetch_guard_test.go:77 {\"2.45.0\", true}` and `:24`, and add a test that refuses 2.45.0.\n  - Fix the citation, and point `lazy_fetch_guard.go:15-23`, docs/trust-and-security.md:40-41, docs/semantic-provider-requirements.md:432, CHANGELOG.md:22 and provider.go:18957-18959 at 2.45.1.\n  - Optional: admit the maint backports (2.44.1+ and the others listed above). Refusing them is safe, just over-strict.\n\n## Item by item\n**1. Version gate: FAIL**\n- Floor: the 2.45.0 defect above.\n- Vendor suffixes parse correctly: `2.45.2.windows.1`, `2.39.5 (Apple Git-154)` and rc forms (test :24-41 green, `go test ./internal/gitutil -run …LazyFetch…` exit 0). Local /usr/bin/git is 2.50.1 (Apple Git-155) and honours the variable (raw probes a1/a2: no fetch).\n- Unknown versions fail closed on every path (LookPath, Stat, run, timeout, parse all return the zero value with Effective=false; lazy_fetch_guard.go:63-89).\n- **Probe/use cwd mismatch, new, medium-low.** The probe runs in `os.TempDir()` (lazy_fetch_guard.go:78) while real calls run in the repo. A cwd-sensitive shim (asdf/mise-style `.tool-versions`) can probe 2.54 and then execute a different Git in the repo.\n  - Repro: `.g3/shim/git` plus `.tool-versions` set to `git 2.44.0` in the clone. eg exit 0. Shim log: `2.54.0 cwd=/var/folders/…/T argv: version`, then every repo call is `2.44.0`, and a `run_command: git -c fetch… fetch origin` child appears (stopped only by GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL; missing stays 1).\n  - Fix: probe with Dir set to the repo root and key the cache by dir, or pin the resolved binary.\n- PATH swap within a process: not possible (both lookups use the process PATH; nothing calls Setenv PATH).\n- Same size+mtime binary swap or symlink retarget: needs write access to the toolchain, so outside the threat model. The cache lives only for the process, which is a short-lived CLI. Optionally add inode/ctime to the key.\n\n**2. Env coverage: PASS (with a weak static test)**\n- The only launch sites are git.go:2712 and :2898. No go-git. `entireio/cli` is imported only for `palette`.\n- No `git grep`, gc, maintenance or upload-pack ever appeared in any spy log.\n- Hostile repo config on an admitted partial clone:\n  - Config tried: core.fsmonitor, sshCommand, credential.helper, uploadpack.packObjectsHook, diff.external, textconv/filter clean/smudge/process via `.gitattributes`, core.hooksPath hooks (incl. pre-auto-gc), protocol.ext.allow=always, gitProxy, askPass, gpg.program with showSignature, gc.auto=1, maintenance.auto, an `ext::` promisor URL.\n  - Ran index, query (head and worktree), snapshot, snapshot --worktree, commit, neighbors, impact on 2.54: **0 PWN files**, missing stays 1.\n  - Control: raw unguarded git on the same fixture creates PWN-ext, PWN-fsmonitor and PWN-process, so the fixture is live.\n- Includes are still refused (provider.go:18072). Alternates are still checked (provider.go:18593+). Neither path changed.\n- Static test weakness: `TestEveryGitSubprocessIsBuiltByTheGuardedConstructors` misses an aliased import and package-level func values. Adding `internal/sem/zz_evade.go` with `import ex \"os/exec\"; var launch = ex.CommandContext; ex.Command(\"git\",\"fetch\")` leaves the test green (exit 0); file then removed. Suggested fix: match on the import path or use go/types, and scan package-level var initializers. Low severity: it is a tripwire, not a proof.\n\n**3. Coverage on ≥2.45.1: PASS.** Spy runs on 2.54 found 0 fetches each for:\n- cat-file --batch-command, ls-tree -l, git grep over a tree with a missing blob, log --name-only with an inexact rename, diff --find-renames.\n- Missing objects become errors: `lazy fetching disabled…` / `could not fetch <oid>`.\n- Submodules: `submodule.recurse=false` is pinned and grep uses `--no-recurse-submodules`. No read command auto-runs gc or maintenance.\n- On 2.45.0, grep and cat-file are also clean (fetch_if_missing); only the rename and diff prefetch leaks.\n- Upstream master (lazy-fetch trusted-bit, 2026-10-22) still checks the variable before spawn (promisor-remote.c:328). `uploadpack.lazyFetchTrusted` is protected config used by upload-pack only, so it does not affect eg.\n\n**4. Core repro on 2.54: PASS.** Fixtures via `.g3/mkfix.sh`, `--missing=print` count = 1 each.\n- cl1 (HEAD blob missing) and cl2 (history rename blob missing), production binary through the PATH and GIT_EXEC_PATH spy: index, query --head, query (worktree), snapshot, neighbors, impact all exit 0, 0 fetch children, every call carries `NLF=1 GAP=`, missing_after=1.\n- cl1 index reports `E_FILE_READ` for gone.go.\n- `snapshot --head` is not a flag; I used `snapshot` (HEAD) and `--worktree`.\n- **Warning for anyone repeating this:** the prescribed parent `GIT_TRACE=1` check proves nothing. git.go:2785 strips `GIT_TRACE*`, and no trace file was produced. That is why I used the spy plus a build with a trace variable injected.\n\n**5. Weakened builds: PASS.** The guard is load-bearing:\n- Trace build, both guards: 0 fetches.\n- Without NLF: `run_command: git -c fetch.negotiationAlgorithm=noop fetch origin … --filter=blob:none --stdin`, missing stays 1.\n- Without NLF and GAP: missing goes to **0**, files=2.\n- Source restored (`git status` clean).\n\n**6. `show -s` → `log -1 --no-walk`: PASS**\n- Byte-identical under eg's exact pins on root, merge and SSH-signed+notes commits. 18 hostile repo configs tried (showSignature, format.pretty, decorate, color.ui=always, abbrev, follow, diffMerges, notes, …); 51/51 rows exact against `rev-parse` (.g3/cmp6.sh).\n- On the partial clone with a rename+edit HEAD: show exits 128, log exits 0 with exact output.\n- Pre-existing, not a regression: repo `i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-16` re-encodes the output under both forms. eg fails closed: `git log returned malformed HEAD commit/tree metadata`, exit 1, which is a DoS only. Optional fix: pin `i18n.logOutputEncoding`.\n\n**7. Messages and docs: FAIL**\n- \"Git 2.45 or newer reads partial clones offline\" is false for 2.45.0.\n- \"predates 2.45, so it ignores GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH\" is false for 2.44.1+ and the other maint releases. For an unknown version it asserts \"predates\" without knowing (provider.go:18952-18959).\n- Diagnosis re-probes on its own (provider.go:18930). A transient probe timeout in the safety check followed by a successful probe in the diagnosis produces a diagnosis that blames nothing.\n- The CHANGELOG says partial clones \"now work\", but `commit HEAD` on 2.54 exits 1 on the rename fixture, and co-change is silently dropped (the PR notes the co-change case).\n\n**Not tested:** a real Windows / Git for Windows 2.45.0 UNC SMB stat; that rests on a source citation only (transport.c:1144 vs :1147). macOS autofs `/net` stat egress. A real asdf/mise install (simulated with a shim instead). The full package test suites were not run (CPU discipline). I recorded nothing in the Brain store because it is shared state. Worth recording: the GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH chokepoint arrived in 2.45.1 and the 2024-04 maint releases, not in 2.45.0.\n"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
