{"parentUuid":"f43055c2-0bf8-421e-8174-d3f111a451d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2Udchhbvixv36TFVwZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed in git's source that the early-exit check is missing in promisor-remote.c at v2.45.0/v2.44.0 but present at v2.44.1, v2.45.1, and v2.46.0, so the minimum required version is 2.45.1. I'll send agent #372 back with the needed changes.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2276,"cache_read_input_tokens":464363,"output_tokens":2419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":249},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2276,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2419,"cache_read_input_tokens":464363,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2276},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"9b9ae2c3-90d0-4fc7-938b-af38a8fffba7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgN2UdDeKoSGdsmCQXkfx","requestRef":"fcb7ef11-db85-4dae-b048-f2012ca055ad","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b8e9f654-83a0-4e9d-bac8-1af3d7234f8c","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:41:49.397Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"b8e9f654-83a0-4e9d-bac8-1af3d7234f8c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2Udchhbvixv36TFVwZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AACPN1NDhuY2R6pxxyw27x","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"BLOCKING: #372 floor must be 2.45.1 + 4 fixes","message":"An independent adversarial review found a **blocking** defect in #372. I verified the core claim myself: `promisor-remote.c` contains the `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` early return in `fetch_objects()` at v2.44.1, v2.45.1 and v2.46.0, but NOT at v2.45.0 or v2.44.0.\n\nThe check came from 7b70e9efb18c (\"upload-pack: disable lazy-fetching by default\"), which shipped in the 2024-04 security releases: 2.39.4, 2.40.2, 2.41.1, 2.42.2, 2.43.4, 2.44.1 and **2.45.1**. Your citation `2c206fc` does not resolve.\n\nIn 2.45.0 the variable only sets `fetch_if_missing=0` (environment.c:211). Rename-detection prefetch (diffcore-rename.c:125/897, diff.c:6960) calls `promisor_remote_get_direct` without checking it.\n\nThe reviewer built git 2.45.0 from source (`/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review/.g3/git245`) and reproduced:\n- The PR binary with 2.45.0 on PATH spawns `git fetch origin … --filter=blob:none --stdin` from `log --name-only` (FileCochanges, git.go:1248) and from `diff --find-renames` (ChangedFiles, git.go:1164).\n- It is stopped only by GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL. On Git for Windows 2.45.0, `transport.c:1144 is_file(url)` stats a UNC promisor URL before the allowlist check, which is SMB egress.\n\nTheir scripts and fixtures (mkfix.sh, prod.sh, the shim) are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review/.g3/`. Reuse them.\n\n## Required changes. Push to the same branch, no force-push\n1. **Floor = 2.45.1.**\n   - Parse the patch level. Refuse 2.45.0, `2.45.0.windows.1` and `2.45.0.rcN`. Admit `2.45.1.windows.1` and above.\n   - Admitting the maint backports is optional; refusing them is safe. Keep it simple unless it's trivial and tested.\n   - Fix `lazy_fetch_guard_test.go:77 {\"2.45.0\", true}` and `:24`. Add explicit refuse cases for 2.45.0 and its vendor forms.\n   - Fix the citation, and every \"2.45\" claim: lazy_fetch_guard.go:15-23, docs/trust-and-security.md:40-41, docs/semantic-provider-requirements.md:432, CHANGELOG.md:22, provider.go:18957-18959.\n   - **Weakening:** set the floor back to 2.45.0 and show the new refuse test goes red. If feasible, add an integration test using the built 2.45.0 binary, skipped when it's absent. At minimum, put the reviewer's repro in the PR body.\n2. **Probe/use cwd mismatch (medium-low).**\n   - The probe runs in `os.TempDir()` (lazy_fetch_guard.go:78), but real calls run in the repo. A cwd-sensitive shim (asdf or mise `.tool-versions`) can probe 2.54 and then run 2.44 in the repo; the reviewer reproduced this with `.g3/shim`.\n   - Fix: probe with `Dir` = the repo root, and key the cache by the resolved dir; or resolve and pin the exact binary path used for every later call.\n   - Add a test with a cwd-sensitive fake git.\n3. **Static launch test misses aliases.**\n   - `import ex \"os/exec\"; var launch = ex.CommandContext; ex.Command(\"git\",\"fetch\")` passes `TestEveryGitSubprocessIsBuiltByTheGuardedConstructors`.\n   - Match on the import path, not the identifier; go/types is fine. Also scan package-level var initializers and func values.\n   - Weaken it with exactly that evasion file and show it goes red.\n4. **Messages and docs.**\n   - \"predates 2.45\" is false for the 2.44.1+ maint releases, and for an unknown version it asserts something it doesn't know (provider.go:18952-18959). Say \"lazy fetch cannot be proven disabled for this Git (<version>)\".\n   - The diagnosis re-probes on its own (provider.go:18930), so a transient timeout can produce a diagnosis that blames nothing. Use the same probe result as the safety check.\n   - The CHANGELOG overclaims \"partial clones now work\". `commit HEAD` exits 1 on a rename-fixture partial clone, and co-change can drop (#378 adds the warning). State exactly what works.\n5. Optional and cheap: pin `-c i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-8` on the HEAD-metadata log call (a pre-existing DoS with a UTF-16 repo config).\n\nNote for your tests: git.go:2785 strips `GIT_TRACE*`, so a parent-level `GIT_TRACE` check proves nothing. Use the spy git or a trace-injected build, as the reviewer did.\n\n## Done means\n- All of the above, each with a red-then-restored weakening.\n- Focused tests with `-race` under mlock, plus the gitutil and sem packages.\n- Push, then watch CI to a result.\n- Update the PR body: the corrected floor, which guard does the work, and the probe-cwd fix.\n- Report per the protocol.","type":"message","recipient":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"An independent adversarial review found a **block…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2276,"cache_read_input_tokens":464363,"output_tokens":2419,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":249},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2276,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2419,"cache_read_input_tokens":464363,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2276},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AACPN1NDhuY2R6pxxyw27x":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"BLOCKING: #372 floor must be 2.45.1 + 4 fixes","message":"An independent adversarial review found a **blocking** defect in #372. I verified the core claim myself: `promisor-remote.c` contains the `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH` early return in `fetch_objects()` at v2.44.1, v2.45.1 and v2.46.0, but NOT at v2.45.0 or v2.44.0.\n\nThe check came from 7b70e9efb18c (\"upload-pack: disable lazy-fetching by default\"), which shipped in the 2024-04 security releases: 2.39.4, 2.40.2, 2.41.1, 2.42.2, 2.43.4, 2.44.1 and **2.45.1**. Your citation `2c206fc` does not resolve.\n\nIn 2.45.0 the variable only sets `fetch_if_missing=0` (environment.c:211). Rename-detection prefetch (diffcore-rename.c:125/897, diff.c:6960) calls `promisor_remote_get_direct` without checking it.\n\nThe reviewer built git 2.45.0 from source (`/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review/.g3/git245`) and reproduced:\n- The PR binary with 2.45.0 on PATH spawns `git fetch origin … --filter=blob:none --stdin` from `log --name-only` (FileCochanges, git.go:1248) and from `diff --find-renames` (ChangedFiles, git.go:1164).\n- It is stopped only by GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL. On Git for Windows 2.45.0, `transport.c:1144 is_file(url)` stats a UNC promisor URL before the allowlist check, which is SMB egress.\n\nTheir scripts and fixtures (mkfix.sh, prod.sh, the shim) are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review/.g3/`. Reuse them.\n\n## Required changes. Push to the same branch, no force-push\n1. **Floor = 2.45.1.**\n   - Parse the patch level. Refuse 2.45.0, `2.45.0.windows.1` and `2.45.0.rcN`. Admit `2.45.1.windows.1` and above.\n   - Admitting the maint backports is optional; refusing them is safe. Keep it simple unless it's trivial and tested.\n   - Fix `lazy_fetch_guard_test.go:77 {\"2.45.0\", true}` and `:24`. Add explicit refuse cases for 2.45.0 and its vendor forms.\n   - Fix the citation, and every \"2.45\" claim: lazy_fetch_guard.go:15-23, docs/trust-and-security.md:40-41, docs/semantic-provider-requirements.md:432, CHANGELOG.md:22, provider.go:18957-18959.\n   - **Weakening:** set the floor back to 2.45.0 and show the new refuse test goes red. If feasible, add an integration test using the built 2.45.0 binary, skipped when it's absent. At minimum, put the reviewer's repro in the PR body.\n2. **Probe/use cwd mismatch (medium-low).**\n   - The probe runs in `os.TempDir()` (lazy_fetch_guard.go:78), but real calls run in the repo. A cwd-sensitive shim (asdf or mise `.tool-versions`) can probe 2.54 and then run 2.44 in the repo; the reviewer reproduced this with `.g3/shim`.\n   - Fix: probe with `Dir` = the repo root, and key the cache by the resolved dir; or resolve and pin the exact binary path used for every later call.\n   - Add a test with a cwd-sensitive fake git.\n3. **Static launch test misses aliases.**\n   - `import ex \"os/exec\"; var launch = ex.CommandContext; ex.Command(\"git\",\"fetch\")` passes `TestEveryGitSubprocessIsBuiltByTheGuardedConstructors`.\n   - Match on the import path, not the identifier; go/types is fine. Also scan package-level var initializers and func values.\n   - Weaken it with exactly that evasion file and show it goes red.\n4. **Messages and docs.**\n   - \"predates 2.45\" is false for the 2.44.1+ maint releases, and for an unknown version it asserts something it doesn't know (provider.go:18952-18959). Say \"lazy fetch cannot be proven disabled for this Git (<version>)\".\n   - The diagnosis re-probes on its own (provider.go:18930), so a transient timeout can produce a diagnosis that blames nothing. Use the same probe result as the safety check.\n   - The CHANGELOG overclaims \"partial clones now work\". `commit HEAD` exits 1 on a rename-fixture partial clone, and co-change can drop (#378 adds the warning). State exactly what works.\n5. Optional and cheap: pin `-c i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-8` on the HEAD-metadata log call (a pre-existing DoS with a UTF-16 repo config).\n\nNote for your tests: git.go:2785 strips `GIT_TRACE*`, so a parent-level `GIT_TRACE` check proves nothing. Use the spy git or a trace-injected build, as the reviewer did.\n\n## Done means\n- All of the above, each with a red-then-restored weakening.\n- Focused tests with `-race` under mlock, plus the gitutil and sem packages.\n- Push, then watch CI to a result.\n- Update the PR body: the corrected floor, which guard does the work, and the probe-cwd fix.\n- Report per the protocol."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9b9ae2c3-90d0-4fc7-938b-af38a8fffba7","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgN2UdDeKoSGdsmCQXkfx","requestRef":"fcb7ef11-db85-4dae-b048-f2012ca055ad","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3fb83abb-532c-4d3f-bee9-292bdda90766","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:42:03.848Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
