{"parentUuid":"8e7d632d-b63f-430b-9f93-e98ea191ea0e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2WMe54emiZG565upBF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NJvt3rghxNhL7ekexcAyok","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"entire brain memories retract --help 2>&1 | grep -E 'Usage|--' | head -6; entire brain memories retract fact:0e3ce1673cd4981e07318b7d --branch main --json 2>&1 | tail -3; entire brain remember \"entire-graph may admit partial clones (promisor remotes, e.g. blob:none) only when the runtime Git is >= 2.45.1, NOT 2.45.0. The GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH early return in promisor-remote.c fetch_objects() arrived in commit 7b70e9efb18c via the 2024-04 security releases (2.39.4, 2.40.2, 2.41.1, 2.42.2, 2.43.4, 2.44.1, 2.45.1); in 2.45.0 the variable only sets fetch_if_missing=0, and rename-detection prefetch (diffcore-rename.c, diff.c) still spawns 'git fetch' (reproduced with git 2.45.0 built from source). GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 is the load-bearing guard on >=2.45.1; GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL= is a second layer (fetch attempted then refused; on Git for Windows the transport stats a UNC URL before the allowlist check, so it is not sufficient alone). Probe the Git version in the repo's own cwd (shims like asdf/mise are cwd-sensitive). Avoid 'git show -s' on partial clones; use 'git log -1 --no-walk'. (PR #372 review)\" --path constraints.git.invariant --branch main --json 2>&1 | grep -E '\"id\"' | head -1","description":"Retract the wrong 2.45 fact and record the corrected one"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3061,"cache_read_input_tokens":466639,"output_tokens":665,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3061,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0