{"parentUuid":"b9b3d7d8-0a84-474e-bdef-472aeea9a0a5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN2X2Cp5HdkKZErgRuXe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018J344f15hkJvj4bKcstkmu","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Correction: #372 floor is 2.45.1, not 2.45.0","message":"Correction to what I told you about #372, found by an independent adversarial review and verified by me from git's source.\n\n**The GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH early return is NOT in git 2.45.0.** It's in `promisor-remote.c` `fetch_objects()` at v2.44.1, v2.45.1 and v2.46.0, but absent at v2.45.0 and v2.44.0. It came from 7b70e9efb18c in the 2024-04 security releases (2.39.4 / 2.40.2 / 2.41.1 / 2.42.2 / 2.43.4 / 2.44.1 / 2.45.1).\n\nIn 2.45.0 the variable only sets `fetch_if_missing=0`, so rename-detection prefetch still spawns `git fetch`. The reviewer built 2.45.0 from source, and the PR binary spawned a fetch from `log --name-only` and `diff --find-renames`, stopped only by GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL. On Git for Windows 2.45.0, the transport stats a UNC URL before the allowlist check.\n\n- **#372 is back in progress:** floor 2.45.1, probe the version in the repo's own cwd (asdf/mise shims are cwd-sensitive), a stronger static launch test, and corrected messages. It is NOT ready until re-verified.\n- **Your entiredb re-index on that binary was safe:** this machine runs git 2.54.0, which is above the corrected floor.\n- **Brain fact corrected:** I retracted `fact:0e3ce1673cd4981e07318b7d` (which said ≥2.45) and recorded `fact:d2e8201fb1ec8478625f97ee` with the 2.45.1 floor and the reasons. If you copied the 2.45 number anywhere on your side, fix it too.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Correction to what I told you about #372, found b…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":nul