{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"af4421aa2f74a0e5b2aee29de148a0752a4a281443a66bef2e3f517ad171e7cb","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018J344f15hkJvj4bKcstkmu","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Correction: #372 floor is 2.45.1, not 2.45.0","message":"Correction to what I told you about #372, found by an independent adversarial review and verified by me from git's source.\n\n**The GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH early return is NOT in git 2.45.0.** It's in `promisor-remote.c` `fetch_objects()` at v2.44.1, v2.45.1 and v2.46.0, but absent at v2.45.0 and v2.44.0. It came from 7b70e9efb18c in the 2024-04 security releases (2.39.4 / 2.40.2 / 2.41.1 / 2.42.2 / 2.43.4 / 2.44.1 / 2.45.1).\n\nIn 2.45.0 the variable only sets `fetch_if_missing=0`, so rename-detection prefetch still spawns `git fetch`. The reviewer built 2.45.0 from source, and the PR binary spawned a fetch from `log --name-only` and `diff --find-renames`, stopped only by GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL. On Git for Windows 2.45.0, the transport stats a UNC URL before the allowlist check.\n\n- **#372 is back in progress:** floor 2.45.1, probe the version in the repo's own cwd (asdf/mise shims are cwd-sensitive), a stronger static launch test, and corrected messages. It is NOT ready until re-verified.\n- **Your entiredb re-index on that binary was safe:** this machine runs git 2.54.0, which is above the corrected floor.\n- **Brain fact corrected:** I retracted `fact:0e3ce1673cd4981e07318b7d` (which said ≥2.45) and recorded `fact:d2e8201fb1ec8478625f97ee` with the 2.45.1 floor and the reasons. If you copied the 2.45 number anywhere on your side, fix it too."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WTkQdQFYHJr1pn5J2aVEc1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G3-Ba'].update(status='doing', note='BLOCKING, found by the D-review: the floor must be git 2.45.1, not 2.45.0 (GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH early return absent in v2.45.0 source; reproduced a fetch with git 2.45.0 built from source). Also: probe the version in the repo cwd (shim bypass), a static launch test that catches aliased imports, corrected messages/CHANGELOG. Original agent resumed. Brain fact corrected (retracted 0e3ce167, recorded d2e8201f).')\nT['D-review-372'].update(status='done', note='Verdict: UNSAFE as written → SAFE WITH CHANGES once floor = 2.45.1. Env coverage PASS (15 hostile repo configs, 0 PWN); coverage on ≥2.45.1 PASS; show -s → log PASS. Verified the core claim from git source tags. A re-review is needed after the fix.')\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Mark 372 blocked on the floor fix on the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
