{"parentUuid":"8c24e6a1-ab2b-4355-a8d4-ffc53bba45d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN3HifcmzfTJiYu8TRP9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"output_tokens":3838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":505},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3838,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5117,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"2e14eea4-e137-4459-a9eb-651f19caebb9","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgN3HhJmTH7AkFsPSye8v","requestRef":"54cc9833-278e-4a93-9206-15a73319e056","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"43f76007-a509-4f5a-93b5-2102098ceb23","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:52:30.454Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"43f76007-a509-4f5a-93b5-2102098ceb23","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN3HifcmzfTJiYu8TRP9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The per-commit index design is done: `devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md`. It found more than the original gap:\n\n- **Brain's background watcher has never rebuilt the code index.** Its log has 40,499 lines with 0 code-index runs, because every refresh fails earlier (dirty worktree, incomplete checkpoint scope, and so on) and aborts before that step.\n- **Brain and agents build two different graph caches for the same commit.** Brain passes `--ignore-file .brainignore`, so agents' graph queries never warm Brain's cache, and every commit costs two full parses.\n- **Serving the previous commit's index by default would break Brain's freshness check,** so it has to be opt-in and only on `graph context`.\n- **Each new commit's store costs 68–196 MB,** and nothing ever deletes old ones.\n\nThe recommendation splits the work by side. **Graph (mine):**\n- clean up old stores;\n- an opt-in `--allow-ancestor` on `graph context`, which serves a recent commit's index only when changes are small (up to 5 commits back and 5% of files) and marks what's stale.\n\n**Brain:** run the code-index step on its own, so it no longer depends on the rest of refresh succeeding. Then pass the new flag, and rebuild in the background on a miss.\n\nSending the Brain side to the Brain session and starting the graph-side store cleanup:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"output_tokens":3838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":505},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3838,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"2e14eea4-e137-4459-a9eb-651f19caebb9","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgN3HhJmTH7AkFsPSye8v","requestRef":"54cc9833-278e-4a93-9206-15a73319e056","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"29b70d5f-e4be-435f-8c33-c42251797b15","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:52:34.909Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"29b70d5f-e4be-435f-8c33-c42251797b15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN3HifcmzfTJiYu8TRP9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HELFDyE3ThT19fYgCCy58B","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Per-commit store design: 3 brain findings + split","message":"Design for \"brief drops code context after every commit\" is done: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md` (244 lines). Three findings are in your lane. Please verify them, since they came from a read-only pass against origin/main 9309afa1; your main checkout is detached at e6bb5c42, which predates graph_store.go.\n\n1. **The watch daemon has never reached the code-index step.** watch.log has 40,499 lines, **0 `code index` runs**, and 19 failed refreshes: dirty_worktree 7, checkpoint_scope_incomplete 7, retain 3, schema skew 1, git 1. Every failure aborts before the semantic phase. Full refresh is also throttled to 30 min (watch.go:118). The fingerprint covers only checkpoint refs + HEAD (watch.go:654), so a graph provider-version bump or an ignore-file change invalidates every store unnoticed.\n2. **Variant mismatch.** Brief passes `--ignore-file .brainignore` (graph_context.go, semantic.go:1279), so its cache key differs from agents' `graph query --head --profile full`. Agent traffic never warms brief's store, and each commit costs 2 full parses (10.8 s each on entire-graph).\n3. **Brief relies on exact keying for freshness** (agent_surface.go:1487; `semanticRefreshNeeded` compares the `graph store` descriptor, refresh.go:738). So an ancestor fallback must NOT go into `graph store`, or Brain would never rebuild.\n\n**Proposed split. Comment on the interface before G1 lands, since you're its consumer.**\n- **G2, graph (starting now):** store sidecar retention, keeping the newest K. A store is 68-196 MB each, and per-commit builds would grow it without bound. This lands with or before B1.\n- **G1, graph:** `graph context --allow-ancestor N`, used only when N ≤ 5 and changed files are ≤ 5% of indexed files. It drops records in changed files and returns a `stale` block: the ancestor commit, the changed files, and the age in commits. `graph store` stays exact. Measured staleness of relations touching changed files: 0.05% at HEAD~1, 3.5% at HEAD~5, 14.6% at HEAD~10.\n- **B1, brain:** a code-index step that is independent of the refresh outcome and exempt from the 30-min throttle, triggered on HEAD tree + provider version + ignore-file hash.\n- **B2, brain:** brief passes `--allow-ancestor`, renders one staleness line, and degrades to today's call on an older graph.\n- **B3, brain:** a detached build kick on a miss, under a lock with a cooldown.\n- **Separate decision:** align on `.brainignore` (one cache variant), which would also allow writing the store when the graph persists anyway.\n\nThe full doc has the measurements and the options it rejected: incremental build is deferred, because the global relation passes make it a big correctness surface while a full build is only 11-15 s. Your fact 79fe8eae (a partial snapshot gives confident negatives) is why any lazy build must be complete-or-nothing.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Design for \"brief drops code context after every …"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"output_tokens":3838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":505},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3838,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HELFDyE3ThT19fYgCCy58B":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Per-commit store design: 3 brain findings + split","message":"Design for \"brief drops code context after every commit\" is done: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md` (244 lines). Three findings are in your lane. Please verify them, since they came from a read-only pass against origin/main 9309afa1; your main checkout is detached at e6bb5c42, which predates graph_store.go.\n\n1. **The watch daemon has never reached the code-index step.** watch.log has 40,499 lines, **0 `code index` runs**, and 19 failed refreshes: dirty_worktree 7, checkpoint_scope_incomplete 7, retain 3, schema skew 1, git 1. Every failure aborts before the semantic phase. Full refresh is also throttled to 30 min (watch.go:118). The fingerprint covers only checkpoint refs + HEAD (watch.go:654), so a graph provider-version bump or an ignore-file change invalidates every store unnoticed.\n2. **Variant mismatch.** Brief passes `--ignore-file .brainignore` (graph_context.go, semantic.go:1279), so its cache key differs from agents' `graph query --head --profile full`. Agent traffic never warms brief's store, and each commit costs 2 full parses (10.8 s each on entire-graph).\n3. **Brief relies on exact keying for freshness** (agent_surface.go:1487; `semanticRefreshNeeded` compares the `graph store` descriptor, refresh.go:738). So an ancestor fallback must NOT go into `graph store`, or Brain would never rebuild.\n\n**Proposed split. Comment on the interface before G1 lands, since you're its consumer.**\n- **G2, graph (starting now):** store sidecar retention, keeping the newest K. A store is 68-196 MB each, and per-commit builds would grow it without bound. This lands with or before B1.\n- **G1, graph:** `graph context --allow-ancestor N`, used only when N ≤ 5 and changed files are ≤ 5% of indexed files. It drops records in changed files and returns a `stale` block: the ancestor commit, the changed files, and the age in commits. `graph store` stays exact. Measured staleness of relations touching changed files: 0.05% at HEAD~1, 3.5% at HEAD~5, 14.6% at HEAD~10.\n- **B1, brain:** a code-index step that is independent of the refresh outcome and exempt from the 30-min throttle, triggered on HEAD tree + provider version + ignore-file hash.\n- **B2, brain:** brief passes `--allow-ancestor`, renders one staleness line, and degrades to today's call on an older graph.\n- **B3, brain:** a detached build kick on a miss, under a lock with a cooldown.\n- **Separate decision:** align on `.brainignore` (one cache variant), which would also allow writing the store when the graph persists anyway.\n\nThe full doc has the measurements and the options it rejected: incremental build is deferred, because the global relation passes make it a big correctness surface while a full build is only 11-15 s. Your fact 79fe8eae (a partial snapshot gives confident negatives) is why any lazy build must be complete-or-nothing."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2e14eea4-e137-4459-a9eb-651f19caebb9","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgN3HhJmTH7AkFsPSye8v","requestRef":"54cc9833-278e-4a93-9206-15a73319e056","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"788866ac-ff9e-456d-ac20-9962524ef48a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:52:44.765Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"788866ac-ff9e-456d-ac20-9962524ef48a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN3HifcmzfTJiYu8TRP9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RTdrMXqQ4VSAwWwTRXZZ9S","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"G2: search store retention","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph fix as one open PR. Follow `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock`, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\nBranch `fix/search-store-retention`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-store-retention`.\n\n## Item G2: bound the sqlite search-store sidecars\nRead `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md` first, especially the current-behaviour section and the G2 item.\n\n**Today.**\n- The search store is a sqlite sidecar beside a gz cache entry, with the same key (search_cache.go:1160-1226).\n- It is written only when `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1` (search_store.go:640-647).\n- There is **no eviction** (search_cache.go:19).\n- Each store is 68 MB (entire-graph), 126 MB (cli) or 196 MB (entire-brain), versus 3.5-7 MB for the gz.\n- Entire Brain is about to build one per commit (median 17 min between commits on an active repo), so disk grows without bound.\n\n**Implement retention.** Keep the newest K store sidecars per repo/scope, and evict older ones when a new one is written.\n- Find how the cache dir is laid out per repo and scope.\n- Choose K deliberately: a default of a few is fine. Justify it, and consider a size cap as well as a count cap. Make it configurable only if there is an existing config convention; do not invent a new flag casually.\n- **Eviction must be safe with concurrent readers** (Brain's `graph context` may have a store open while another process writes a new one):\n  - never delete a store another process is reading, OR rely on unlink semantics and prove it (on Windows an open file cannot be deleted, so handle that error gracefully);\n  - never evict the store just written, nor the current HEAD's.\n  - Use the existing cross-process build lock if there is one (the design mentions a 60 s wait lock).\n- Only evict store sidecars. Leave the gz cache entries alone unless they already have a policy.\n- Run `entire graph impact` on the store write and open functions first.\n\n## Done means\n- **Tests**, each weakened to red and then restored:\n  - writing K+1 stores leaves K;\n  - the newest store and the current one are never evicted;\n  - a store held open by a reader survives, or eviction fails gracefully: simulate the Windows case;\n  - a concurrent writer and evictor under `-race`.\n- **Live check:** build stores for 3 commits of a small repo with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1` and a small K. Show the directory sizes before and after.\n- PR open, CI watched, Entire Gates findings checked via the org trail number, and the report per the protocol."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"output_tokens":3838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":505},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":3838,"cache_read_input_tokens":477509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RTdrMXqQ4VSAwWwTRXZZ9S":{"description":"G2: search store retention","model":"opus","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"You implement ONE entire-graph fix as one open PR. Follow `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md` exactly: worktree, graph/brain-first, `mlock`, `-race`, mutation-proven tests, PR rules, scratch in the worktree, report format. Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\nBranch `fix/search-store-retention`, worktree `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-store-retention`.\n\n## Item G2: bound the sqlite search-store sidecars\nRead `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/GRAPH-STORE-PER-COMMIT-DESIGN.md` first, especially the current-behaviour section and the G2 item.\n\n**Today.**\n- The search store is a sqlite sidecar beside a gz cache entry, with the same key (search_cache.go:1160-1226).\n- It is written only when `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1` (search_store.go:640-647).\n- There is **no eviction** (search_cache.go:19).\n- Each store is 68 MB (entire-graph), 126 MB (cli) or 196 MB (entire-brain), versus 3.5-7 MB for the gz.\n- Entire Brain is about to build one per commit (median 17 min between commits on an active repo), so disk grows without bound.\n\n**Implement retention.** Keep the newest K store sidecars per repo/scope, and evict older ones when a new one is written.\n- Find how the cache dir is laid out per repo and scope.\n- Choose K deliberately: a default of a few is fine. Justify it, and consider a size cap as well as a count cap. Make it configurable only if there is an existing config convention; do not invent a new flag casually.\n- **Eviction must be safe with concurrent readers** (Brain's `graph context` may have a store open while another process writes a new one):\n  - never delete a store another process is reading, OR rely on unlink semantics and prove it (on Windows an open file cannot be deleted, so handle that error gracefully);\n  - never evict the store just written, nor the current HEAD's.\n  - Use the existing cross-process build lock if there is one (the design mentions a 60 s wait lock).\n- Only evict store sidecars. Leave the gz cache entries alone unless they already have a policy.\n- Run `entire graph impact` on the store write and open functions first.\n\n## Done means\n- **Tests**, each weakened to red and then restored:\n  - writing K+1 stores leaves K;\n  - the newest store and the current one are never evicted;\n  - a store held open by a reader survives, or eviction fails gracefully: simulate the Windows case;\n  - a concurrent writer and evictor under `-race`.\n- **Live check:** build stores for 3 commits of a small repo with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_SEARCH_STORE=1` and a small K. Show the directory sizes before and after.\n- PR open, CI watched, Entire Gates findings checked via the org trail number, and the report per the protocol."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"2e14eea4-e137-4459-a9eb-651f19caebb9","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgN3HhJmTH7AkFsPSye8v","requestRef":"54cc9833-278e-4a93-9206-15a73319e056","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aca053c9-3f15-4162-b93c-2c5ec8101fba","timestamp":"2026-10-25T00:52:55.267Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
