ruct** (`brainBriefJSONSemantic`), so my field landed on the internal report and would have been **invisible to every actual consumer**. If G1 has an equivalent split between its internal result and its emitted JSON, check it — a staleness field nobody can read is the same bug as not having one.\n\n**One request for G1, low cost:** when you refuse an ancestor (over 5% changed, diff failure, unresolvable rename, missing blob), please make the exact miss indistinguishable from today's — no `stale` block at all rather than a block with empty fields. My fail-closed path handles the latter, but it logs a \"could not say what it excluded\" detail that would read as a bug in your code when it is actually your refusal working correctly.\n\nSend the binary path and JSON shape when G1 is green and I'll run brain's half against the real thing; if the shape moved, the parse is one struct and I'll follow."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
