ilt git 2.45.1 and 2.44.1 from source (sha256 verified) and reused the reviewer's 2.44.0 and 2.45.0 builds. With GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 and a spy git in GIT_EXEC_PATH:\n     - 2.44.0 and 2.45.0 start a fetch on `log --name-only` and `diff --find-renames` (2.44.0 also on cat-file).\n     - 2.44.1, 2.45.1, Apple 2.50.1 and 2.54.0 start none.\n   - New tests built on this:\n     - gitutil oracle `TestLazyFetchGuardMatchesObservedGitBehaviour`: fails if any Git the guard admits starts a fetch.\n     - cli product oracle `TestNoProviderCommandStartsALazyFetchWhicheverGitIsOnPath`: index, query, diff and commit for each Git on PATH.\n     - Both always check the PATH Git; the `ENTIRE_GRAPH_TEST_GITS` env var adds the source builds.\n\n2. **Probe runs in the repository directory.**\n   - `LazyFetchGuard(dir)` runs `git version` in the repo and caches by (canonical dir, binary path, size, mtime).\n   - Failures are cached too, so the refusal and its diagnosis share one answer.\n   - The diagnosis now calls the guard once and reuses that result for the decision and the text.\n   - Tests: a cwd-sensitive fake git (`.tool-versions` selects 2.44.0); a sem test that the predicate probes the repo dir; a failed-first-probe test in both gitutil and sem.\n\n3. **Static launch test is alias-proof.** It now matches by import path, covers package-level initializers and function values, rejects dot imports, `exec.Cmd` literals and `new(exec.Cmd)`, and flags wrappers used as values. The Windows `syscall.CreateProcess` surrogate is allowlisted with its reason. A self-test file contains the exact evasion.\n\n4. **Messages and changelog.**\n   - The refusal now says \"lazy fetching cannot be proven disabled for the Git on PATH (<v>)\". It never says \"predates\"; for an unknown version it says the version could not be determined.\n   - The changelog lists exactly what works: index/query --head, impact, neighbors, def, context, store, health, snapshot (all exit 0 on a rename partial clone, verified).\n   - It also lists what fails or degrades: missing HEAD blob gives E_FILE_READ; diff/commit exit 1; co-change is dropped (#378).\n\n5. **Optional item done.** `-c i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-8` is pinned on the HEAD log call. The UTF-16 failure reproduced on base too, so it was pre-existing.\n\nWeakening, each shown red then restored with a clean `git diff`:\n- floor back to 2.45.0: parse test (2.45.0, .windows.1, .rc0, .rc2), gitutil oracle (\"2.45.0 trusted but log --name-only started a lazy fetch\"), cli product oracle (git245 spawns `fetch origin --filter=blob:none --stdin`) and test (c)\n- probe in os.TempDir(): cwd test red; predicate probing elsewhere: sem probe-dir test red\n- success-only caching: both shared-probe tests red\n- evasion.go dropped into internal/gitutil: two violations reported\n- name-based scanner: alias self-test red\n- message saying \"predates\": red\n- diagnosis using its own probe: red\n- encoding pin removed: red\n- 2.44.1 backport row dropped: red\n- dropping `noLazyFetchEnv`: product oracle red on PATH Git, 2.44.1 and 2.45.1, which proves the env var is the guard doing the work\n\nLocal:\n- focused tests in gitutil, sem and cli green under `-race` with mlock\n- whole gitutil (13s) and sem (187s) packages green with `-p 1` under mlock\n\nLive: entiredb and cli `index --head` exit 0 with counts unchanged (2542 files / 36068 symbols; 1427 / 28619).\n\nN2 re-measured at load1 3.9-5.8, base → new medians, 3 reps:\n- cli: 34.26s → 2.51s\n- entiredb: 6.61s → 2.03s\n- Ordered result lists are identical to base; only provenance and the fallback warnings change.\n\nCI on 36c0cc41:\n- green: 34 checks, including test ubuntu, macOS and Windows plus all shards, lint, build×3 and CodeQL\n- failed: Entire Gates, on Approvals only (Findings passed with no blocking issues, Checks passed, up to date)\n- running: none\n\nThe PR body is rewritten:\n- corrected floor and citation\n- reviewer repro\n- Git-version oracle table\n- the one-guard-at-a-time matrix\n- the statement that GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH does the work\n- probe-cwd fix\n- site list\n- measurements\n- full weakening table\n- what works and what doesn't\n\nScratch files live in <worktree>/.g3 (shared info/exclude ignores it). Not done: a Brain fact, because the protocol forbids touching ~/.local/share/entire."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
