{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"09fa6a2845cd403c0759bdfadaa406ed79f34329c9b1276b8beaff9ff91c8314","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"#372 is fixed, and properly this time:\n- **Minimum version:** now git 2.45.1, plus the older security releases that also carry the fix.\n- **Real-git test:** the agent built several git versions from source, and a test now fails if any git the graph allows ever starts a fetch. The vulnerable versions do fetch, and every allowed one starts none.\n- **Version check:** it now runs inside the repo folder, which closes the version-manager bypass.\n- **Stray-launch test:** it can no longer be fooled by import aliases.\n- **CI:** all green.\n\nSince this PR loosens a safety guard, I'm sending the original reviewer back to try to break the fixed version:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TzdbHzAf63WkBbsK7b7GwH","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a5c431d074520beed","summary":"Re-review #372 fixes at 36c0cc41","message":"#372 has been revised in response to your review. The head is now **36c0cc41** on `fix/index-partial-clones`; confirm it with `gh pr view 372 --json headRefOid`. Re-review it adversarially with the same default stance: UNSAFE until you re-derive it yourself. Your worktree and `.g3/` (with your git 2.45.0 build) are still there. Fetch and check out the new head, detached, read-only.\n\nThe author claims:\n1. **Floor 2.45.1, PLUS a backport table:** 2.39.4, 2.40.2, 2.41.1, 2.42.2, 2.43.4, 2.44.1 and later in each line. Refused: 2.45.0, `.windows.1`, `.rcN`, `2.45.GIT`, unknown.\n   - They built 2.45.1 and 2.44.1 from source and added an oracle test `TestLazyFetchGuardMatchesObservedGitBehaviour` (gitutil), plus a product oracle `TestNoProviderCommandStartsALazyFetchWhicheverGitIsOnPath` (cli). Extra source builds come from the `ENTIRE_GRAPH_TEST_GITS` env var.\n   - **Attack the backport table hardest.** Is every admitted line's fix COMPLETE, including the rename/diff prefetch paths, not just `fetch_objects`? Check promisor-remote.c and the call sites at each admitted tag. Are there later patch releases in those lines that regressed? How does the parser handle `2.39.10` versus `2.39.4` (numeric vs lexical), and vendor strings for backport versions?\n2. **The probe runs in the repo dir**, cached by (canonical dir, binary path, size, mtime). Failures are cached, and the diagnosis reuses the same result. Re-run your cwd-sensitive shim attack.\n3. **The static launch test is alias-proof:** import-path matching, package-level initializers, func values, dot imports, `exec.Cmd` literals, `new(exec.Cmd)`, and wrappers used as values. A Windows `syscall.CreateProcess` surrogate is allowlisted. Re-run your evasion file, then try harder: reflection, `os.StartProcess`, `syscall.Exec`/`ForkExec`, cgo, a build-tagged file, a `_test.go` vs non-test file boundary, and a vendored or internal package outside the scanned roots.\n4. **Messages:** \"lazy fetching cannot be proven disabled for the Git on PATH (<v>)\". Verify there's no remaining \"predates\" or bare \"2.45\" claim anywhere.\n5. **Also re-confirm** your earlier PASS items still hold on the new head: env coverage, the hostile repo configs, 0 fetches on 2.54, `show -s` → log, and the new `i18n.logOutputEncoding` pin.\n\nLight CPU only: focused tests, your fixtures, `-race` on focused tests via `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/mlock '<cmd>'`. No full suites.\n\nReport (≤ 40 lines): a verdict of SAFE TO MERGE / SAFE WITH CHANGES / UNSAFE, then per item: verdict | evidence | required change."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TWhMEaBaqTUd7Nhidi5uSZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && entire trail finding list 2510 --status any --json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"import json,sys; d=json.load(sys.stdin); print('372 findings:', d['counts'], [(x.get('status'),x.get('severity')) for x in d.get('findings',[])])\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G3-Ba'].update(note='Fixed at 36c0cc41: floor 2.45.1 + the 2024-04 backport table (built 2.44.0/2.44.1/2.45.0/2.45.1 from source; oracle tests fail if an admitted Git fetches); probe in the repo cwd with a shared cached result; alias-proof static launch test; corrected messages/CHANGELOG; i18n encoding pin. CI 34 green; only Approvals pending. query --head cli 34.3 → 2.5 s, entiredb 6.6 → 2.0 s. RE-REVIEW running (same reviewer).')\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('board ok')\nEOF","description":"Check 372 findings and update the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
