 on the rename fixture:\n  - 2.39.4, 2.44.1 and 2.45.1 with `GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1`: exit 128, 0 fetches, missing stays 1.\n  - 2.45.0: `diff` actually fetched (missing 1→0).\n  - Control: unguarded 2.39.4 fetches, so the fixture is live.\n- **Product check.** `eg2 index --head` on cl1/cl2 plus `commit HEAD`: 2.39.4, 2.44.1, 2.45.1 and 2.54 give 0 fetch children. 2.45.0 and 2.44.0 are refused (exit 1) after a single `git version` call.\n- **Oracle tests.** Both pass with my builds passed in `ENTIRE_GRAPH_TEST_GITS`. I weakened the table to `45: 0`: both went red (`with Git \"2.45.0\" on PATH (guard effective true) provider commands started Git child commands`), then I restored it.\n- **Parser** (scratch test): 2.39.10 → true (compared numerically, not as text); 2.39.3, 2.45.0, 2.45.0.windows.1, 2.45.0.rc2, 2.45.GIT, 2.45.0.123.gX, 2.45.1-rc0, 2.44.0.vfs.0.3 → false; 2.39.5 (Apple Git-154), 2.44.1.windows.1, 2.45.1.windows.1, 2.44.1.3.gX, 2.46.0.rc0, 2.46.GIT, 2.45.2.vfs.0.0 → true. All correct.\n- **Recommended, not blocking:** CI only has Git 2.55/2.56, so the table is protected only by local runs with the env var. Add a CI job that builds at least 2.45.0 and one backport.\n\n**2. Probe in the repo dir: mostly PASS, one residual (required change)**\n- I re-ran the attack with an asdf-style shim (`.g3/shim2`, walks up from `$PWD`) via `.g3/shimrun.sh r2`. Fixed cases:\n  - (a) `.tool-versions` at the repo root: the probe now sees 2.44.0 and refuses (exit 1).\n  - (b) `--repo sub` with `sub/.tool-versions`: refused.\n  - (c) cwd = sub with no `--repo` (index and query): exit 0, and every non-probe call ran 2.54 in the root, 0 fetches.\n- **(d) Still open: a repo reached through a symlink.** `--repo evil/link`, with `link` pointing at `real/cl` and `evil/.tool-versions` selecting the old Git:\n  - The probe runs at the physical path because `lazyFetchGuardDir` calls `EvalSymlinks` (`lazy_fetch_guard.go:119-123`; the probe itself runs at `:108`). Shim log: `2.54.0 cwd=<W>/real/cl argv: version`.\n  - Every real command runs at the logical path with logical `PWD`: 16 calls as `2.44.0 cwd=<W>/evil/link`, and **1 lazy-fetch child spawned**. It was stopped only by `GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL` (missing stays 1).\n  - Severity is low: it needs a cwd-sensitive shim plus a version file in the symlink path's logical parent directories.\n  - **Required change:** run `git version` in exactly the directory string the commands use (`provider.go:18119`, `:18938`), or run every command in the canonical directory. Canonicalize only the cache key, never the probe's working directory.\n- Caching failures and sharing one result between the refusal and its diagnosis: confirmed in code (`LoadOrStore` stores the failure status too). `TestPartialCloneRefusalAndDiagnosisShareOneProbe` passes.\n\n**3. Static launch test: PARTIAL (test strength only, not blocking)**\n- My alias evasion is now caught (`zz_evade.go:5:14`, `:7:22`; test exit 1).\n- A linkname pull of `os.StartProcess` is rejected by the linker (`invalid reference to os.StartProcess`), so it is not an evasion.\n- **Still uncaught:** each of these compiles (build exit 0) and the test stays green (exit 0):\n  - a zero-value `var c exec.Cmd` followed by `c.Start()`;\n  - a struct that embeds `exec.Cmd`;\n  - `reflect.New(reflect.TypeOf((*exec.Cmd)(nil)).Elem())`;\n  - `syscall.Syscall(SYS_EXECVE, …)`;\n  - cgo `C.system`;\n  - a package under a `bin/` directory: the walker skips `bin`/`node_modules` (`lazy_fetch_guard_test.go:440`), but Go compiles the package when it is imported.\n- `_test.go` files and build-tagged files are fine: test files are never shipped, and the parser scans build-tagged files regardless of tags.\n- Shipped third-party dependencies that import `os/exec` (bubbletea, colorprofile, modernc libc) are outside the scan; none of them run git.\n- Current code has none of these evasions; only the two constructors launch git.\n- **Suggested:** enumerate files with `go list` (including CgoFiles, flagging any `import \"C\"`), flag any `os/exec.Cmd` type reference outside the allowlist, flag `Syscall*` calls with exec or spawn numbers, and stop skipping `bin/`.\n\n**4. Messages: PASS (nit)**\n- Production message: `lazy fetching cannot be proven disabled for the Git on PATH (2.45.0) … GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH stops every lazy fetch in Git 2.45.1 or newer (or 2.39.4, … 2.44.1 on an older release line)`. The unknown-version wording no longer asserts anything about the version.\n- No remaining \"predates\" or bare \"2.45\" claim in production code or docs. Stale \"2.45\" remains only in test comments and messages: `search_cache_scope_context_review_test.go:110`, `search_cache_history_review_test.go:39`, `provider_git_config_preflight_windows_test.go:28`, `git_test.go:2394`. Fix these.\n- Nit: say \"2.39.4+ …\" so the backport versions don't read as exact versions.\n\n**5. Re-confirmation of earlier PASS items: PASS**\n- **Fetch spy:** 42 spy runs (query head/worktree, snapshot, snapshot --worktree, neighbors, impact, def × cl1/cl2 × Git 2.54/2.45.0/2.39.4): 0 fetch children, 0 calls missing a guard.\n- **Hostile repo configs** (`.g3/hostile.sh`, now also with `i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-16`) on 2.54, 2.39.4 and 2.45.0: 0 PWN files, missing stays 1.\n- **HEAD lookup** with the pinned `-c i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-8` (`git.go:135`): output matches `rev-parse` on all 72 rows (51 identical to `show -s`; the rest are where `show` fails). `eg2 index --head` exits 0 on repos set to UTF-16, UTF-16LE, ISO-8859-1, EBCDIC-US and SHIFT_JIS.\n- **Optional:** FileCochanges and FindCommitWithCheckpoint still don't pin the encoding, so co-change degrades on such repos (degraded output, no egress).\n- **Focused tests under `-race`** via mlock (gitutil, sem and cli tests matching the guard, partial-clone and launch-scan names, run against the 2.39.4, 2.45.1 and 2.45.0 builds): exit 0.\n\n**Not tested:** Windows / Git for Windows, real asdf or mise installs (simulated with a shim), the 2.40.2–2.43.4 backports (source check only, not built), Apple Git-154's actual source, and full test suites (light-CPU rule).\n"},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
