{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"28523f8b24c9430510c577d2a1cbfcefde81da6532d8a4476c875a2ecd056946","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Re-review verdict on #372: **safe, with one small required change.** The main promise now holds on every allowed git version:\n- the reviewer checked git's source at 37 releases;\n- built five versions itself;\n- ran 42 attempts to trigger a fetch, and none happened.\n\nThe one remaining gap: if the repo is reached through a symlink, the version check runs in the real folder but the commands run in the linked path. A version manager could then select different gits for the two. It's unlikely, but it's a real bypass. Sending the author back for that plus the cleanups:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WzJZqRpDhe4m7G4kSAf7jV","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"Re-review: SAFE WITH CHANGES — symlink probe fix","message":"The re-review of 36c0cc41 came back **SAFE WITH CHANGES**. The backport table passes against all 37 tags checked and against 2.39.4/2.44.1/2.45.1 built from source. The messages pass. The fetch spy and the hostile configs are re-confirmed (0 fetches, 0 PWN).\n\n## REQUIRED\n1. **Probe and commands must use the same directory string.**\n   - Today `lazyFetchGuardDir` calls `EvalSymlinks` (lazy_fetch_guard.go:119-123), so the probe runs at the PHYSICAL path (:108). Real commands run at the LOGICAL path with a logical `PWD` (provider.go:18119, :18938).\n   - The reviewer reproduced it: `--repo evil/link` with `link → real/cl` and `evil/.tool-versions` selecting the old Git. The probe sees 2.54 at `real/cl`; 16 commands run 2.44.0 at `evil/link`, and **1 lazy-fetch child was spawned**, stopped only by GIT_ALLOW_PROTOCOL.\n   - Fix: run `git version` in exactly the directory string (and `PWD`) the commands use, OR run every command in the canonical dir. **Canonicalize only the cache key, never the probe's cwd.**\n   - The reviewer's shim and runner are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-372-review/.g3/` (`shim2`, `shimrun.sh`, case r2/d).\n   - Add a symlink test with a cwd-sensitive fake git. Weaken it (reintroduce `EvalSymlinks` for the probe cwd) and show it goes red.\n2. **Stale \"2.45\" in tests:** search_cache_scope_context_review_test.go:110, search_cache_history_review_test.go:39, provider_git_config_preflight_windows_test.go:28, git_test.go:2394.\n3. **Wording nit:** write the backport list as \"2.39.4+, 2.40.2+, …\" so the versions don't read as exact ones.\n\n## RECOMMENDED. Do these if each stays small, or list them as follow-ups in the PR\n4. **Static launch test hardening.** It still misses: a zero-value `var c exec.Cmd` then `c.Start()`; a struct embedding `exec.Cmd`; a `reflect.New` of `exec.Cmd`; `syscall.Syscall(SYS_EXECVE…)`; cgo `C.system`; and a package under `bin/`, because the walker skips `bin`/`node_modules` at lazy_fetch_guard_test.go:440 even though Go compiles an imported `bin/` package.\n   - Suggested: enumerate files via `go list` (including CgoFiles; flag any `import \"C\"`); flag any `os/exec.Cmd` type reference outside the allowlist; flag `Syscall*` with exec/spawn numbers; stop skipping `bin/`.\n5. **Encoding pin:** pin `-c i18n.logOutputEncoding=UTF-8` on FileCochanges and FindCommitWithCheckpoint too. Today co-change degrades on UTF-16 repos; there's no egress, only degraded output.\n6. **CI coverage for the table:** CI only has Git 2.55/2.56, so the backport table is protected only by local runs with `ENTIRE_GRAPH_TEST_GITS`. Add a CI job that builds Git 2.45.0 plus one backport from source (cached) and runs the two oracle tests, if that's a modest workflow addition. Otherwise list it as a follow-up.\n\n## Same rules as before\nWeakening for every change, focused `-race` under mlock, push with no force, watch CI, update the PR body (add the symlink case to the repro table), and check findings on org trail **2510** with the fresh CLI. Report per the protocol."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017syjxyRom16pz2deTCa1Zw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G3-Ba']['note']+=' | Re-review: SAFE WITH CHANGES. The core no-egress claim holds (37 tags source-checked, 5 Gits built, 42 spy runs with 0 fetches). Required: probe/command dir mismatch through a symlink (probe canonicalized, commands logical); plus stale test comments and the wording nit. Recommended: static-test hardening, encoding pin on co-change, CI job with old Gits. Author resumed.'\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Record the 372 re-review verdict on the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
