{"parentUuid":"a28467fa-4eb7-4cff-852c-610be166f80e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgN8Qq6M66VSEvTJcdKmA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QvZBQXuSKoQnRYTxuz7Ssh","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"Add: URL-named non-origin promisor test + motivation","message":"Two small additions for #372 while you're in it:\n\n1. **Test the real-world shape.** On devenv/cli the promisor is on the CHECKPOINT remote, whose name is a full URL: `remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor=true` plus `partialclonefilter=blob:none`. It is NOT on `origin`. Your live check on devenv/cli already passed, so the code handles it. But add a fixture test with a promisor on a non-origin remote whose name is a URL (dots, slashes and a colon in the config key), so the detection and admission can't regress to \"only checks origin\". Weaken it (detect only `remote.origin.promisor`) and show it goes red.\n2. **Add the motivation to the PR body.** It's stronger than the current one. On this machine Brain could build graph indexes only for entire-graph. cli and entiredb both refused with the promisor message, which is why entire-graph is the only one of the five Brain repos with a `semantic` source. #372 is what gives Brain code context on partial-clone repos at all.","type":"message","recipient":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"Two small additions for #372 while you're in it:\n\n1…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_read_input_tokens":510671,"output_tokens":1790,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":326},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":1790,"cache_read_input_tokens":510671,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1189,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1189},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QvZBQXuSKoQnRYTxuz7Ssh":{"to":"aead2ee30e4f0404a","summary":"Add: URL-named non-origin promisor test + motivation","message":"Two small additions for #372 while you're in it:\n\n1. **Test the real-world shape.** On devenv/cli the promisor is on the CHECKPOINT remote, whose name is a full URL: `remote.https://github.com/entireio/cli-checkpoints.git.promisor=true` plus `partialclonefilter=blob:none`. It is NOT on `origin`. Your live check on devenv/cli already passed, so the code handles it. But add a fixture test with a promisor on a non-origin remote whose name is a URL (dots, slashes and a colon in the config key), so the detection and admission can't regress to \"only checks origin\". Weaken it (detect only `remote.origin.promisor`) and show it goes red.\n2. **Add the motivation to the PR body.** It's stronger than the current one. On this machine Brain could build graph indexes only for entire-graph. cli and entiredb both refused with the promisor message, which is why entire-graph is the only one of the five Brain repos with a `semantic` source. #372 is what gives Brain code context on partial-clone repos at all."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"a6d62333-8ada-4e53-ab06-9760c400e991","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgN8QpgYtE5znxD312Gew","requestRef":"837b2414-b8d7-4f3d-95b6-6834b3df7782","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"137b9126-00df-46cf-b162-f420b7941506","timestamp":"2026-10-25T01:59:43.358Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd"