probe at the exact logical --repo path with a cache keyed by the logical string (symlink case d: refused, 0 fetches); URL-named promisor test; alias/value/syscall/cgo/bin-proof static scan; encoding pins; NEW CI job builds Git 2.45.0 + 2.44.1 and confirms 2.45.0 fetches and 2.44.1 does not. CI 35 green; only Approvals pending; 0 findings. Final focused re-check of the symlink fix by the reviewer running.'\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('board ok')\nEOF","description":"Add the restore rule to protocol and update the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XNDKd6kqGEvzUhHhXKt3Kz","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a5c431d074520beed","summary":"Final focused check of #372 at ace66ffc","message":"Final, FOCUSED check of #372, now at **ace66ffc** (confirm with `gh pr view 372 --json headRefOid`). The author addressed your required change and all the recommended ones. Verify only these; keep it short and light CPU.\n\n1. **Symlink case d.** Re-run your exact attack (`.g3/shim2`, `.g3/shimrun.sh`, cases a/b/c/d) on the new head.\n   - The author says the probe now runs at the exact logical `--repo` string (`filepath.Abs` only, no EvalSymlinks), and the sem resolver carries `commandDir`.\n   - They deliberately keyed the cache by the logical string too, not canonical, to avoid a cache hit for `real/repo` being reused for `evil/link`. Judge whether that's sound.\n   - Expected: case d refused, 0 commands, 0 fetches.\n   - Also try a symlink in the MIDDLE of the path, and `--repo` given as a relative path with `..`.\n2. **Scan hardening.** Re-run your previously uncaught evasions: zero-value `exec.Cmd` + `Start`, embedded `exec.Cmd`, `syscall.Syscall(SYS_EXECVE…)`, cgo `C.system`, and a `bin/` package. Each should now be caught. The author lists reflect `Elem()`, `plugin.Open`, assembly, computed syscall numbers and third-party deps as known gaps (follow-ups). Agree or disagree that those are acceptable as follow-ups.\n3. **CI matrix.** Glance at the `lazy-fetch-git-matrix.yml` run on ace66ffc. Does it really build 2.45.0 and 2.44.1 and run the oracles, and does it fail if the builds weren't exercised? `gh run list --branch fix/index-partial-clones` / `gh run view --log`.\n\nReport in ≤ 20 lines with a verdict: SAFE TO MERGE / SAFE WITH CHANGES / UNSAFE."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
