{"parentUuid":"1ccd7a5e-f5c4-4d60-bc16-00bed6ddd26d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNBPA1gAtV7qzhmNhMoX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Awg1pNi7ZHcHk7igdgY7ej","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Compute merge order for 12 graph PRs","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only analysis: compute a safe merge order for 12 open entireio/entire-graph PRs. Do NOT merge, push, comment on, or edit anything. Output: caveman-ultra compressed tables. Use RTK for shell.\n\nPRs: #142, #370, #371, #372, #373, #374, #375, #376, #377, #378, #379, #380. #377 is STACKED on #371: its base branch is `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`. All the others target `main`.\n\n## Steps\n1. `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin main` and fetch each PR head to `refs/remotes/pr/<N>` (`pull/<N>/head`). That's a main checkout: fetch only, never checkout or commit there.\n2. For each PR, get head sha, base, files changed (`gh pr view <N> --json files,headRefOid,baseRefName,mergeable,mergeStateStatus`), and commits-behind-main.\n3. **Pairwise conflicts.** For every pair (A, B) of PRs targeting main, run `git merge-tree --write-tree --name-only <merge-base> pr/A pr/B` (git ≥ 2.38 form: `git merge-tree --write-tree pr/A pr/B`). Record whether they conflict and which files. Do the same for #377 against #371's head, and against each other PR.\n4. **Sequential simulation.** Find an order that minimises conflicts. Simulate it in a SCRATCH clone (`git clone --no-local /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/merge-sim` — never the main checkout):\n   - start from origin/main;\n   - merge each PR head in order with `git merge --no-ff --no-edit`;\n   - at each step record clean vs conflict and the conflicting files.\n   - Where a conflict appears, try the next candidate order.\n   - Note the rules: #371 must precede #377. #372, #373, #375 and #376 touch search_cache.go and provider.go, so check them carefully.\n5. Note any PR whose cache/schema version bump (for example #374 bumped provider-records v21→v22 and search-snapshot v26→v27) would collide with another PR's bump, so two PRs claim the same version number. Grep each PR's diff for version constants.\n\n## Report\n- A pairwise conflict matrix (only the conflicting pairs, with files).\n- The recommended merge order, with the simulated result per step.\n- Version-bump collisions, if any.\n- Any PR needing a rebase after an earlier merge, and how hard (trivial vs real conflict).\n- Remove the merge-sim clone when done."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1847,"cache_read_input_tokens":544911,"output_tokens":2248,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":364},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1847,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2248,"cache_read_input_tokens":544911,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1847,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1847},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Awg1pNi7ZHcHk7igdgY7ej":{"description":"Compute merge order for 12 graph PRs","model":"sonnet","run_in_background":"true","prompt":"Read-only analysis: compute a safe merge order for 12 open entireio/entire-graph PRs. Do NOT merge, push, comment on, or edit anything. Output: caveman-ultra compressed tables. Use RTK for shell.\n\nPRs: #142, #370, #371, #372, #373, #374, #375, #376, #377, #378, #379, #380. #377 is STACKED on #371: its base branch is `perf/alias-grep-corpus-paths`. All the others target `main`.\n\n## Steps\n1. `git