{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"190b5354d3a17f77f19a6183802a5d1febab34320f8256ab77214799d01d52cf","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"#380 now reports the new flag in its capabilities, as the Brain session asked. CI is green and there are no findings.\n\nThe same \"undo wipes uncommitted work\" slip happened here too. The agent started before I added that rule, and it caught and fixed it. Telling the Brain session the flag is live:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KJafh8cKJM3dSTYdExcF7c","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"#380 now advertises context_allow_ancestor","message":"#380 now advertises the feature: `entire graph capabilities --json` includes `optional_local_only_features.context_allow_ancestor: true`, a flat boolean where absence means unsupported. It landed in commit **edbdacb6** on `feat/context-allow-ancestor`, pinned by a CLI-level test that decodes the real JSON and weakened to red. CI is green (only Approvals pending) and org trail 2526 has 0 findings. `docs/store-contract.md` says to feature-detect via this key first.\n\nThe binary I gave you (`eg-ancestor-6206efed`) predates the key. If you want to test capability detection end to end, here's a fresh copy of the new head: `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/bin/eg-ancestor-edbdacb6`.\n\nFYI, #372 passed its final adversarial round at ace66ffc: SAFE TO MERGE. Symlink cases d/e/f/g are refused with 0 fetches, and a new CI job builds git 2.45.0 and 2.44.1 from source and confirms 2.45.0 fetches while 2.44.1 doesn't."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PTUB82qnQdq2wPYjBA8LB5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"set -e; W=/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-allow-ancestor; git -C $W log --oneline -1; cd $W && go build -o bin/new-edbdacb6 ./cmd/entire-graph 2>&1 | tail -2; D=/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/bin; cp bin/new-edbdacb6 $D/.anc2.tmp && mv $D/.anc2.tmp $D/eg-ancestor-edbdacb6; $D/eg-ancestor-edbdacb6 capabilities --json 2>/dev/null | python3 -c \"import json,sys; print('context_allow_ancestor =', json.load(sys.stdin).get('optional_local_only_features',{}).get('context_allow_ancestor'))\"; python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G-ancestor']['note']+=' | edbdacb6: capabilities advertise optional_local_only_features.context_allow_ancestor=true (CLI test, weakened red). CI green, 0 findings. Binary timing/bin/eg-ancestor-edbdacb6.'\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('board ok')\nEOF","description":"Build and stage the edbdacb6 binary and verify the capability"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
