o AI attribution, no force-push to anyone else's branch, and commit before any experiment (never restore with `git checkout -- file`). Use caveman-ultra compressed output and RTK.\n\n## Setup\n- `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph fetch -q origin main` plus each PR head (`pull/<N>/head:refs/remotes/pr/<N>`).\n- `git -C /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph worktree add -b integration/g3-all /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-integration origin/main`\n\n## Merge order\nUse `git merge --no-ff` of each PR head:\n370 → 371 → 377 → 373 → 379 → 376 → 375 → 372 → 380 → 374 → 142 → 378\n\n(#377 is stacked on #371, so its head contains #371.)\n\n## Known conflicts (from a simulation)\n- **CHANGELOG.md** (372/374/378/380): trivial, adjacent additions. Keep all entries, in a sensible order.\n- **#142 × #374 in provider.go `syntheticBoundarySymbols`** (1 hunk).\n  - #142 adds a `stop` func (cancellation polling) and drops `symbolBlockFromLines`.\n  - #374 replaced the body-token heuristic with the identifier-only `looksLikeToolHandler` (internal/sem/tool_handler.go), so the body slice is gone.\n  - The correct resolution keeps BOTH intents: #374's identifier-only decision, and #142's cancellation polls.\n  - Read both PRs' diffs and descriptions (`gh pr view 142`, `gh pr view 374`) before resolving.\n- **#375 × #378 in search_cache.go `loadCachedSearchSnapshot`.** This is SEMANTIC, not just textual.\n  - #378 makes `fileChangesWithRelations` return `(history, warning)`, adds a `withoutWarningCode` strip, and carries the warning over in `selectiveSearchSnapshotFromFull`.\n  - #375 replaced the full re-sort with `spliceFileChangesWithRelations(cached.Snapshot.Relations, history)`.\n  - The merged form must: take `history, warning`; strip and re-add the co-change warning exactly as #378 intends; and feed `history` into #375's splice, keeping #375's skip-when-unchanged path and identity guarantees.\n- **#142 × #378 in provider.go**: inspect and resolve.\n\n**For each real conflict:** run `entire graph impact` on the touched functions, resolve, then save the resolution as a patch file in `<worktree>/.g3/resolutions/` (e.g. `142-x-374.patch`, `375-x-378.patch`). When the user merges in order, #142 and #378 will need exactly these resolutions applied on rebase.\n\n## Verify the combination\n- `go build ./...` and `go vet ./...`.\n- Under mlock: the full `internal/sem` (`-p 1 -parallel 4 -timeout 40m`), `internal/gitutil`, `internal/cli` and `cmd/...` tests.\n- The key tests from each PR under `-race`: the splice tests (#375), the co-change warning tests (#378), the tool-handler tests (#374), the cancellation and truncation tests (#142), the partial-clone and lazy-fetch oracle tests (#372), the ancestor and capability tests (#380), and the retention tests (#379).\n- **Behaviour spot-check** on a clone in `timing/repos/` (cli or entire-brain), fresh cache dir:\n  - `index --head`, a warm `query`, `def`/`neighbors`/`impact` on one symbol;\n  - check outputs are sane;\n  - check the warm def/neighbors/impact time is in the ~0.45-0.5 s range (#375) and cold index is about 30% faster than main (#373). Compare against a main binary, 3 reps, interleaved.\n- **Cache-version question:** #374 bumps providerRecordsCacheVersion v21→v22 and searchSnapshotCacheVersion v26→v27. Decide whether #378's change to cached data (it now records the co-change failure REASON in the records-cache transaction and in derived selective views, where before it kept only an `unavailable` flag) needs a version bump. If old cached entries would silently lack the warning, they would keep the very silent drop #378 fixes. Look at how the records cache serializes it. Report yes/no with evidence. If yes, say whether #374's bump already covers it once both land (same release) or #378 needs its own.\n\n## Push as a DRAFT PR, for CI only\n- `git push -u origin integration/g3-all`.\n- `gh pr create --draft --base main --title \"DO NOT MERGE: integration CI for graph PRs #142, #370-#380\" --body <file in .g3/>`.\n  - The body says it is verification only, lists the merge order, the conflict resolutions (with the patch files), and the local verification results.\n  - Do not request reviewers.\n- Watch CI to a result. On a cascade, grep `DATA RACE` first. Fix only integration-resolution bugs on this branch. If a failure comes from one of the original PRs, report it; do not fix it here.\n\n## Report (≤ 40 lines)\n- the integration PR number;\n- per merge step: clean / resolved;\n- the resolution summaries plus the patch file paths;\n- local test results;\n- the behaviour and timing spot-check;\n- the cache-bump verdict;\n- CI enumerated green/failed/running.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa/tasks/aabe72c829f22357b.output","canReadOutputFile":true,"canContinueAgent":true},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"1d6b4a52-23ea-4dee-8666-695f6a42d5ab","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","root":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","branch":"main","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":1,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":251},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"entirehq/devenv","visibility":"private"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-brain","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/cli","visibility":"public"},{"host":"github.com","remote":"entireio/entire-graph","visibility":"public"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","platform":"macos"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"073cb57d-c962-4885-b377-d9e108d5d1cb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"ex