wo symbols, so #378's disclosure correctly stays silent; with one resolved match, new emits `W_VALUE_REFERENCES_UNMODELLED`.\n  \n  **Cache verdict: YES, #378 needs its own records-cache bump, v22 → v23. No search-cache bump.**\n  - The records key holds a `history-unavailable-scope` term and the co-change pairs, not the failure reason, and #378 leaves the key unchanged.\n  - Reproduced on #378's missing-blob fixture with \"dev\" builds and a shared cache:\n    - a v22 binary without #378 writes the entry;\n    - the #378 binary replays it with 0 warnings;\n    - a fresh cache gives 1 warning;\n    - a scratch v23 build on the shared cache gives 1 warning.\n  - The search cache heals itself: every full-profile hit re-reads history and a failed read is a miss (confirmed on the same fixture).\n  - #374's bump does not cover this. Any dev build made between the #374 and #378 merges writes v22 entries that lack the warning. Release and nightly builds are not exposed, because their version string is part of the key.\n  \n  **CI on #381:** 35 green, 0 failed. Entire Gates is still running (pending); `entire trail finding list 2530` returns \"has no open changes\".\n  - macOS test passed in 13 m, ubuntu in 4.7 m, Windows on all 8 shards.\n  - The CI test job runs plain `go test ./...` with no `-race` (test.yml:118). The race evidence is the local run above.\n  - CI found nothing in the original PRs to report.\n  \n  I did not record a brain memory for the cache finding or the #142 x #376 break, because the real Brain store is shared state I'd need the other session's OK to write. Suggest recording both.","handback":true,"handbackReportText":"## G3 integration of 12 graph PRs: all CI green except Entire Gates (still pending)\n\n**PR:** entireio/entire-graph **#381**, draft, no reviewers, title \"DO NOT MERGE: integration CI for graph PRs #142, #370-#380\". Branch `integration/g3-all`, head 463dbab0. Worktree: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-integration. Body file: /Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-integration/.g3/pr-body.md\n\n**Merge steps** (origin/main d4a0c186, then `--no-ff` each PR head):\n- Clean: 370, 371, 377, 373, 379, 376, 375, 372.\n- 380, 374: CHANGELOG only. Every entry kept, ordered Added / Changed / Fixed.\n- 142: conflict with #374 resolved, plus a semantic test fix for #376.\n- 378: conflicts with #375 and #142 resolved, plus CHANGELOG.\n- One extra commit after step 12: 463dbab0, the #142 x #376 test fix.\n\n**Resolutions.** Patches are in `/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/eg-integration/.g3/resolutions/`, and each is also embedded in the PR body. All except 142-x-376 are `git show --remerge-diff` output.\n- `142-x-374.patch`: #142's `stop` poll every `stopPollStride` and its `(nil,true)` return wrap #374's `looksLikeToolHandler(source)`. No body slice. Two comments that still said \"rescans content, superlinear\" are corrected. Two corrections to the brief:\n  - it is #374, not #142, that removes `symbolBlockFromLines` from this loop;\n  - there was also a semantic break: #142's test `TestTF142R12...UnbudgetedAreUnchanged` used a `Tool` fixture that only the old body-text heuristic accepted. I renamed it to `searchToolHandler`.\n  - Weakening checks: the old fixture goes red, and dropping the poll turns StopsMidScan red.\n- `142-x-376.patch`, no textual conflict: `TestTF142R5...` asserted that the warm selective view is persisted, which #376 removes on purpose. It passes on #142 alone and fails on the merge. It now requires the cache to stay at the complete entry. Weakening: putting the write back goes red (\"1 to 2 file(s)\").\n- `375-x-378.patch`:\n  - Takes `history, _ := fileChangesWithRelations(...)`. #378 returns `(relations, error)`, not `(history, warning)` as the brief said.\n  - Feeds `history` into #375's splice, so the unchanged-skip and full-resort fallback are kept.\n  - Strips `W_COCHANGE_HISTORY_UNAVAILABLE` unconditionally, because readable history with no pairs must still retire the warning.\n  - Keeps both helpers. #378's carry-over into the selective view merged cleanly.\n- `142-x-378.patch`: keeps #142's pre-call `!relationsShouldStop()` and in-loop poll, and takes #378's error and warning, recorded only when `ctx.Err()==nil`.\n- Graph impact:\n  - `syntheticBoundarySymbols`: one direct caller (`processProviderFile`), 7 in total.\n  - `looksLikeToolHandler`: only `syntheticBoundarySymbols` and its own test.\n\n**Local tests** (under mlock, with `env -u FORCE_COLOR`):\n- build and vet clean;\n- full `internal/sem` (`-p 1 -parallel 4`): ok, 215.6 s;\n- `internal/gitutil`, `internal/cli` (246 s), `cmd/entire-graph`, `cmd/graph-bench`: ok;\n- `-race` on 208 key tests from every PR (146 in sem, 38 in cli, 23 in gitutil, plus cmd `TestExitCode`): all ok, no DATA RACE.\n\n**Spot-check** on timing/repos/cli @3d1b73ff, base = main against this tip, fresh cache and plugin dir per run, 3 reps interleaved, medians. load1 rose from 3.9 to 9.0 during the block (above the protocol's ~8 ceiling by the end), but the spread stayed tight.\n\n| step | base | new | Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| cold `index --head` | 11.80 s | 7.82 s | −33.8% (#373 target ~30%) |\n| first warm `query` | 11.65 s | 3.51 s | −70% (preselect 7437 → 486 ms) |\n| warm `def` | 0.605 s | 0.440 s | in the 0.45–0.5 s target |\n| warm `neighbors` | 0.626 s | 0.448 s | in target |\n| warm `impact` | 0.627 s | 0.458 s | in target |\n\n- Output identity (g2-strip): reps are byte-identical within each binary. Base vs new differs only as #374 and #371 say:\n  - tool symbols 5 → 2, and their edges;\n  - `files_content_read_during_preselection` 0 → 1381.\n  - The callers lists are identical.\n- `OpenRepository` matches two symbols, so #378's disclosure correctly stays silent; with one resolved match, new emits `W_VALUE_REFERENCES_UNMODELLED`.\n\n**Cache verdict: YES, #378 needs its own records-cache bump, v22 → v23. No search-cache bump.**\n- The records key holds a `history-unavailable-scope` term and the co-change pairs, not the failure reason, and #378 leaves the key unchanged.\n- Reproduced on #378's missing-blob fixture with \"dev\" builds and a shared cache:\n  - a v22 binary without #378 writes the entry;\n  - the #378 binary replays it with 0 warnings;\n  - a fresh cache gives 1 warning;\n  - a scratch v23 build on the shared cache gives 1 warning.\n- The search cache heals itself: every full-profile hit re-reads history and a failed read is a miss (confirmed on the same fixture).\n- #374's bump does not cover this. Any dev build made between the #374 and #378 merges writes v22 entries that lack the warning. Release and nightly builds are not exposed, because their version string is part of the key.\n\n**CI on #381:** 35 green, 0 failed. Entire Gates is still running (pending); `entire trail finding list 2530` returns \"has no open changes\".\n- macOS test passed in 13 m, ubuntu in 4.7 m, Windows on all 8 shards.\n- The CI test job runs plain `go test ./...` with no `-race` (test.yml:118). The race evidence is the local run above.\n- CI found nothing in the original PRs to report.\n\nI did not record a brain memory for the cache finding or the #142 x #376 break, because the real Brain store is shared state I'd need the other session's OK to write. Suggest recording both."},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
