{"parentUuid":"ec8eee3a-b049-4924-8265-3f69ead48499","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNF5kDCjfXauNGN4JQu8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The combined test branch is done: draft PR [#381](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381), marked DO NOT MERGE. All 12 PRs together pass every CI check, plus the full local test suites and race-detector runs on 208 key tests.\n\nMeasured against `main` on the cli repo:\n\n| What | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cold index | 11.8 s | 7.8 s (−34%) |\n| First warm query | 11.7 s | 3.5 s (−70%) |\n| Warm `def`/`neighbors`/`impact` | about 0.62 s | about 0.45 s |\n\nResults are identical apart from the intended changes.\n\nIt found two things that pairwise checks couldn't:\n- **A hidden test clash.** A #142 test expects a file that #376 deliberately stopped writing, with no text conflict between them. The fix is saved as a patch for when #142 is rebased.\n- **#378 needs its own cache version bump.** Without it, a cache written by a build from before #378 would replay without the new warning, which is exactly the silent drop #378 fixes. The agent reproduced this. Release builds aren't affected, but dev builds are.\n\nSending #378's author back to add the bump, and recording both findings:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_read_input_tokens":565538,"output_tokens":2961,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":642},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3306,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2961,"cache_read_input_tokens":565538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3306},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"4b667434-2f9e-462d-b19b-463ad0b1676d","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgNF5iuKZXSw6431EnLFr","requestRef":"57c824db-8fe7-4918-9825-d86d71fe9d15","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"66f4f3ba-a40a-4402-97ec-b4cdf27480d9","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:27:15.818Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"66f4f3ba-a40a-4402-97ec-b4cdf27480d9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNF5kDCjfXauNGN4JQu8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PUpzybxxy6uMPgFvMEcnzK","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a3b6bf1cdaae82402","summary":"#378 needs records-cache bump v22→v23","message":"One required addition to #378, found by the integration branch (#381), which reproduced it.\n\n**#378 needs a records-cache version bump.** The records-cache key holds a `history-unavailable-scope` term and the co-change pairs, but NOT the failure reason, and #378 leaves the key unchanged. So an entry written by a binary without #378 replays under #378 with 0 warnings: the silent drop #378 exists to fix. Repro on your missing-blob fixture with a shared cache:\n- a v22 non-#378 build writes the entry;\n- #378 replays it with 0 warnings;\n- a fresh cache gives 1;\n- a scratch v23 build gives 1.\n\nThe search cache self-heals, since a failed history read is a miss, so it needs no bump.\n\n**Version number.** PR #374 bumps `providerRecordsCacheVersion` v21→v22 and lands BEFORE #378 in the merge order. So #378 must end at **v23**. On your branch (based on main = v21), set it to v23 directly, with a comment saying it follows #374's v22. The rebase conflict with #374 then resolves trivially to v23. Leave the search-snapshot version alone.\n\n**Test:** an entry written under the previous records-cache version is not replayed by the new binary, so the warning appears. Weaken it (revert the bump) and show it goes red.\n\nCommit before weakening, and restore from a byte copy, never `git checkout -- file`. Push to the same branch with no force, watch CI, check findings on the org trail, and update the PR body (cache bump plus why). Report in ≤ 15 lines.","type":"message","recipient":"a3b6bf1cdaae82402","recipient_kind":"agent","content":"One required addition to #378, found by the integ…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_read_input_tokens":565538,"output_tokens":2961,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":642},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3306,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2961,"cache_read_input_tokens":565538,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3306},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[{"type":"thinking_dropped","path":"messages.2.content.0","reason":"prefix_binding_mismatch"}],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PUpzybxxy6uMPgFvMEcnzK":{"to":"a3b6bf1cdaae82402","summary":"#378 needs records-cache bump v22→v23","message":"One required addition to #378, found by the integration branch (#381), which reproduced it.\n\n**#378 needs a records-cache version bump.** The records-cache key holds a `history-unavailable-scope` term and the co-change pairs, but NOT the failure reason, and #378 leaves the key unchanged. So an entry written by a binary without #378 replays under #378 with 0 warnings: the silent drop #378 exists to fix. Repro on your missing-blob fixture with a shared cache:\n- a v22 non-#378 build writes the entry;\n- #378 replays it with 0 warnings;\n- a fresh cache gives 1;\n- a scratch v23 build gives 1.\n\nThe search cache self-heals, since a failed history read is a miss, so it needs no bump.\n\n**Version number.** PR #374 bumps `providerRecordsCacheVersion` v21→v22 and lands BEFORE #378 in the merge order. So #378 must end at **v23**. On your branch (based on main = v21), set it to v23 directly, with a comment saying it follows #374's v22. The rebase conflict with #374 then resolves trivially to v23. Leave the search-snapshot version alone.\n\n**Test:** an entry written under the previous records-cache version is not replayed by the new binary, so the warning appears. Weaken it (revert the bump) and show it goes red.\n\nCommit before weakening, and restore from a byte copy, never `git checkout -- file`. Push to the same branch with no force, watch CI, check findings on the org trail, and update the PR body (cache bump plus why). Report in ≤ 15 lines."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"4b667434-2f9e-462d-b19b-463ad0b1676d","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNF5iuKZXSw6431EnLFr","requestRef":"57c824db-8fe7-4918-9825-d86d71fe9d15","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b883b663-37d2-4f05-92b9-51b111ea0ebc","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:27:21.222Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"parentUuid":"b883b663-37d2-4f05-92b9-51b111ea0ebc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNF5kDCjfXauNGN4JQu8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QF8isXsYTnCwvHYpXFj1m3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && entire brain remember \"In entire-graph, a change that alters what a records-cache entry carries (not just its key) needs its own providerRecordsCacheVersion bump; another PR's bump in the same release does not cover dev builds made between the two merges. Found when PR #378 started recording the co-change failure reason: a pre-#378 v22 entry replayed under #378 with zero warnings (the silent drop #378 fixes). The search-snapshot cache self-heals here because a failed history read is a miss. Dev builds share a cache key; release/nightly builds include the version string, so they are not exposed.\" --path constraints.cache.invariant --branch main --json 2>&1 | grep '\"id\"' | head -1; entire brain remember \"Pairwise merge-tree simulation of PRs misses semantic test breaks: entire-graph #142's test TestTF142R5 asserted the warm selective view is persisted, which #376 deliberately removes; there was no textual conflict, and it only failed in the combined build. Before a multi-PR merge handoff, build one integration branch with every PR in order and run the full suites plus CI on it (graph #381).\" --path workflow.release.gotcha --branch main --json 2>&1 | grep '\"id\"' | head -1","description":"Record the cache-bump and integration lessons in graph brain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3306,"cache_read_input_tokens":565538,"output_tokens":2961,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":642},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_i