{"parentUuid":"11c06970-7022-4556-8ee6-efc1deb0d246","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":[],"platform":"darwin","shell":"zsh","osVersion":"Darwin 25.5.0","scratchpadDirectory":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5/scratchpad"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/Users/suhaan/devenv"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4928d277-f326-4d43-b000-b0380447c915","timestamp":"2026-10-25T03:27:43.604Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph (was /Users/suhaan/devenv)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"7825c1a4bdc2cec56289122d7610a173928f76a955211dea6a813dda52d6753d","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The combined test branch is done: draft PR [#381](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/381), marked DO NOT MERGE. All 12 PRs together pass every CI check, plus the full local test suites and race-detector runs on 208 key tests.\n\nMeasured against `main` on the cli repo:\n\n| What | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Cold index | 11.8 s | 7.8 s (−34%) |\n| First warm query | 11.7 s | 3.5 s (−70%) |\n| Warm `def`/`neighbors`/`impact` | about 0.62 s | about 0.45 s |\n\nResults are identical apart from the intended changes.\n\nIt found two things that pairwise checks couldn't:\n- **A hidden test clash.** A #142 test expects a file that #376 deliberately stopped writing, with no text conflict between them. The fix is saved as a patch for when #142 is rebased.\n- **#378 needs its own cache version bump.** Without it, a cache written by a build from before #378 would replay without the new warning, which is exactly the silent drop #378 fixes. The agent reproduced this. Release builds aren't affected, but dev builds are.\n\nSending #378's author back to add the bump, and recording both findings:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PUpzybxxy6uMPgFvMEcnzK","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a3b6bf1cdaae82402","summary":"#378 needs records-cache bump v22→v23","message":"One required addition to #378, found by the integration branch (#381), which reproduced it.\n\n**#378 needs a records-cache version bump.** The records-cache key holds a `history-unavailable-scope` term and the co-change pairs, but NOT the failure reason, and #378 leaves the key unchanged. So an entry written by a binary without #378 replays under #378 with 0 warnings: the silent drop #378 exists to fix. Repro on your missing-blob fixture with a shared cache:\n- a v22 non-#378 build writes the entry;\n- #378 replays it with 0 warnings;\n- a fresh cache gives 1;\n- a scratch v23 build gives 1.\n\nThe search cache self-heals, since a failed history read is a miss, so it needs no bump.\n\n**Version number.** PR #374 bumps `providerRecordsCacheVersion` v21→v22 and lands BEFORE #378 in the merge order. So #378 must end at **v23**. On your branch (based on main = v21), set it to v23 directly, with a comment saying it follows #374's v22. The rebase conflict with #374 then resolves trivially to v23. Leave the search-snapshot version alone.\n\n**Test:** an entry written under the previous records-cache version is not replayed by the new binary, so the warning appears. Weaken it (revert the bump) and show it goes red.\n\nCommit before weakening, and restore from a byte copy, never `git checkout -- file`. Push to the same branch with no force, watch CI, check findings on the org trail, and update the PR body (cache bump plus why). Report in ≤ 15 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QF8isXsYTnCwvHYpXFj1m3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph && entire brain remember \"In entire-graph, a change that alters what a records-cache entry carries (not just its key) needs its own providerRecordsCacheVersion bump; another PR's bump in the same release does not cover dev builds made between the two merges. Found when PR #378 started recording the co-change failure reason: a pre-#378 v22 entry replayed under #378 with zero warnings (the silent drop #378 fixes). The search-snapshot cache self-heals here because a failed history read is a miss. Dev builds share a cache key; release/nightly builds include the version string, so they are not exposed.\" --path constraints.cache.invariant --branch main --json 2>&1 | grep '\"id\"' | head -1; entire brain remember \"Pairwise merge-tree simulation of PRs misses semantic test breaks: entire-graph #142's test TestTF142R5 asserted the warm selective view is persisted, which #376 deliberately removes; there was no textual conflict, and it only failed in the combined build. Before a multi-PR merge handoff, build one integration branch with every PR in order and run the full suites plus CI on it (graph #381).\" --path workflow.release.gotcha --branch main --json 2>&1 | grep '\"id\"' | head -1","description":"Record the cache-bump and integration lessons in graph brain"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AKuHJ2A6cq4fUps5MvMDqz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv-worktrees/timing/G3-PROTOCOL.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"- **CI runs tests with `-race`.**\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,\"- **entire-graph CI does NOT run `-race`** (test.yml:118 runs plain `go test ./...`; brain's CI does). **Your local `-race` run is the only race evidence**, so it is mandatory.\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['D4-handoff']['note']+=' | INTEGRATION #381 (draft, DO NOT MERGE): all 12 combined, CI 35 green, full sem/cli/gitutil suites ok, 208 key tests -race ok. cli: cold index −34%, first warm query 11.65 → 3.51 s, warm def/neighbors/impact 0.60 → 0.44-0.46 s. Resolutions saved in eg-integration/.g3/resolutions (142-x-374, 142-x-376 semantic test break, 375-x-378, 142-x-378). #378 needs a records-cache bump to v23 (being added).'\nT['G3-C1']['note']+=' | Adding a records-cache bump to v23 (found by integration #381).'\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Fix the race note in protocol and update the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
