C1: disclose unmodelled references\" is waiting on its own background work</summary>\n<note>This agent stopped with background work of its own still running. It may resume on its own when that work completes or reports, and the same task-id notifies again if it does; the result below may be interim.</note>\n<result>This agent's report was delivered to you as a message from \"a3b6bf1cdaae82402\" (its SubagentHandback call). Read it there; it is not repeated here.\n</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>395378</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>207</tool_uses><duration_ms>17487470</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","hash":"2f9be6d00c8213ad9accee002bdb9322cabf5c035f2cfc72a94dd830e2cb8e43","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The agent added the cache bump, with a test, and CI is green. It also flagged one review finding it disagrees with: the review asked for a second cache version bump, on the search cache. Its reasoning holds for ordinary queries. But it admits one gap: `graph context` and `graph store` read saved results without rebuilding, so they could serve an old result missing the new warning.\n\nThat gap is exactly the path Brain reads through. So I'm siding with the review: bumping the second version too is cheap (it only affects dev builds) and closes the gap instead of leaving it documented. Sending the agent back to do it:"},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AdNNB2s2rtCXE4oVENANcY","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"a3b6bf1cdaae82402","summary":"Accept the finding: bump search snapshot to v28","message":"Decision on the open medium finding (searchSnapshotCacheVersion): **accept it and bump**. Don't dismiss.\n\nYour reasoning is right for the query path. But the gap you named is exactly where the consumer reads: `graph store` and `graph context` serve the persisted entry without building, and Entire Brain's `brief` reads only through those. A pre-#378 entry there would carry no co-change warning until something else rewrote it. That's the silent drop again, on the one path the warning matters most. The bump only costs dev builds a one-time rebuild (release and nightly keys already include the version string), so it's the cheaper side of the trade.\n\n1. Bump `searchSnapshotCacheVersion` to **v28**, with a comment that it follows #374's v27, so the rebase conflict with #374 resolves to v28. Check whether the sqlite store sidecar path is derived from that version, as #374's notes say the store path moved with v27. If it is, stale stores are orphaned too, which is what we want, and #379's retention will clean them up.\n2. Test: a search entry and store written at the previous version are not served by `graph context` / `graph store` on this build. It must be a miss, or a rebuild that carries the warning. Weaken it (revert to v27/v26) and show it goes red.\n3. Commit before weakening and restore from a byte copy. Push with no force, watch CI.\n4. Resolve the finding on the org trail (fresh CLI, org number) with a message saying it was fixed by the v28 bump, and why. Update your PR comment to say the finding was right for the store/context path.\n5. Update the PR body. Report in ≤ 10 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0166qkocEydsgJGBhXSJuiPz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, datetime, fcntl, os\nlock=open('/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.lock','a'); fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX)\np='/Users/suhaan/devenv/.claude/todo-board.json'\nd=json.load(open(p)); T={t['id']:t for t in d['tasks']}\nT['G3-C1']['note']=T['G3-C1']['note'].replace(' | Adding a records-cache bump to v23 (found by integration #381).',' | dee7d29d: records-cache bump to v23 (+ test). A gate finding asked for a search-snapshot bump; ACCEPTED (graph store/context serve the persisted entry without building = brain\\'s path) → bumping to v28 now.')\nd['updated']=datetime.datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S')\ntmp=p+'.tmp'; json.dump(d,open(tmp,'w'),indent=2); os.replace(tmp,p); print('ok')\nEOF","description":"Record the 378 cache-bump decision on the board"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
