{"parentUuid":"16197238-9e26-468a-9336-f705d00c8810","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNKQJpinJgCmykzvhHiu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A5GytZUamiGx4ukyGNgPcC","name":"SendMessage","input":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Brain half received; 2 gaps before handoff","message":"Got your half: 13 PRs, the two ancestor stacks (#479→#481, #488→#489), and #484 after graph #380. Your caveat about the findings gate is the important part, and I won't quote 0 findings for brain. Two gaps I'd close in your lane before the handoff:\n\n1. **Agent reviews never ran on brain.** \"Reviews don't start automatically on this repository, so start the review manually\" means the Findings sub-gate is passing on the ABSENCE of a review. That's the silent-zero shape exactly; on graph the same CLI listed real findings on several trails, so the pipeline works where reviews run. Starting the agent review is part of the gate's own process, not an approval request, so it doesn't conflict with Suhaan's \"stop asking\". I'd start it on all 13, then sweep findings with the org trail numbers once they post. If it can't be started from the CLI, say so and it goes on Suhaan's list as \"brain PRs have had no agent review\".\n2. **A sequential merge check for the six export.go PRs** (#474, #479, #480, #481, #488, #489). Pairwise-clean wasn't enough on graph: #381 found a semantic test break with no textual conflict (#142's test asserting a file #376 deliberately stopped writing). Build a brain integration branch with all 13 in your intended order, plus a draft \"DO NOT MERGE\" PR for CI. Save each conflict resolution as a patch, so the real rebases at merge time are mechanical. My #381 recipe is in its PR body if useful.\n\nThe **owner: user** items are noted for the handoff: Approvals ×13, the transcript-mode / re-distill cost decision, the 37 GB store delete (held), and graph #372 (now SAFE TO MERGE after three adversarial rounds).\n\nD2 (fresh-env adoption check): I'll run it against the combined graph build from #381, using a plugin dir, and your current brain. Noted that devenv/cli SubagentStart hooks are newly wired, so there's no comparison with pre-hook runs; I'll baseline fresh.","type":"message","recipient":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","recipient_kind":"name","content":"Got your half: 13 PRs, the two ancestor stacks (#…"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2069,"cache_read_input_tokens":581749,"output_tokens":2569,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":958},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2069,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":2569,"cache_read_input_tokens":581749,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2069,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2069},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01A5GytZUamiGx4ukyGNgPcC":{"to":"fix-brain-initialization-ux","summary":"Brain half received; 2 gaps before handoff","message":"Got your half: 13 PRs, the two ancestor stacks (#479→#481, #488→#489), and #484 after graph #380. Your caveat about the findings gate is the important part, and I won't quote 0 findings for brain. Two gaps I'd close in your lane before the handoff:\n\n1. **Agent reviews never ran on brain.** \"Reviews don't start automatically on this repository, so start the review manually\" means the Findings sub-gate is passing on the ABSENCE of a review. That's the silent-zero shape exactly; on graph the same CLI listed real findings on several trails, so the pipeline works where reviews run. Starting the agent review is part of the gate's own process, not an approval request, so it doesn't conflict with Suhaan's \"stop asking\". I'd start it on all 13, then sweep findings with the org trail numbers once they post. If it can't be started from the CLI, say so and it goes on Suhaan's list as \"brain PRs have had no agent review\".\n2. **A sequential merge check for the six export.go PRs** (#474, #479, #480, #481, #488, #489). Pairwise-clean wasn't enough on graph: #381 found a semantic test break with no textual conflict (#142's test asserting a file #376 deliberately stopped writing). Build a brain integration branch with all 13 in your intended order, plus a draft \"DO NOT MERGE\" PR for CI. Save each conflict resolution as a patch, so the real rebases at merge time are mechanical. My #381 recipe is in its PR body if useful.\n\nThe **owner: user** items are noted for the handoff: Approvals ×13, the transcript-mode / re-distill cost decision, the 37 GB store delete (held), and graph #372 (now SAFE TO MERGE after three adversarial rounds).\n\nD2 (fresh-env adoption check): I'll run it against the combined graph build from #381, using a plugin dir, and your current brain. Noted that devenv/cli SubagentStart hooks are newly wired, so there's no comparison with pre-hook runs; I'll baseline fresh."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"785600fb-7b31-403f-8d9e-eba131bcb3a5","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgNKQJTQA3dkwCcSkcCma","requestRef":"b77d5f3c-161d-43cc-b853-59d67dfe66d5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c0ea857c-0f92-43a1-a9df-b1f2548d6f1f","timestamp":"2026-10-25T04:24:02.535Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"xhigh","perTurnEffort":"xhigh","session_id":"6e41b4d8-b432-41b0-bc86-517a25b228fa","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph","sessionId":"b0108f24-43a4-413e-94c9-bd361b6fafc5","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"main","slug":"lets-plan-cool-then-fluffy-walrus"}
